\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Supreme Court Maintains Widespread Access to  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pills; High court decision allows providers to continue sending common  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone to patients by mail\b0\par\par\uc2 By James Romoser, Lydia Wheeler and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,018 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 May 2026\par 22:38 GMT\par \uc2 wsj.com\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The Supreme Court on Thursday maintained widespread access to a common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, allowing doctors to continue mailing the drug to patients without first seeing them in person.\par \par \uc2 The decision, which came in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/25pdf/25a1207_21p3.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brief order}}}\uc2  on the high court's emergency docket, keeps on hold an earlier lower-court ruling that would have curtailed access to the drug, mifepristone, which is the most common method of ending a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Two conservative justices\u8212\'20\'14\uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14dissented from the court's decision to maintain access to the drug for now.\par \par \uc2 The high court acted on emergency appeals from two drugmakers that manufacture mifepristone, which is used in combination with another drug, misoprostol, to induce abortions. The companies rushed to the Supreme Court after the Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/appeals-court-curtails-access-to-mail-order-abortion-pills-15da02e3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on May 1 blocked mifepristone}}}\uc2  from being prescribed through virtual appointments and sent to patients by mail.\par \par \uc2 The appeals court found that Louisiana, which sued to challenge the Food and Drug Administration's regulations on mifepristone, was likely to succeed in its claim that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  under President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had relied on flawed data when it loosened restrictions on the drug.\par \par \uc2 Alito {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/justice-alito-temporarily-restores-access-to-abortion-pills-by-mail-e7f78daa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had ordered a temporary pause}}}\uc2  on the lower-court ruling to give the justices time to consider the drugmakers' request. On Thursday, a majority of the Supreme Court kept the ruling on hold indefinitely while litigation proceeds in the lower courts.\par \par \uc2 Alito wrote an emphatic six-page dissent, saying easy access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill through the mail is undercutting the landmark Supreme Court decision that overturned Roe v. Wade and allowed states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He referenced shield laws in some blue states that protect providers who send mifepristone through the mail to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than a dozen states}}}\uc2  that have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "What is at stake is the perpetration of a scheme to undermine our decision in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization," Alito wrote, referring to the 2022 decision, which he wrote.\par \par \uc2 "This scheme would not have been possible under \uc2 FDA\uc2  regulations had the federal government not taken steps in 2021 and 2023 to facilitate mail-order abortions," Alito added.\par \par \uc2 Thomas added a short dissent of his own, arguing that an obscure 1873 federal statute, known as the Comstock Act, makes it a crime to send mifepristone by mail for use in abortions.\par \par \uc2 The drugmakers "are not entitled to a stay of an adverse court order based on lost profits from their criminal enterprise," he said.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups have repeatedly called on the federal government to use the Comstock Act to punish \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, but the government hasn't done so. Supporters of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights say the statute only applies when the sender intends for the drug to be used in an illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and note there are legal abortions in every state.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court, as is common in emergency orders, didn't explain its reasoning in keeping the lower court's ruling on hold. Of the five conservative justices who voted to overturn Roe in 2022, three justices\u8212\'20\'14\uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14didn't register any dissent from Thursday's decision.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration further loosened restrictions in 2021 by doing away with the in-person dispensing requirement in light of the risks related to Covid-19. The change, which the \uc2 FDA\uc2  made permanent in 2023, allowed the pill to be prescribed through telehealth and sent to patients by mail.\par \par \uc2 Studies have shown that mifepristone is safe, including when prescribed remotely and taken at home. Antiabortion groups say those studies are flawed because the federal government doesn't track serious, nonfatal side effects.\par \par \uc2 In a social-media post, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  said it would press forward to complete a promised safety review of mifepristone and "in an effort to provide greater transparency, will provide updates as key milestones are reached." The antiabortion movement has grown frustrated with the Trump administration for not undoing the Biden-era decisions that expanded access to the drug.\par \par \uc2 Since the end of Roe, the number of abortions performed each year has actually increased. Of the roughly 1.1 million abortions that took place in 2025, 300,000 were provided via telehealth, a 25% increase from the year before, according to data from the Society of Family Planning, a group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Danco Laboratories\uc2 , one of mifepristone's manufacturers, said the decision means "a safe and effective drug Americans depend on will continue to be available while the litigation proceeds."\par \par \uc2 This is the second time the Supreme Court has considered whether to restrict access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill. In 2024, the court unanimously rejected an effort brought by doctors and antiabortion groups, saying they lacked standing because they didn't prescribe the drug and weren't affected by the FDA's regulations that expanded access to the drug.\par \par \uc2 That left the door open for states, including Louisiana, to bring challenges instead. The Fifth Circuit found that Louisiana had suffered the required injury to challenge FDA's regulations because it paid $92,000 in Medicaid costs for two women who needed emergency care after the drug was mailed to them from out-of-state and they suffered complications.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana and other red states have argued that the easy availability of mifepristone through the mail is undermining statewide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. The antiabortion movement, meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/trump-anti-abortion-movement-76393c1c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has grown increasingly frustrated}}}\uc2  with the Trump administration for not undoing the FDA regulations. The FDA has said it is reviewing the guidelines around mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana Attorney General Liz Murrill on Thursday evening said, "It's shocking that the Supreme Court would block this common-sense return to medically ethical practices and oversight" and vowed the state will keep fighting the FDA's regulations.\par \par \uc2 Write to James Romoser at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:james.romoser@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 james.romoser@wsj.com}}}\uc2 , Lydia Wheeler at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:lydia.wheeler@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lydia.wheeler@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020260514em5e008kd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
