\par \par \uc2 Dr. Marty Makary at the White House last year. PHOTO: Anna Moneymaker/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Food and Drug Administration Commissioner Marty Makary resigned Tuesday after months of policy fights with top officials in the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  and the White House.\par \par \uc2 His departure became official after President Trump signed off last week on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/trump-planning-to-fire-fda-commissioner-marty-makary-34c072e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a plan to fire Makary}}}\uc2 , The Wall Street Journal previously reported. Makary offered his resignation, effective Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "Everybody wants that job," Trump said. "Marty is a terrific guy and he's going to go on and lead a good life. He was having some difficulty." He added on his Truth Social platform that Kyle Diamantas, the deputy commissioner for food, would take over leading the agency in an acting capacity.\par \par \uc2 The president also posted a text message from Makary that included his resignation and a list of what he considered his accomplishments, such as reducing drug-review times. "It's been the honor of a lifetime to serve as your \uc2 FDA\uc2  Commissioner. I am forever grateful," Makary said.\par \par \uc2 Makary, an author and former Johns Hopkins surgeon who became a highly visible champion for the Make America Healthy Again movement, was seen for months by other administration officials as struggling to manage his agency. He skirmished with health-department officials and the White House, where some came to regard him as a rogue agent, the Journal has reported.\par \par \uc2 His departure caps a tumultuous period that included clashes over vaping, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and drug policy. His agency, a part of \uc2 HHS\uc2  under Secretary \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2 , was also dogged by the impact of layoffs led by the \uc2 Department of Government Efficiency\uc2  and rapid turnover in the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's leadership ranks.\par \par \uc2 "Marty, you took on entrenched interests, challenged the status quo, and never lost sight of the American people we serve," Kennedy said in a social-media post. "You pushed forward critical reforms and helped advance our mission to Make America Healthy Again."\par \par \uc2 Makary becomes the latest top lieutenant fired under Kennedy since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/cdc-director-susan-monarez-removed-from-post-2f60725c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the ouster last summer}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  Director Susan Monarez and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/white-house-pushes-shake-up-at-hhs-ahead-of-midterms-6ad882a5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the February removal}}}\uc2  of deputy secretary Jim O'Neill.\par \par \uc2 Top administration officials became convinced Makary had to go because, in addition to months of turmoil, complaints from some in the pharmaceutical industry continued to mount, people familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy agreed with Trump's decision, according to people familiar with his thinking. The secretary last year had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/rfk-jr-fda-head-management-7dce398f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considered installing someone else}}}\uc2  to run the \uc2 FDA\uc2  while Makary remained a figurehead.\par \par \uc2 Makary was in office for about 13 months. He took up many policies championed by Kennedy's MAHA supporters, such as approving new natural-food dyes and leading a review of infant-formula safety.\par \par \uc2 After news of Makary's departure Tuesday, some of his supporters took to X to praise him.\par \par \uc2 "Washington doesn't know what to do with people who can't be bought. Dr. Marty Makary was one of the few people inside Washington willing to challenge the corporate capture of our health agencies," Vani Hari, a MAHA influencer known as the Food Babe, posted on X. "He questioned the status quo, stood up to powerful interests, and gave millions of Americans hope that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  could finally put public health over pharmaceutical and chemical industry profits."\par \par \uc2 Trump recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/trump-pressures-fda-commissioner-to-approve-flavored-vapes-9dad81ee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 became frustrated with Makary}}}\uc2  for not moving fast enough to approve flavored vapes and other nicotine products. Makary in February {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/white-house-pushes-for-flavored-vapes-blocked-by-fda-head-2f8f0138"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to authorize}}}\uc2  blueberry and mango vape flavors from Los Angeles manufacturer Glas, worried that fruit flavors would encourage youth vaping. After the pressure from Trump, Makary reversed course and authorized the flavors. His agency Friday also unveiled a new policy that would allow some nicotine vapes and pouches that haven't yet been authorized by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to enter the market\u8212\'20\'14a boon to the tobacco industry.\par \par \uc2 Rare-disease patients and their advocates criticized Makary for not being flexible enough when it comes to evidence to prove treatments for their ailments work. Rare-disease drugs can be hard to test because the pool of potential study subjects is so small.\par \par \uc2 Drug-industry representatives pushed in recent weeks for a steady hand to lead the \uc2 FDA\uc2 . After Makary's departure, \uc2 John Crowley\uc2 , president and chief executive of the \uc2 Biotechnology Innovation Organization\uc2  trade association, said: "What we need now is strong, stable and science-driven leadership at the \uc2 FDA\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 "We are losing the biotech race with China," Crowley added. "\uc2 FDA\uc2  must be strengthened immediately."\par \par \uc2 Leaders of antiabortion groups including Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America called for Makary to be fired after he didn't produce a promised safety study of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill. The Journal has reported that Makary said he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/trump-anti-abortion-movement-76393c1c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could have stalled approval}}}\uc2  of a generic form of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, but didn't.\par \par \uc2 "Dr. Makary was part of a broader symptom of an administration that has not paid attention to pro-life issues," said Sen. Bill Cassidy (R., La.), who chairs the committee that will need to approve Makary's successor. "I care deeply about life, and I anticipate the next FDA nominee shall as well."\par \par \uc2 Within hours of the announcement, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups were attacking Diamantas for work his law firm did representing Planned Parenthood regarding a dispute with one of its clinics that was slated to open in Florida's Kissimmee Health Center medical complex.\par \par \uc2 "We cannot allow someone who represented Planned Parenthood to oversee rules surrounding the deadly \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone," Lila Rose, an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activist, posted on X.\par \par \uc2 "Kyle Diamantas was a junior legal associate who was assigned to that case by his superiors. He expressed his objections to representing Planned Parenthood, based on his personal convictions, and ultimately removed himself from the case," said White House spokesman Kush Desai.\par \par \uc2 Write to Liz Essley Whyte at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:liz.whyte@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liz.whyte@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Natalie Andrews at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:natalie.andrews@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 natalie.andrews@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020260512em5c005sd\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
