\par \par \uc2 Packages of Mifepristone tablets. PHOTO: Natalie Behring for WSJ\par \par \uc2 A U.S. appeals court has blocked doctors from mailing a popular \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug to pregnant women, in a temporary ruling that nonetheless deals a blow to access to the most common {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/abortion-pill-increase-roe-wade-68472ff8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 method for ending a pregnancy}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals on Friday put on hold for now a 2023 Food and Drug Administration regulation allowing doctors to send mifepristone pills through the mail without seeing a patient in person. A unanimous panel of Republican appointees said Louisiana, which brought the suit, was likely to succeed in its claim that the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's rationale for allowing the pills to be dispensed via mail was based on flawed data.\par \par \uc2 The panel also found that Louisiana was likely to suffer irreparable harm if the regulation were to remain in place while litigation proceeds.\par \par \uc2 "Every \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  facilitated by \uc2 FDA\uc2 's action cancels Louisiana's ban on medical abortions and undermines its policy that 'every unborn child is human being from the moment of conception and is, therefore, a legal person,'" the panel wrote.\par \par \uc2 A federal trial judge in April had also found that Louisiana was likely to succeed in its challenge to the regulation. But the judge declined to immediately block it, ruling the public interest favored allowing the practice of mailing pills to continue while the \uc2 FDA\uc2  reviewed the drug's safety.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved mifepristone, in combination with misoprostol, for medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2000. It is approved for use for up to 10 weeks of pregnancy and has been used millions of times.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana's Republican attorney general, Liz Murrill, applauded the appeals panel ruling, saying the "nightmare is over."\par \par \uc2 GenBioPro, which manufactures a generic version of the pill, said the appeals court ruling will create "unnecessary barriers" for women to access mifepristone across the U.S., including those in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana is one of several GOP-led states challenging \uc2 FDA\uc2  regulations on mifepristone. The Trump administration asked the judge to block the case, stating Louisiana lacked standing and citing the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's ongoing mifepristone review.\par \par \uc2 The number of abortions performed each year has increased even after more than a dozen states banned the procedure since the Supreme Court in 2022 eliminated a federal right to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 A growing proportion of abortions in the U.S. are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/abortion-telemedicine-medication-data-89cf7423"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provided using telemedicine}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14including for women in states that have banned nearly all abortions. The \uc2 FDA{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/fda-allows-women-to-get-abortion-pill-by-mail-11639698022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed mifepristone to be dispensed}}}\uc2  by mail during the Biden administration. In the years since, doctors in a handful of states with so-called shield laws have been able to prescribe and mail the medication to women in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 A number of studies have demonstrated the safety and efficacy of mifepristone, physician groups say. But antiabortion groups say those studies are flawed because the federal government doesn't track serious, nonfatal side effects.\par \par \uc2 In 2024, a unanimous Supreme Court dismissed on procedural grounds a case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone-f78f3320"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeking to roll back FDA approval of mifepristone}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After Trump returned to office last year, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  promised to review the safety of the drug. But antiabortion groups have criticized the Trump administration for slow-walking the review. In the fall, the \uc2 FDA{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/fda-abortion-pill-generic-trump-rfk-jr-47a9fa72"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved a new generic form}}}\uc2  of mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 Write to Victoria Albert at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:victoria.albert@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 victoria.albert@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020260501em51008c1\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
