\par \par \uc2 'It's effectively over,' Sen. Bernie Moreno says of the attempt to renew expired healthcare subsidies. PHOTO: Kevin Dietsch/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Top Senate negotiators said an effort to renew expired healthcare subsidies had effectively collapsed, likely ending the hopes of 20 million Americans that the tax-credit expansion could be revived and lower their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/aca-health-insurance-cost-subsidies-expire-37a595a9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 monthly insurance premiums}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Talks had centered on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/aca-subsidies-deal-republican-senate-d3e73e2c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a proposal}}}\uc2  from Sens. Bernie Moreno (R., Ohio) and \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  (R., Maine) to extend a version of the enlarged Affordable Care Act subsidies for at least two years, while cutting off higher-income people from participating and eventually giving enrollees the option of putting money into health savings accounts. It also would eliminate zero-dollar premium plans. But lawmakers from both parties now say the chances of a deal have all but evaporated.\par \par \uc2 "It's effectively over," Moreno said Wednesday. Sen. \uc2 Bill Cassidy\uc2  (R., La.)\u8212\'20\'14the architect of an adjacent plan\u8212\'20\'14agreed. While Collins declined to be as definitive, she did say that it was "certainly difficult."\par \par \uc2 The collapse in negotiations comes as new, higher health-insurance bills are kicking in for many households and just months after a standoff over extending the subsidies sparked the longest government shutdown in U.S. history. Now, both parties are set to head into the midterm elections with no breakthrough on healthcare coverage. Instead, the focus in Washington has largely turned to new restrictions of immigration enforcement officers.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ACA\uc2  subsidies were first expanded in 2021 by Democrats during the coronavirus pandemic with no Republican support. They allowed people with incomes over 400% of the poverty line\u8212\'20\'14currently $128,600 for a family of four\u8212\'20\'14to receive tax credits reducing the cost of premiums. The subsidies dramatically expanded the number of people who could obtain health insurance without paying a premium. The expanded subsidies expired at the end of last year.\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats who had been working to find a middle ground agreed that talks had collapsed over how to handle \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  coverage.\par \par \uc2 "Hyde language was an obstacle," said Sen. Tim Kaine (D., Va.), using the shorthand that refers to the existing ban on using federal funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is named after the original sponsor, former Rep. Henry Hyde (R., Ill.). "My Republican colleagues are dug in on that," added Sen. Mark Kelly (D., Ariz.).\par \par \uc2 Cassidy, chairman of the Senate Health, Education, Labor and Pensions Committee, said the primary impediment to a deal was how to treat \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  coverage. "The other issues maybe we could have gotten," he said.\par \par \uc2 ACA\uc2  marketplace plans can offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  coverage, but existing law bars the use of federal funds toward \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , except in cases of rape or incest or to save a mother's life. Subsidies can be used to pay for a plan that covers \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but enrollees have to pay a small out-of-pocket sum for the specific cost of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  coverage to ensure federal money isn't used for that. Antiabortion activists argue that the subsidies indirectly fund \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\par \par \uc2 "Republicans will never support anything that allows federal tax dollars to be used for subsidizing abortions, period," said Moreno.\par \par \uc2 Democrats, who had met behind closed doors on Tuesday night, decided to approach Moreno on Wednesday about removing the ban on using federal dollars to fund abortions put into the provision creating health savings accounts, according to Kaine.\par \par \uc2 For his part, Moreno blamed Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D., N.Y.), saying that he was giving priority to a potent election-year issue over a policy outcome. "He wants a political issue," Moreno said.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Schumer said Democrats have been trying to negotiate a deal to extend \uc2 ACA\uc2  tax credits since the summer. Moreno "is trying to distract from the reality: the credits expired and Americans are paying thousands more because Republicans can't get their act together," Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 Schumer, for his part, has continued to push for restoration of \uc2 ACA\uc2  tax credits for the next three years in line with legislation that has already passed the House.\par \par \uc2 "This is my final offer," Moreno told reporters last week as he sent off his proposal to Democrat leadership. "There's no way I can get 35 Republicans to vote for anything more." But Moreno said he didn't hear back from Democratic leadership.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have a 53-47 majority in the Senate, where most legislation requires 60 votes to advance.\par \par \uc2 Write to Siobhan Hughes at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Siobhan.hughes@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Siobhan.hughes@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Anvee Bhutani at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:anvee.bhutani@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anvee.bhutani@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Anvee Bhutani at \par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020260204em24008hl\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
