\par\par \uc2 Health News\par \uc2 Health\par \b \uc2 FDA\uc2  Approves New Generic Version of the  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pill Mifepristone; The decision, which has drawn backlash from antiabortion groups and lawmakers, comes as the agency launches a review of the drug's safety\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 693 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2025\par 00:20 GMT\par \uc2 wsj.com\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Food and Drug Administration\uc2  approved a new generic version of a pill used to terminate pregnancies, a decision that comes as the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  reviews the drug's safety.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  authorized a generic form of mifepristone, a 200-milligram oral tablet, on Tuesday from Evita Solutions, according to a letter posted on the agency's website. Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the most common form of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the U.S. and has faced heightened scrutiny from antiabortion groups and lawmakers who have sought to limit its use.\par \par \uc2 Health and Human Services Secretary \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2  said during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/rfk-jr-hearing-takeaways-d738be09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an appearance before a Senate committee}}}\uc2  last month that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  was examining the science behind mifepristone and collecting "new data."\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone, in combination with misoprostol, was approved for medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in 2000. The drug can be used through about 10 weeks of pregnancy and has been used millions of times. Studies have shown the two-drug regimen of mifepristone and misoprostol is safe and effective. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  also approved a generic version of mifepristone in 2019.\par \par \uc2 The latest approval drew backlash from antiabortion lawmakers and groups that have questioned the drug's safety and pushed for further restrictions on how it can be prescribed and dispensed.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 FDA\uc2  had promised to do a top-to-bottom safety review of the chemical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug, but instead they've just greenlighted new versions of it for distribution," Sen. \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  (R., Mo.) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/HawleyMO/status/1973801164052574259"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a post on X}}}\uc2 . "I have lost confidence in the leadership at \uc2 FDA\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 "This reckless decision by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to expand the availability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs is unconscionable," Marjorie Dannenfelser, the president of the Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America group, said in a written statement. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
