\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone can be used through about 10 weeks of pregnancy. PHOTO: Natalie Behring for WSJ\par \par \uc2 Kennedy said in a post on X Thursday the \uc2 FDA\uc2  "only approved a second generic mifepristone tablet because federal law requires approval when an application proves the generic is identical to the brand-name drug."\par \par \uc2 Evita Solutions said in a statement that the medication is expected to be available in January. "Availability of our product will expand patients' options for medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with an affordable product backed by decades of safe use," the company said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups have repeatedly emphasized the safety of medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and have criticized efforts to restrict its access. Earlier this week, a group of 20 Democratic attorneys general said in a statement that the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's decision to review the drug "ignores decades of research that proves mifepristone is safe and effective."\par \par \uc2 "If access to mifepristone is challenged, we will take action to protect it," they said.\par \par \uc2 In recent years, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  has allowed women to access the medication through telehealth providers and receive it by mail. A growing proportion of abortions in the U.S. are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/abortion-telemedicine-medication-data-89cf7423"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provided using telemedicine}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14including for women in states that have banned nearly all abortions since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 Doctors in a handful of states with so-called shield laws have prescribed the medication to women in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. The shield laws are designed to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers from legal jeopardy, including extradition. This practice has faced legal and regulatory challenges that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activists say can further hinder access.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone-f78f3320"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected an attempt}}}\uc2  to restrict access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill last year on procedural grounds.\par \par \uc2 Attorneys general in states including Idaho, Kansas and Missouri have since revived the case, and challenged access to mifepristone in federal court. The Trump administration asked the judge to dismiss that case in May, echoing arguments made by the Justice Department under former President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . The Trump administration said the Republican-led states didn't have legal standing to sue and didn't address specific \uc2 FDA\uc2  regulations in its court filing.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020251002ela2005sd\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
