\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Abortions Accessed Through Telemedicine Are Growing Despite Legal Challenges; Three years after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade, abortions in the U.S. are on the rise due to provider shield laws\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 835 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 June 2025\par 10:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The number of abortions in the U.S. accessed through telemedicine is growing. So are the challenges to this mechanism that has allowed patients in states with near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans to acquire the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill.\par \par \uc2 Abortions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/roe-v-wade-is-gone-but-abortions-are-on-the-rise-383ffaf4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are on the rise in the U.S}}}\uc2 . despite more than a dozen states enforcing near-total bans on the procedure, according to a report released Monday by #WeCount, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -data project sponsored by the Society of Family Planning, which supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. There were more than 1.14 million abortions in the U.S. in 2024 compared with around 1.06 million in 2023, the report said.\par \par \uc2 One in four abortions in the U.S. were provided using telehealth at the end of 2024, compared with just 7% at the end of 2022, the report said. Half of those medication abortions were prescribed through telemedicine to patients living under bans by doctors operating in states with so-called shield laws. Eight states, including New York and Massachusetts, have shield laws designed to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers from legal jeopardy, including extradition.\par \par \uc2 "Telehealth has become a lifeline for so many people across the country," said Ushma Upadhyay, a public-health scientist and co-chair of #WeCount.\par \par \uc2 Legal disputes\par \par \uc2 The acceleration of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  via telemedicine has been fueled by a combination of these shield laws, Food and Drug Administration regulations and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a patchwork of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2  that has emerged since the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade}}}\uc2  three years ago. But this growing practice is facing a series of legal and regulatory challenges that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activists said could further erode access and antiabortion groups say are necessary for patient safety.\par \par \uc2 Texas Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/texas-sues-new-york-doctor-challenging-abortion-provider-shield-laws-521b35c6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued a New York-based doctor}}}\uc2  in December for allegedly violating his state's law by prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to a 20-year-old pregnant patient. A Louisiana grand jury indicted the same doctor in January for allegedly prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to a pregnant teenager in the state. Louisiana Attorney General Liz Murrill said in May the state is investigating a possible second case involving the same doctor.\par \par \uc2 New York Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  said the state wouldn't comply with Louisiana's request to extradite the doctor, citing her state's shield law, and signed legislation that allows doctors to leave their names off prescription labels for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. New York's Ulster County Clerk declined to file a summary judgment against the doctor for a $100,000 penalty from Texas.\par \par \uc2 It isn't immediately clear how Texas and Louisiana will proceed. A representative for Murrill declined to comment and a representative for Paxton didn't respond to a request for comment. Legal experts have said these cases might land in federal court.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Margaret Daley Carpenter, the doctor at the center of these cases, is a co-founder of the organization \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Coalition for Telemedicine, one of several providers that prescribe out-of-state patients medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through telehealth. Carpenter couldn't be reached for comment.\par \par \uc2 "The growing success of telemedicine has put it more on the enemies list of the antiabortion movement," said Julie F. Kay, executive director and co-founder of ACT.\par \par \uc2 Regulatory review\par \par \uc2 In the last quarter of 2024, shield-law practices provided an average of 12,330 abortions a month, according to the #WeCount report. They provided an average of 8,747 abortions a month in the first quarter of 2024.\par \par \uc2 Possible changes to regulations around the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill could also affect how it is prescribed. The Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone-f78f3320"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed a case}}}\uc2  in 2024 that targeted this regulation to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill on procedural grounds. But a federal judge in Texas is considering a revived case that seeks to block clinicians from prescribing medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through telemedicine and sending it by mail.\par \par \uc2 Health and Human Services Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/rfk-jr-hhs-hearings-takeaways-1a8564c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a recent congressional hearing}}}\uc2  he asked \uc2 FDA\uc2  Commissioner Marty Makary to review mifepristone's label.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved mifepristone, in combination with misoprostol, for medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2000. The drug is approved for use for up to 10 weeks of pregnancy. Multiple {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/abortion-pill-access-case-texas-judge-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 studies have shown}}}\uc2  the two-drug regime of mifepristone and misoprostol is safe and effective. Antiabortion groups and some conservative lawmakers have questioned the drug's safety.\par \par \uc2 Leaders at shield-law providers said they were aware of the legal risks even under the protection of their own state laws. They don't travel to or through certain states due to the possibility of extradition.\par \par \uc2 "Our mantra is no anticipatory obedience," said Angel Foster, a co-founder of Massachusetts Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Project, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-pill-parties-shipping-148e3c15"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sends \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills to ban states}}}\uc2 . "We aren't going to change anything unless we have to in order to be legally compliant."\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020250623el6n00nzx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
