\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  Is Latest Target in Trump's Washington; Legal, political and financial threats pressure  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 -rights juggernaut\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas, Mariah Timms and Jess Bravin \par \uc2 878 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2025\par 18:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  is closing clinics and facing more financial strains as Republican control of Washington opens new avenues for weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider.\par \par \uc2 The organization went before the Supreme Court on Wednesday for a case that will help determine whether states can kick healthcare providers that offer abortions out of their Medicaid programs, a move that would further imperil the organization's presence in conservative states.\par \par \uc2 Republicans who control Congress and the White House are using cuts to federal spending to target progressive groups. Antiabortion leaders are making a push to get GOP lawmakers in the coming weeks to strip some $700 million in Medicaid and other federal funding that \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  receives for nonabortion healthcare services. Already the Trump administration has frozen about $20 million {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/trump-administration-plans-to-freeze-family-planning-grants-541441be"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in family-planning grants}}}\uc2  to \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  clinics in about a dozen states.\par \par \uc2 "This is an opportunity we cannot afford to miss," Rep. Chris Smith (R., N.J.), said at a Capitol Hill event last week calling to defund \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Any loss of funding would exacerbate the organization's financial challenges. A burst in fundraising after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the overturning of Roe v. Wade}}}\uc2  nearly three years ago has dissipated, and \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  is operating at a loss and treating fewer patients, according to the most recent publicly available financial reports.\par \par \uc2 "This isn't the first time we have faced attacks, and we know it won't be the last. We will always fight to protect patients and ensure they can get the essential care they need," Planned Parenthood President and Chief Executive \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  is a sprawling organization with a national office that serves as a fundraising, lobbying and communications juggernaut. A network of about 50 local affiliates operate some 600 clinics that provide services including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , contraception, breast-cancer screenings and other healthcare. Overall, its clinics provide about a third of abortions in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Nationally, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  operated at a loss in 2023\u8212\'20\'14the most recently available data\u8212\'20\'14running nearly $68 million behind its expenses as contributions dropped 15% from a decade high of more than $428 million in 2022. The national office has laid off dozens of staff members over the past couple of years, in part to send $70 million in additional funding to its local affiliates, many of which have also struggled financially.\par \par \uc2 Local Planned Parenthood clinics have had to navigate restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that have slashed the number of procedures they can legally perform in some states and made it difficult to recruit staff amid a broader healthcare-worker shortage.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  affiliates have announced temporary or permanent clinic closures even in states with protective \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, including Illinois, New Mexico, Ohio and the organization's home state of New York. The New York affiliate recently said it would sell its Manhattan clinic, ending a century-long presence in the borough; it has closed four other clinics over the past year.\par \par \uc2 The affiliate loses more than $30 million annually, its representatives told city lawmakers last week in a plea for more public funds. "The care New Yorkers deserve and have come to rely on from PPGNY over many years is in real danger," said Dr. Gillian Dean, the affiliate's chief medical officer.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday's Supreme Court arguments focused on South Carolina's decision in 2018 to disqualify \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  from Medicaid, the joint federal-state program for limited-income Americans. Although Medicaid funds don't pay for abortions, the state believes any income \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  receives frees up other money the organization could use to help women end unwanted pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 The justices were reviewing a lower-court ruling that found a \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  patient was entitled to take the state to court over its disqualification of the clinic for reasons unrelated to the quality of care.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2  said denying individuals a remedy could invite other states to promote healthcare policies unrelated to professional competence, such as limiting access to contraception and therapies for transgender individuals. Taking a different view, Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  suggested it was up to the federal government to rein in the state if it objected to \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 's exclusion.\par \par \uc2 A decision is expected by July.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What does the future hold for \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 ? Join the conversation below.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents are making a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/antiabortion-clash-trump-e7a49766"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rare united push}}}\uc2 to get Congress to strip \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 's federal Medicaid dollars, appealing to Republicans' broader cost-cutting efforts. Shortly after the November election, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14then co-heads of the \uc2 Department of Government Efficiency\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14cited \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 's federal dollars as an example of government waste.\par \par \uc2 The changes to \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 's funding could come as part of a restructuring of the federal Medicaid program in the coming few weeks. \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  so far hasn't been a focal point for Republican negotiators in the House and Senate, although some key Republican legislators said they would be open to such cuts.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com}}}\uc2 , Mariah Timms at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:mariah.timms@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mariah.timms@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Katy Stech Ferek at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:katy.stech@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 katy.stech@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020250402el42001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
