\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Vince Haley Is the Most Influential Trump Adviser You've Probably Never Heard Of; The longtime speechwriter is director of the White House's Domestic Policy Council, and he has quietly shaped president's agenda\b0\par\par\uc2 By Meridith McGraw and Natalie Andrews \par \uc2 1,329 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 March 2025\par 11:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 Vince Haley grew up in Alexandria, Va. An earlier version of this article incorrectly said he was born and raised in Richmond, Va. (Corrected on March 21)\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14President Trump has stocked his administration with provocateurs whose frequent appearances on cable news and combative posture on social media have made them well-known public figures.\par \par \uc2 Vince Haley is not that guy.\par \par \uc2 Haley, who leads the White House's Domestic Policy Council, prefers to stay out of the spotlight. He has posted on his largely dormant X account just once. He rarely gives interviews. And there are only a handful of photos of him online.\par \par \uc2 But his low profile belies his influence, according to interviews with nearly two dozen people who know him. Haley is one of a handful of trusted advisers who have worked for Trump since his 2016 campaign. A longtime speechwriter for the president, he has learned to channel Trump's voice and identify policy proposals that win over conservative voters.\par \par \uc2 He is credited by his colleagues with shaping the Republican Party's position on such issues as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , laying the groundwork during the 2024 campaign for Trump's cryptocurrency and anti-Dei initiatives. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trumps-second-term-plans-anti-woke-university-freedom-cities-28f8123d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has also helped the president craft}}}\uc2  some of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/01/celebrating-americas-250th-birthday/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more-unconventional ideas}}}\uc2 , such as "Freedom Cities" and the "National Garden of American Heroes."\par \par \uc2 "I can't imagine anyone having greater insight into the president's thought process, policies that appeal to him, what he likes, what he's not going to like," said Joe Grogan, who served as Domestic Policy Council director during Trump's first term.\par \par \uc2 As the head of the White House's domestic-policy operation, Haley, 58 years old, works closely with \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , Trump's deputy chief of staff for policy, on the rollout of the dozens of executive orders the president has signed since he took office two months ago. He has been tasked with making sure Trump follows through on the promises he made on the campaign trail. Inside the West Wing, the Domestic Policy Council is even informally referred to as the "Office of Promises Kept."\par \par \uc2 "Vince, \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , they are policy people, and I feel like the policy folks are ascendant," said Kellyanne Conway, who served as senior counselor to Trump in his first term and remains close to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Haley is taking the lead on health policy, drug-price transparency, energy and housing, according to administration officials, as well as other projects important to the president, such as America's 250th birthday and a commission on religious liberty.\par \par \uc2 Trump has tasked Miller with overseeing the president's signature issues, such as immigration and the border, and he has given \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  broad authority to slash government spending. The result is that Haley will have to navigate a crowded sphere of influence to ensure the Domestic Policy Council gets its work done.\par \par \uc2 With Miller and Musk in that space, "That's just a lot of cooks\u8212\'20\'14and so that would complicate the job immensely," said Cecilia Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz, who had the same position under former President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 From Newt Gingrich to \uc2 Donald Trump\par \par \uc2 Haley's deep knowledge of Republican policy stems in part from years working under Newt Gingrich, the former House speaker, and connections across a constellation of conservative groups.\par \par \uc2 Haley co-wrote a book with Gingrich in 2008 called "Drill Here, Drill Now, Pay Less" that advocated for expanded oil drilling. The book was part of an effort by Republicans to focus on increased energy production under the slogan "drill, baby, drill," a phrase that Trump and his top advisers use to this day.\par \par \uc2 Haley has worked with Trump since 2016, through three presidential campaigns, two presidencies and countless changes in staff. During last year's campaign, Haley often sat next to Trump on his private plane, according to a former campaign official.\par \par \uc2 He has long worked closely with Ross Worthington, another former Gingrich aide, who is now Trump's director of speechwriting. Haley occupies Miller's former office in the West Wing and works next door to Worthington.\par \par \uc2 In the first Trump White House and at campaign rallies, Haley would write speeches, and then stand next to the teleprompter operator as Trump veered off the script. He was also known to scan the crowd at Trump events to gauge how supporters responded to specific policies, such as banning transgender athletes. The most popular policies have moved to the center of Trump's second-term agenda.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What is your view on the implementation of President Trump's domestic-policy agenda? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Haley "is kind of like the walking encyclopedia of DJT policy," said \uc2 Tony Fabrizio\uc2 , Trump's campaign pollster. "And he also has a really good understanding of the president's voice and how the president would frame something."\par \par \uc2 During last year's presidential campaign, it was Haley's idea to take Democrats' contention that Trump was waging war on democracy\u8212\'20\'14and turn it back on them, according to Chris LaCivita, a co-manager of Trump's campaign. Haley wrote a series of speeches for Trump on how the real "war on democracy" was actually the weaponization of the justice system, a phrase that turned up on rally posters.\par \par \uc2 Long before Robert F. Kennedy Jr. joined the Trump campaign, Haley saw an opening for Trump to focus on the increasing number of children with chronic disease. After meeting with advocates, Haley wrote a speech on the issue that Trump delivered in June 2023, more than a year before the phrase "Make America Healthy Again" was coined by the Trump campaign, said a person who worked closely with Haley.\par \par \uc2 In the speech, Trump promised to create a commission to investigate the rise in autism, autoimmune disorders and other illnesses. That commission was announced soon after Kennedy was confirmed.\par \par \uc2 Shaping the Republican platform\par \par \uc2 Haley also played a central role in Trump's embrace of cryptocurrency. He met with at least one cryptocurrency executive, David Bailey, who pitched a $15 million fundraiser and a speech for Trump at a cryptocurrency conference in Nashville, Tenn. Trump agreed to participate in the dinner and the speech.\par \par \uc2 Haley also wrote the language about cryptocurrency that appeared in last year's Republican Party platform and sought ideas for how Trump could more aggressively embrace the issue.\par \par \uc2 Colleagues said Haley's Catholic faith is a driving force. Raised in Alexandria, Va., Haley, along with his twin sister, is the youngest of 11 children. He practiced law in New York and San Francisco until the 9/11 terrorist attacks inspired him to leave law and work in public policy for Gingrich. He and his wife, Bethany, have four children.\par \par \uc2 As the debate over federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits roiled the Republican Party in 2024, Haley worked to bridge the divide between Christian conservative leaders who didn't want the party to abandon the issue and those who said strict limitations on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  might alienate voters.\par \par \uc2 In spring 2024, Haley expressed to top campaign advisers that embracing a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban would put Trump in a political box. Social conservatives were pushing Trump to endorse a 16-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\u8212\'20\'14a position that went even further than some swing states\u8212\'20\'14but wasn't nearly as restrictive as other states such as Iowa.\par \par \uc2 Haley worked with Trump and other advisers to draft a Republican platform that recognized a "right to life," but ultimately left \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to the states. Trump's team credited him with avoiding a political pitfall.\par \par \uc2 "He was a key part in ensuring that we did not get into a debate about weeks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," LaCivita said. "He was so trusted by the conservative right, the Christian right, he was able to fend off a lot of potential political issues."\par \par \uc2 Write to Meridith McGraw at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Meridith.McGraw@WSJ.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Meridith.McGraw@WSJ.com}}}\uc2  and Natalie Andrews at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:natalie.andrews@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 natalie.andrews@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020250321el3l00209\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
