\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Democrats' Anti-Musk Strategy Gets First Test in Wisconsin Election; Billionaires from both sides of political spectrum pouring money into race that is poised to break record for most expensive judicial contest in U.S. history\b0\par\par\uc2 By John McCormick \par \uc2 1,163 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 March 2025\par 15:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MILWAUKEE\u8212\'20\'14\uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  has become a central character in a Wisconsin Supreme Court campaign after pouring millions into a race that marks the first major 2025 ballot test of Democratic efforts to cast the world's richest man as a political villain.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the April 1 election, Democrats have focused on Musk nearly as much as the actual Republican candidate. They are featuring the \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  chief executive and the head of President Trump's Department of Government Efficiency in campaign ads and staging protests against him. Musk is increasingly unpopular with Democratic and independent voters as he leads Trump's efforts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/federal-workers-doge-job-cuts-maps-988416ec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to cut federal employees}}}\uc2  and spending. He is part of the party's playbook in elections later this year and the 2026 midterms\u8212\'20\'14especially if Wisconsin Democrats can show him to be a political liability for Republicans. "This will be a test of whether Musk's unlimited bank account can overcome the intense rage that he has generated among Democratic voters," said Ben Wikler, the state's Democratic Party chairman.\par \par \uc2 The contest between liberal Dane County Judge Susan Crawford and Republican \uc2 Brad Schimel\uc2 , a former state attorney general and current Waukesha County judge, is technically nonpartisan. But neither party is viewing it that way and both are deploying top surrogates, with Donald Trump Jr. scheduled to visit Wisconsin Monday followed by Minnesota Gov. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the 2024 Democratic vice presidential nominee, on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Crawford is making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights central to her campaign, while Schimel is wooing Trump's base and focusing on his experience as a prosecutor.\par \par \uc2 Musk has a financial interest in the outcome. His {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/business/autos/trump-hater-of-evs-says-hes-buying-a-tesla-66553ef8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 electric-vehicle maker}}}\uc2  is challenging a Wisconsin "factory store" law that bars manufacturers from owning dealerships. \uc2 Tesla\uc2  has two company stores in the state, but buyers must travel elsewhere to pick up vehicles. The case could make its way up to the very court Musk is trying to shape.\par \par \uc2 Schimel said in an interview he is "grateful" to have Musk's financial support, but has never spoken to him. He declined to promise to recuse himself, if elected and Musk has business before the court, because such questions are "tough in the abstract." The judge said that if Musk is "looking for someone that's going to give him an automatic win on his cases, he might be supporting the wrong guy."\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  didn't respond to an email seeking comment.\par \par \uc2 The race is poised to become the most expensive judicial contest in U.S. history, even before a final flurry of spending. The previous record was set in Wisconsin's 2023 Supreme Court contest, when roughly $55 million was spent and the court flipped to a liberal majority for the first time in 15 years.\par \par \uc2 The Wisconsin race carries massive stakes in the battleground state where Trump won his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/election/2024/general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 narrowest margin}}}\uc2  in November. The outcome will weigh heavily on the fate of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and union organizing and potentially the composition of two GOP-held congressional districts that could be critical in Democratic efforts to win the House of Representatives in 2026.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, in what is expected to be the only debate between the two candidates, Crawford mentioned Musk several times, including one reference to her opponent as "Elon Schimel."\par \par \uc2 In an interview, Crawford said she doesn't see Musk's involvement as beneficial to her candidacy\u8212\'20\'14or for Wisconsin voters.\par \par \uc2 "They're trying to sell more cars here," said Crawford, a former attorney for unions and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Musk is easily the biggest individual donor in the race, based on disclosures so far. His America PAC's latest filing shows nearly $6.2 million spent on get-out-the-vote efforts. Building America's Future, a nonprofit he is linked to that doesn't have to disclose its donors, has already run or has reservations for $6.3 million in Wisconsin advertising, data from AdImpact shows. Musk was the largest 2024 election-cycle donor, spending close to $300 million to help Trump and other Republicans. He was drawn into the race by the prospect of flipping the court's control, according to a person familiar with the PAC's activities. The organization is targeting infrequent voters, the person said, as it did in support of Trump's election in November. The Wisconsin victor will win a 10-year term on the state court. It currently has a four-to-three liberal majority, but the retirement of a judge who has been on the court since 1995 has put the majority in play.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin's high court will soon decide whether it believes an 1849 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is the law of the state. It will also hear a separate case on whether the Wisconsin constitution protects the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Schimel has been criticized by Democrats for saying that the liberal majority, made up of four women who stood up behind Crawford at a news conference after the debate, were "driven by their emotions" during oral arguments on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
