\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin Supreme Court candidate Susan Crawford at a news conference after the debate alongside the court's liberal majority. PHOTO: John McCormick/WSJ\par \par \uc2 In the interview, Schimel said there was "nothing about gender" in what he said about emotions and that he was referring to a "loss of objectivity that was evident" in how the liberal justices were questioning lawyers in the case.\par \par \uc2 While Musk has attracted the most attention, he's just one of the billionaires weighing in on the race. Among Democrats, they include financier \uc2 George Soros\uc2  ($1 million), Illinois Gov. JB Pritzker ($500,000) and \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2  co-founder \uc2 Reid Hoffman\uc2  ($250,000). Their donations to the state Democratic Party were funneled to Crawford's campaign.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Do you think the Democrats' strategy in Wisconsin will be successful? Why or why not? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Richard and Elizabeth Uihlein, whose packing supply company is based in Wisconsin, gave $1.3 million to Republicans to help Schimel and their super PAC has already spent or has reservations for $2.5 million in advertising.\par \par \uc2 Other Republican billionaires financing the race include roofing magnate \uc2 Diane Hendricks\uc2  ($975,000) and Joe Ricketts ($500,000), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/SB10000872396390443720204578000490604078074"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the founder}}}\uc2  of what became online brokerage \uc2 TD Ameritrade\uc2  and an owner of the \uc2 Chicago Cubs\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The GOP megadonors made their contributions to the state Republican Party, before it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cfis.wi.gov/ReportsOutputFiles/0300173SpringPre-Primary2025e8170210202565829PMCF-2Report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 transferred nearly $1.7 million}}}\uc2  to Schimel's campaign.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://law.marquette.edu/poll/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marquette Law School poll}}}\uc2  taken in late February of Wisconsin voters showed the race very much up in the air. The survey also showed 53% of voters overall view Musk unfavorably, a number that jumps to 58% for independents and 97% for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Write to John McCormick at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:mccormick.john@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mccormick.john@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020250315el3f0015p\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
