\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 RFK Jr. Backs Vaccines and Trump's Agenda in Senate Testimony; Kennedy vowed to fight chronic disease and called  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  a tragedy\b0\par\par\uc2 By Liz Essley Whyte and Kristina Peterson \par \uc2 891 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 January 2025\par 21:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2  said he supports vaccines and vowed to lessen the burden of chronic diseases during fiery questioning from senators who will decide whether to confirm him as President Trump's health secretary.\par \par \uc2 Members of the Senate's finance committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/trump-cabinet-confirmation-hearings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 questioned Kennedy}}}\uc2  on the first of two days of testimony before a vote to install him as Health and Human Services secretary. He can only afford to lose backing from three Republicans in the Senate unless some Democrats back him.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy said that he is most passionate about alleviating chronic diseases and that he would otherwise defer to Trump's orders. Kennedy deflected some questions about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, Medicare drug-price negotiations and Medicaid cuts. And he rebutted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/rfk-jr-wants-to-rethink-the-measles-vaccine-heres-what-the-science-shows-2527380e?mod=googlenewsfeed&st=wLL55s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims that he opposes vaccines}}}\uc2  or would profit from working against them, despite his past activism raising doubts about the shots.\par \par \uc2 "The only thing I want is good science," Kennedy said.\par \par \uc2 Democrats questioned whether Kennedy had the management experience to lead an organization with the health department's vast reach. It spends more than $1.7 trillion annually on the healthcare of millions of Americans, pandemic preparedness and scientific research.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy is a lawyer, environmental activist and scion of the Kennedy clan whose colorful life was a recurring feature of his confirmation hearing. Senators entered into the record a letter from his cousin Caroline Kennedy, daughter of president \uc2 John F. Kennedy\uc2 , calling Kennedy an unqualified conspiracy theorist.\par \par \uc2 "Bobby is addicted to attention and power. Bobby preys on the desperation of parents of sick children," Caroline Kennedy wrote.\par \par \uc2 Sen. Michael Bennet (D., Colo.) asked \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2  to clarify whether he had said previously that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/see-how-ticks-and-mosquitoes-are-carrying-diseases-to-more-of-the-u-s-63bace7f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lyme disease}}}\uc2  was a bioweapon, a decades-old conspiracy theory. "I did probably say that," Kennedy said.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy pushed back on questioning from Sen. \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  (D., Ore.) about his past statements doubting vaccine safety. Kennedy has said he believes the polio vaccine might have done more harm than good and has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/rfk-jr-wants-to-rethink-the-measles-vaccine-heres-what-the-science-shows-2527380e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 linked childhood vaccines to autism}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14claims scientists have said are unfounded.\par \par \uc2 "I support the measles vaccine. I support the polio vaccine. I will do nothing as \uc2 HHS\uc2  secretary that makes it difficult or discourages" people from getting those vaccines, Kennedy said.\par \par \uc2 Sen Elizabeth Warren (D., Mass.) asked if Kennedy would swear off fees from vaccine lawsuits against pharmaceutical companies for at least four years after serving as health secretary. Kennedy declined, but said he would comply with ethics guidelines.\par \par \uc2 Democrats including Bennet attacked Kennedy for retreating from his past support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. "This is a job where it is life and death," Bennet said. "It's too important for the games that you're playing, Mr. Kennedy."\par \par \uc2 Kennedy said he believes every \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a tragedy but didn't commit to more restrictions on mifepristone, a drug known as the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill.\par \par \uc2 "President Trump has asked me to study the safety of mifepristone. He has not yet taken a stand on how to regulate it. Whatever he does, I will implement it," Kennedy said.\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 James Lankford\uc2  (R., Okla.), who opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, said after the hearing that he was satisfied with Kennedy's comments. "He made some very clear statements today on that," Lankford said.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/robert-f-kennedy-jr-shifts-to-independent-presidential-bid-e3570e7f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaigned for president}}}\uc2  as an independent before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/robert-f-kennedy-jr-drops-out-of-presidential-race-endorses-trump-f043e9b9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsing Trump}}}\uc2  in August. He brought with him a coalition of "Make America Healthy Again" supporters who want more support for alternative medicines and a review of ingredients in packaged foods.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy said Wednesday that he would focus on fighting the rise of conditions such as diabetes, asthma and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/adult-adhd-symptoms-treatment-diagnosis-4c371108"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder}}}\uc2 . "Why are healthcare costs so high in the first place? The obvious answer is chronic disease," he said.\par \par \uc2 No Republicans have said publicly they would oppose Kennedy. Sen. \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.), a polio survivor, and centrist Republican Sens. \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine and \uc2 Lisa Murkowski\uc2  of Alaska are considered possible defectors. Republicans control the Senate with 53 votes, so Kennedy can't lose more than three votes, if he gets no support from Democrats. In the event of a tie, Vice President \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  would cast the deciding vote.\par \par \uc2 Republican Sen. \uc2 Bill Cassidy\uc2 , a medical doctor from Louisiana and likely a pivotal vote in Kennedy's confirmation, asked the nominee questions about Medicare and Medicaid that he struggled to answer. Asked how care for people eligible for both federal health programs could be integrated, Kennedy said, "I'm not exactly sure because I'm not in there."\par \par \uc2 Republicans expressed optimism about working with Kennedy to improve healthcare. "God has a divine purpose for you, and I look forward to working with you," Sen. Roger Marshall (R., Kan.), told Kennedy.\par \par \uc2 Sen. Bernie Sanders (I., Vt.), who some had thought might support Kennedy because they share some views on ultraprocessed food and pharmaceutical company profits, grilled the nominee about vaccines and whether healthcare is a human right.\par \par \uc2 "Free speech doesn't cost anybody anything but in healthcare if you smoke cigarettes for 20 years and you get cancer, you are now taking from the pool," Kennedy said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Liz Essley Whyte at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:liz.whyte@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liz.whyte@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Kristina Peterson at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:kristina.peterson@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kristina.peterson@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020250129el1t006el\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
