\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 RFK Jr. Has a Battle Plan to Get Senate Confirmation; Health secretary nominee intends to play down vaccine skepticism, pro- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  stances\b0\par\par\uc2 By Liz Essley Whyte, Kristina Peterson and Natalie Andrews \par \uc2 1,182 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 December 2024\par 13:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14\uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2 's attempt to win over Capitol Hill starts this week with a strategy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/how-rfk-jr-transformed-from-green-hero-to-vaccine-skeptic-e6d89193"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to play down the topic of vaccines}}}\uc2 , adhere tightly to President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's messaging on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and talk up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/donald-trump-rfk-jr-health-policies-bba88214"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 healthy food}}}\uc2  and preventing chronic disease, according to people familiar with his thinking.\par \par \uc2 His {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/rfk-trump-health-policy-vaccines-29afe4cc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nomination to lead}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  has already met {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/trump-cabinet-sexual-assault-allegations-hegseth-rfk-c61fc4b2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resistance in some corners}}}\uc2 , as Republican senators voice concerns about his years of vaccine skepticism, his pro-choice stance and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/trump-agriculture-pick-brooke-rollins-rfk-jr-1a85beda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unorthodox takes on agricultural policy}}}\uc2 . He can afford to lose only three Republican votes if every Senate Democrat votes against his confirmation, and his strategy also includes trying to win support from Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy is slated to be on the Hill several days this week, sitting down with more than two dozen senators and a team of Republican staffers, people familiar with his plans said.\par \par \uc2 His team is hoping to assuage senators' concerns about his criticism of vaccines, according to people familiar with his strategy. He is likely to tell senators that, if confirmed to lead \uc2 HHS\uc2 , he isn't planning to take anyone's vaccines away and instead wants to promote transparent, safe, effective vaccines, the people said.\par \par \uc2 Sen. Ron Johnson of Wisconsin, a Republican who is attempting to persuade fellow senators to vote to confirm Kennedy, said that many of his colleagues like most of Kennedy's message but that some have concerns about his past comments on vaccines. Kennedy has said that the Covid-19 vaccines were the deadliest ever made and that the polio vaccine might have caused more deaths than it averted.\par \par \uc2 "Efforts to undermine public confidence in proven cures are not just uninformed\u8212\'20\'14they're dangerous," said Sen. \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.), adding that the polio vaccine has saved millions of lives. "Anyone seeking the Senate's consent to serve in the incoming administration would do well to steer clear of even the appearance of association with such efforts," said McConnell, who had polio as a child.\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 Mike Rounds\uc2  (R., S.D.) also expressed concern about Kennedy's plans, saying: "I do not want to lose our vaccine programs."\par \par \uc2 Kennedy spokeswoman Katie Miller said he "believes the polio vaccine should be available to the public and thoroughly and properly studied."\par \par \uc2 Many food and pharmaceutical trade associations, including the \uc2 Pharmaceutical Research and Manufacturers of America\uc2 , a lobbying behemoth, have declined to oppose Kennedy's confirmation, out of fear it would hurt their interests in the long run.\par \par \uc2 "You always want to try to work with the regulator," said Nick Shipley, an independent consultant and registered lobbyist who works on pharmaceutical issues. "It probably doesn't behoove anyone to burn down the house on these things."\par \par \uc2 Kennedy dined earlier this month with Trump and pharmaceutical executives at Mar-a-Lago in Florida. The health nominee brought along his attorney and close adviser, \uc2 Aaron Siri\uc2 , people familiar with the dinner said. Siri is a strident vaccine skeptic who has filed a petition for the Food and Drug Administration to revoke approval of a polio shot, among other efforts.\par \par \uc2 Siri has said the polio vaccine needs more study, a claim rejected by health regulators. Siri is the main adviser helping Kennedy vet top staff for the health department, a person familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 Some senators strongly opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as Sen. \uc2 James Lankford\uc2  (R., Okla.), are seen as likely to question Kennedy's beliefs on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Kennedy, a longtime Democrat, supported \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights during his independent presidential bid, and his Team Kennedy website as of Friday said he supported legislation to enshrine the protections of Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy will likely tell concerned senators that, as a member of Trump's administration, he would back the president-elect's position that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an issue best left to the states after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade, a person familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy doesn't see \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy as a high priority and knows that focusing on it would impede his bid to make America healthier, people familiar with his thinking added.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion activists are seeking public concessions from Kennedy and the Trump team in exchange for not opposing his confirmation, according to people familiar with groups that oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Advisers to Kennedy said he plans to stick closely to the main themes of his "Make America Healthy Again" campaign, including the importance of researching chronic disease and cracking down on ultraprocessed foods.\par \par \uc2 "He's very passionate about the reality that we have to turn around the trend that America's becoming so progressively unhealthy," said Dr. Robert Redfield, a former Trump administration official who has been talking to Kennedy. "That's what he's going to focus on."\par \par \uc2 Kennedy's team hopes the health agenda can win over some Democrats, providing some cushion should he lose any GOP support. Their target list includes Sens. Bernie Sanders (I., Vt.) and \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  (D., N.J.), according to a person familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Sanders said last week he hadn't yet been contacted by anyone from Kennedy's team. Sanders said it would be "premature" to announce his decision on the nomination. Booker said he has concerns but isn't an "automatic" no on Kennedy. He had said he doesn't have a meeting scheduled with Kennedy.\par \par \uc2 "The food industry makes billions of dollars by getting our children addicted to unhealthy food, which causes diabetes and a bunch of other illnesses. I think Kennedy understands that," Sanders said earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What questions should the Senate ask RFK Jr. during the confirmation process? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  (D., Pa.) indicated willingness to hear Kennedy out. "I'm not immediately, like, 100% hell no," he said. "If that's going to be the guy, you have to discover where you can work together."\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the MAHA agenda might turn off some senators. Sen. \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2  (R., Iowa) said he would meet with Kennedy in January and planned to talk to him about his previous statements opposing genetically modified foods, many of which are grown by the Iowa farmers he represents.\par \par \uc2 "The most important thing is whether or not he's for genetically modified corn and soybeans because it's increased production so much," Grassley said. Kennedy has called for food labeling on genetically modified food and has said genetically modified organisms are "dangerous."\par \par \uc2 Kennedy is likely to focus on common ground\u8212\'20\'14such as dislike of lab-grown meat\u8212\'20\'14with senators close to farmers and ranchers, a person familiar with the issue said.\par \par \uc2 Laura Kusisto, Catherine Lucey and Jared S. Hopkins contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Liz Essley Whyte at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:liz.whyte@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liz.whyte@wsj.com}}}\uc2 , Kristina Peterson at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:kristina.peterson@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kristina.peterson@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Natalie Andrews at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:natalie.andrews@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 natalie.andrews@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020241216ekcg001jl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
