\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Texas Sues New York Doctor, Challenging  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Provider Shield Laws; Lawsuit says doctor violated Texas law in prescribing pregnancy-ending medication through telemedicine\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas and Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 673 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 December 2024\par 00:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Texas is suing a New York-based doctor for allegedly prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills through telemedicine to a patient from the Lone Star state.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit is believed to be the first challenge to laws designed to shield doctors in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections from legal challenges elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 Texas Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  is accusing Dr. Margaret Daley Carpenter of violating Texas law by prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to a 20-year-old pregnant patient in Collin County, Texas. The lawsuit, filed in Collin County Thursday, is seeking up to $250,000.\par \par \uc2 Texas is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of more than a dozen states}}}\uc2  enforcing a near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the Supreme Court eliminated federal constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Carpenter is the co-medical director and co-founder of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Coalition for Telemedicine, an advocacy group that seeks to expand access to telemedicine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the U.S.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  is prioritizing his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda over the health and well-being of women by attempting to shut down telemedicine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide," the group said in a statement Friday. The statement called shield laws "essential in safeguarding and enabling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care regardless of a patient's zip code or ability to pay."\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit said the patient was allegedly prescribed mifepristone and misoprostol, the two-drug regimen for medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The patient went to the hospital due to "hemorrhage or severe bleeding," and had been around nine weeks pregnant, according to the lawsuit. The lawsuit didn't name the woman.\par \par \uc2 "In Texas, we treasure the health and lives of mothers and babies, and this is why out-of-state doctors may not illegally and dangerously prescribe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing drugs to Texas residents," Paxton said in a statement announcing the lawsuit Friday.\par \par \uc2 New York passed a law in 2023 granting legal protections to doctors who prescribe medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to patients out-of-state through telemedicine.\par \par \uc2 "We will always protect our providers from unjust attempts to punish them for doing their job," New York Attorney General Letitia James said in a statement Friday.\par \par \uc2 Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/abortion-pill-increase-roe-wade-68472ff8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accounted for nearly two-thirds}}}\uc2  of all abortions in the U.S. last year, according to a report released earlier this year by the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a research group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills by blue-state providers to women in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans has thwarted the ability of conservative states to bring down \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates within their borders since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade in 2022. There was a 155% increase in abortions provided by mail in the year ending in June, according to WeCount, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -data project sponsored by the Society of Family Planning, which supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The practice has frustrated conservative politicians, who say these providers are flouting the ability of states to regulate medicine within their own borders. Earlier this year, Arkansas Attorney General Tim Griffin, a Republican, demanded two \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -pill providers stop helping state residents get the pills, saying such actions violated Arkansas law.\par \par \uc2 Providers from states with shield laws have said they are aware of the legal risks associated with prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication to people in states with bans. Many already avoid traveling to those states, making it difficult in practice to enforce any judgment against them.\par \par \uc2 The litigation over contending state laws will likely end up in federal court, said Mary Ziegler, a law professor at the \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Doctors who are working under shield laws are unlikely to change their practices, as many expected legal challenges like this one, Ziegler said.\par \par \uc2 "This is not all surprising to any of these doctors, and I think they feel comfortable enough with the shield protections that they're willing to take the risk," Ziegler said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020241213ekcd006hd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
