\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Voters Continued to Back  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights. It Didn't Help Democrats. Constitutional amendments passed in seven states, but many of those same places also backed Trump\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 976 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 November 2024\par 20:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights met their limit as an electoral force on Tuesday. Voters enshrined broad protections for the procedure across seven states, including Arizona, Montana and deep-red Missouri, but that enthusiasm failed to translate into broader Democratic wins.\par \par \uc2 Since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  overturned Roe v. Wade two years ago, the issue has been a rare bright spot for Democrats, even as voters expressed hunger for change and frustration with the border and the economy. It helped propel the party to better-than-expected results in the 2022 midterms and, in prior ballot-measure fights, voters showed strong bipartisan support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in states as diverse as Ohio, Michigan and Kansas.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's story was a more sobering one for Democrats. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-results-ballot-2024-a4000fa4?st=MDCoui"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  was on the ballot}}}\uc2  in 10 states, where large numbers of voters supported broad protections for the procedure, even as they voted for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Among those who said they think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases, some 30% voted for Trump, according to an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/election-2024-voters-demographics-votecast-survey-5a21c604"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AP VoteCast survey}}}\uc2 , a large survey of people who voted in the election.\par \par \uc2 "This is a very mixed result. I have some cognitive dissonance here because we saw enormous support for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8230\'20\'26juxtapositioned with a really disappointing national result," said Deirdre Schifeling, chief political and advocacy officer for \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Missouri, Trump won 58.5% of the vote, while the state voted in favor of a constitutional amendment protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. In Arizona and Nevada, similar ballot measures passed with more than 60% support\u8212\'20\'14numbers more lopsided than any previous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum since Roe was overturned\u8212\'20\'14yet Trump was ahead in both states Wednesday by healthy margins.\par \par \uc2 Aaron Turner, a 28-year-old who lives about two hours south of St. Louis, Mo., said he voted for both the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights amendment and Trump because he believes the government should play a smaller role in Americans' lives.\par \par \uc2 "I ultimately believe that this is the right thing in that it does allow individuals their own opportunity to make their own moral choices," said Turner, an engineer-in-training.\par \par \uc2 In Florida, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups poured more than $100 million into an effort to overturn an unpopular six-week ban in that state and the measure drew support from 57% of voters on a night when Trump won the state by double digits. But the ballot initiative failed despite the strong support, because it needed to clear a 60% threshold to win. The other two measures that failed came from South Dakota and Nebraska.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups said Tuesday's results showed that voters saw liberals' agenda as too extreme. "Democrats led by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  went 'all in' on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as their number one issue," Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America President Marjorie Dannenfelser said. "Americans have rejected the Democrats' no-limits \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda."\par \par \uc2 Voters ranked \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as their third-most important issue, according to the AP VoteCast survey, but that trailed significantly behind the economy and immigration. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  also garnered less robust support among women than Biden did in 2020, according to those results.\par \par \uc2 Trump, whose three Supreme Court appointments in his first term helped seal Roe's downfall, sought to minimize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 's role in the campaign by saying the issue was now a matter for the states. His efforts to find a middle ground were often fumbling, and he sometimes angered his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/antiabortion-clash-trump-e7a49766"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allies in the antiabortion movement}}}\uc2 , who publicly agonized over whether to vote for him. The strategy, however, appears to have accomplished Trump's goal of giving voters who favored \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights enough assurance to cast a vote for him based on other issues.\par \par \uc2 "Clearly, Trump was not viewed as a threat to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights by enough voters, which is mind boggling," \uc2 Tom Bonier\uc2 , a Democratic political strategist, wrote on X.\par \par \uc2 Republicans also tried to shift the focus to transgender rights, a less broadly popular social issue. They invested heavily in advertisements about transgender players on female sports teams and prior statements Harris had made about surgeries for prisoners.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still widely protected in most states around the country, while it is significantly restricted in 16 others. That state-by-state patchwork is likely to remain, but the president can shift policy in ways that could have nationwide effects on access. For example, the country has seen a huge surge since Roe fell in women ordering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills online without seeing a doctor in person. Antiabortion groups are pushing Trump to curtail that practice.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What do you think the future holds for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the U.S.? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 During the campaign, Democrats leaned into stories of women facing difficult circumstances, including rape, incest and severe pregnancy complications, which have resonated with voters across the political spectrum. Harris blanketed the airwaves in swing states with a tough ad showing Hadley Duvall, a Kentucky woman who was sexually abused by her stepfather and became pregnant when she was 12 years old. Duvall said women in her position wouldn't be able to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in states such as Kentucky today. "Trump did this," she said.\par \par \uc2 Duvall's story helped Democratic Gov. \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  win re-election last year in a hard-fought campaign in red Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 Public opinion researcher Tresa Undem said her polling shows that the issue isn't losing salience among independent voters. But she said the election was ultimately about "a cocktail of things," including a view that Trump would be a disruptive force.\par \par \uc2 Aaron Zitner contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020241106ekb6004ph\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*