\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Republicans Take the Senate; GOP picked up seats in West Virginia, Montana and Ohio\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lindsay Wise and Siobhan Hughes \par \uc2 1,299 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 November 2024\par 12:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/election/2024/general/senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seized control of the Senate}}}\uc2  after picking up seats in West Virginia, Montana and Ohio and beating back challenges in Florida, Nebraska and Texas.\par \par \uc2 Republicans had been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/2024-presidential-senate-and-house-election-forecasts-5c4b54b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 favored to win a majority}}}\uc2  in the chamber; now it's only a question of how big that majority will be. Early Wednesday, Democrats were still defending seats in five other battleground states that President Biden won by less than 3 percentage points: Arizona, Nevada, Michigan, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Candidates, party committees and outside groups poured hundreds of millions into the battle for the Senate. Republicans are now poised to determine the fate of the next president's agenda and whether he or she will be able to confirm executive and judicial nominees, including filling any opening on the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 "As a new Republican Senate majority, our focus will be to take on an agenda that reflects America's priorities\u8212\'20\'14lower prices, less spending, secure borders, and American energy dominance," Sen. \uc2 John Barrasso\uc2  (R., Wyo.), who chairs the Senate Republican Conference, said.\par \par \uc2 Democrats currently hold a narrow 51-49 majority in the Senate, but were defending far more seats this year including three in states won by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2020.\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, wealthy former car-dealership owner \uc2 Bernie Moreno\uc2  defeated three-term Sen. \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2 , the only Democrat holding statewide office there, by riding on Trump's long coattails in the state. West Virginia's Senate seat flipped from blue to red soon after polls closed there at 7:30 p.m., with Republican Gov. \uc2 Jim Justice\uc2  handily winning the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/democratic-sen-joe-manchin-wont-run-for-re-election-in-west-virginia-5f3e2fbf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seat vacated by the retirement}}}\uc2  of independent Sen. Joe Manchin, who caucused with Democrats.\par \par \uc2 In Montana, political newcomer Tim Sheehy ousted Sen. \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2  by running as a Trump-endorsed conservative. As in Ohio, Tester was the last Democrat in statewide elected office in Montana.\par \par \uc2 "Republicans had the advantage to win control of the Senate before Election Day," said Nathan L. Gonzales, editor of Inside Politics, an elections analyst.\par \par \uc2 Democrats also lost their best offensive opportunity in the long shot of Texas, where Sen. Ted Cruz was able to fend off Rep. \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/is-ted-cruz-blowing-his-re-election-race-fef215a2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a former NFL football player and civil-rights attorney}}}\uc2 . In Florida, Republican Sen. \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  also defeated his Democratic challenger, former Rep. \uc2 Debbie Mucarsel-Powell\uc2 , the Associated Press projected.\par \par \uc2 It wasn't all bad news for Senate Democrats, who held on to an open seat in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/republican-larry-hogans-campaign-formula-includes-rejecting-a-trump-endorsement-1531411c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deep-blue Maryland}}}\uc2 . Former Gov. \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  there lost to Democrat Angela Alsobrooks, the Associated Press projected.\par \par \uc2 Republicans tried to capitalize on voters' {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/trump-harris-election-inflation-0797554a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worries about inflation}}}\uc2 , border security and transgender issues, while Democrats counted on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-ballot-measures-election-2024-ed49d798"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enthusiasm for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  to mobilize women, suburbanites and young people.\par \par \uc2 Many voters on Tuesday said they voted along party lines for both president and their Senate candidate, but some said they were motivated by specific issues rather than party loyalty.\par \par \uc2 Sara Gift, a registered Republican in Bucks County, Pa., said she voted for both Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and incumbent Democratic Sen. Bob Casey, over concern about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. "I feel like they're coming for contraception next," Gift, a 47-year-old registered nurse, said of Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Jack Williamson, 86, who described himself as a lifelong Democrat, said he voted for Republican Senate candidate \uc2 Mike Rogers\uc2  in the Detroit suburb of Warren, Mich., because of Democrats' policies surrounding electric vehicles, which he described as a mandate that could "destroy" the auto industry in his state. He said he also voted for Trump.\par \par \uc2 Two to five GOP pickups seen\par \par \uc2 The Cook Political Report had projected Republicans to pick up between two and five seats, including West Virginia.\par \par \uc2 A net gain of two seats was enough to secure a Republican Senate majority, as all GOP incumbents won re-election.\par \par \uc2 In the unexpectedly close race in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/a-tattooed-union-leader-is-threatening-to-topple-a-republican-senator-in-a-deep-red-state-229ed8b4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruby-red Nebraska}}}\uc2 , two-term incumbent Republican Sen. \uc2 Deb Fischer\uc2  defeated independent Dan Osborn, a former union leader.\par \par \uc2 Montana: Tester in trouble\par \par \uc2 Montana was Republicans' best pickup opportunity after West Virginia. Tester, a Democratic farmer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/jon-tester-montana-republican-senate-majority-322f7db8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trailed in the polls}}}\uc2  and early returns behind Sheehy, a businessman and retired Navy SEAL endorsed by Trump.\par \par \uc2 Trump won Montana by 16 percentage points in 2020, and Tester needed a substantial number of Trump supporters to vote for him if he were to defy political gravity and win a fourth term. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
