\par \par \uc2 Montana Democratic Sen. \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2  has been trailing in the polls. PHOTO: Louise Johns for WSJ\par \par \uc2 Sheehy argued that Tester's voting record is too liberal for Montana and that the Democrat would be a rubber stamp for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , should she be elected.\par \par \uc2 Tester was the only Senate Democrat who didn't endorse Harris for president, but he joined other Democrats in campaigning on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, which he framed as a personal freedom in line with Montana's libertarian values.\par \par \uc2 Ohio: Brown tried to hang on\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, the three-term Brown was in the fight of his political life because of the strength of support for Trump in the state. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/strange-bedfellows-democrats-and-trump-blow-up-20-year-unity-on-trade-1511887447"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 longtime trade skeptic}}}\uc2  built a personal brand that superseded shifts in the political tides.\par \par \uc2 Brown faced a barrage of negative advertising as Republicans portrayed him as a liberal, particularly on immigration and on transgender issues. Democrats tried to tarnish the Republican candidate, Moreno, as an untrustworthy car salesman by pointing to his history as the wealthy owner of a chain of auto dealerships. Democrats also made hay of comments by Moreno in September questioning why women over 50 care about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\u8212\'20\'14an offhand remark with the power to stir up a major voting bloc still incensed about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court's 2022 decision}}}\uc2  to end federal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania, Wisconsin, Michigan\u8212\'20\'14and Texas\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, Casey was fighting to survive a challenge from 