\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Voters Are Poised to Reshape  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Access, From Missouri to Montana; Ten states are set to vote on ballot measures that could restore points of access in the South and elsewhere\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,099 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 November 2024\par 10:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups are on track to secure constitutional protections for the procedure in as many as 10 states on Tuesday, which would mark the most significant expansion of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2  since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 Polling data and fundraising totals have signaled strong support for most of the ballot initiatives, which appear in states with a range of political leanings. The measure that could have the biggest practical impact comes from Florida, which had been an island of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the South until a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/six-week-abortion-ban-florida-c5f00f7e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week ban went into effect}}}\uc2  in May of this year. But it is also the toughest test because supporters need to reach a 60% threshold for passage.\par \par \uc2 Other states that could see major changes are Missouri and South Dakota, both of which have strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans currently in place.\par \par \uc2 Voters in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-rights-are-on-the-ballot-in-arizona-will-it-affect-the-presidential-race-1ce0e85f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 battleground states of Arizona}}}\uc2  and Nevada also could decide to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights there. Democrats are hoping the measures {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/kamala-harris-women-voters-election-2024-f544652f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will help drive turnout}}}\uc2  and deliver a presidential victory for Kamala Harris. Arizona currently limits the procedure to 15 weeks of pregnancy, about two months earlier than what was allowed under Roe. Nevada already allows \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to 24 weeks, but supporters say a constitutional amendment would cement those rights.\par \par \uc2 Some 17 states now ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the earliest weeks of pregnancy. Most of the ballot measures would restore access through fetal viability, or about halfway through a typical pregnancy\u8212\'20\'14although opponents argue that the initiatives are so broadly worded that they would allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 "What's very clear across all campaigns is that people don't want the government involved in private medical decisions. That's been this uniting force," said Chris Melody Fields Figueredo, executive director of the Ballot Initiative Strategy Center, a nonprofit that promotes progressive ballot measures.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters already have used ballot initiatives to override conservative legislatures, winning seven consecutive measures since Roe was overturned. In some of the states being contested now, groups favoring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access are fundraising at a clip that far outpaces their opponents, including in Florida where they have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/harris-trump-election-10-25-24/card/florida-abortion-rights-campaign-raises-100-million-signaling-momentum-in-final-days-gTegxW3hLXM06t73eQ6P"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pulled in more than $100 million}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Polling on ballot measures has been more limited than in the presidential contest and other high-profile races. Antiabortion groups say they have seen some late fundraising momentum and remain optimistic they could pull out a win in some of these states, especially Florida.\par \par \uc2 "Going into Election Day, we're seeing ballot-measure races tighten in a way we haven't in previous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -amendment fights," said Kelsey Pritchard, director of state public affairs for Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America. She said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters were using exaggerated scare tactics to suggest that women can never get abortions, even in grave emergencies.\par \par \uc2 Florida is a crucial battleground because before the overturning of Roe, it had the third-highest number of abortions in the U.S. After Roe's downfall, Florida became one of the few access points in the South, and women often drove there overnight from places such as Louisiana and Texas.\par \par \uc2 That has changed since the six-week ban. The state has seen about 2,500 fewer in-person abortions each month, according to WeCount, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -data project sponsored by the Society of Family Planning, which supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. That has had ripple effects across the country, straining clinics in North Carolina and leading to a surge in demand for pills ordered online.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers said women still sometimes travel to Florida from out of state only to find out they are too far along in pregnancy for the procedure. "It's horrible news to have to deliver over and over and over again," said Chelsea Daniels, a doctor at a Miami \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/antiabortion-clash-trump-e7a49766"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 antiabortion side has struggled}}}\uc2  to mount strong campaigns in states across the country, faced with donors pessimistic about the prospects for success. But in Florida it has an ally in Republican Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who has taken an unusually aggressive posture toward defeating the measure, calling it "radical" and "very, very extreme." A state public-health agency has run information on its website defending the ability of women facing medical emergencies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ahca.myflorida.com/content/download/25110/file/9-19-24-Notice-to-Providers.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to obtain abortions}}}\uc2  under current law, and the \uc2 Florida health department{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.flnd.527759/gov.uscourts.flnd.527759.1.1_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently threatened criminal charges}}}\uc2  against television stations for running an ad in support of the measure, saying it was misleading.\par \par \uc2 "If we win in Florida, it will be because of his leadership, and it serves as a model going forward," Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America President Marjorie Dannenfelser said of DeSantis.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents also believe they can win in South Dakota, where they have a fundraising edge. Nebraska, meanwhile, presents the most complicated picture, because the state ballot includes two competing measures, one to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and the other to outlaw the procedure in most cases after the first trimester. That has the potential to muddy the waters.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups are optimistic that they can pull out a win in Missouri, the first state to enforce its near-total ban after the Supreme Court overturned Roe. They have a fundraising advantage, having pulled in about $30 million compared with about $5 million for their opponents.\par \par \uc2 Rachel Sweet, the campaign manager for Missourians for Constitutional Freedom, also has led successful \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights ballot-measure campaigns in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-vote-results-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-supporters-prevail-in-midterm-ballot-measures-11667986139"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kentucky}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/election-day-ballots-ohio-abortion-maine-texas-colorado-d9922480"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2  , using messaging focused on freedom, medical privacy and individual choice.\par \par \uc2 "In a state such as Missouri, you can't win with just Democrats, right? There aren't enough Democrats to do that," Sweet said.\par \par \uc2 The Missouri campaign has featured distinctly religious messaging. Sweet's group has run an ad featuring a pastor who says, "When a woman says an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is right for her, I believe that should be her decision, not the government's."\par \par \uc2 Cassidy Anderson, who is helping lead the campaign against the initiative, said that presenting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a decision between a person and God is a miscalculation in Missouri. "That's a poor choice. You're going to be hard-pressed to find many Bible-believing churches that are going to believe that," she said.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What will be the political impact if the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights side wins on ballot initiatives? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020241103ekb30005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
