\par\par \uc2 Pro VC Industry News\par \uc2 WSJ Pro\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive-Health \highlight\uc2  Startups Prep for Election Outcome; Startups develop strategies geared toward a Trump or Harris presidency\b0\par\par\uc2 By Brian Gormley \par \uc2 819 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 November 2024\par 12:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Venture capitalists and startups in \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  are scenario planning for how the U.S. presidential election could affect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services and other areas in the field.\par \par \uc2 Dandi Fertility, a startup that provides telehealth services and in vitro fertilization care kits to make hormone injections more comfortable, has plans for both a Trump and a Harris presidency, said co-founder and Chief Executive Jake Kent.\par \par \uc2 He said that with the possible influence of Project 2025, a blueprint for the next conservative president by \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 , there is uncertainty about future protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  under a Trump presidency. Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said he has nothing to do with Project 2025 and has voiced support for IVF.\par \par \uc2 Under a Trump presidency, Dandi would increase its efforts in telehealth to provide a centralized resource for patients who may need assistance getting care outside their state if IVF restrictions were to increase.\par \par \uc2 If Harris wins, the company would expect a more supportive political climate for IVF and increased demand for the service. In that scenario, Dandi could work with IVF clinics, which are already struggling with high demand, to provide more personalized care to patients, Kent said.\par \par \uc2 "Depending on how this election goes, it's going to shape which route we push down," Kent added.\par \par \uc2 Venture investment in women's health, a category that includes \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has increased 314% since 2018, \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank\uc2 , a division of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 First Citizens Bank}}}\uc2 , said in January. The growth has come as investors see broader opportunities in the range of health needs for women, the report said.\par \par \uc2 One of the biggest issues is the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. The Supreme Court's 2022 ruling in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization overturned the Roe v. Wade constitutional protection for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and several states have since enacted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Vice President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  supports {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/harris-trump-presidential-debate-election-2024/card/harris-delivers-a-strong-punch-on-abortion-rights-02n3irYiXHiJjdihta36?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restoring national protections}}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  found under Roe v. Wade, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  has said he plans to leave the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  matter to states. Trump also has said he would veto a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Winx Health\u8212\'20\'14a startup provider of vaginal and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-health\b0 \highlight\uc2  products and education, including morning-after pills for emergency contraception\u8212\'20\'14found demand for morning-after medications jumped following the Dobbs decision and after states began putting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  initiatives to voters, according to co-founders Jamie Norwood and Cynthia Plotch.\par \par \uc2 Under a Trump presidency, Winx would lobby at the state level, Plotch said, including on issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  and access to medically accurate sex education.\par \par \uc2 The shifting legal landscape on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and in vitro fertilization is spurring entrepreneurs to consider innovations in both fields, said Maneesha Ghiya, managing partner of FemHealth Ventures.\par \par \uc2 Entrepreneurs, for example, are considering tools to help physicians determine whether a pregnant woman's life is at risk. This would be particularly beneficial in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prohibited except for situations such as when the mother's life is in danger.\par \par \uc2 Others are pursuing prenatal genetic testing technology to identify diseases earlier in a pregnancy so that women retain the option to terminate a pregnancy, even if \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is restricted to a certain number of weeks.\par \par \uc2 In February, the \uc2 Alabama Supreme Court\uc2  ruled that frozen embryos produced during in vitro fertilization were legally children, prompting IVF providers to pause services in that state. Alabama passed a law in March to shield clinicians from criminal and civil penalties for providing IVF services, but several states this year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/ivf-embryo-personhood-abortion-bills-rulings-7ed8b0f8?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced personhood bills}}}\uc2  that would deem frozen embryos to be children.\par \par \uc2 The bills, if passed into law, would force patients in those states to seek IVF services out of state. Entrepreneurs are looking at better technologies for storing embryos, Ghiya said.\par \par \uc2 FemHealth Ventures hasn't invested in any of these areas yet but will consider doing so regardless of the election outcome, she said.\par \par \uc2 Kindbody\uc2 , which has a national network of fertility clinics, is prepared in case states enact IVF restrictions, said founder and Executive Chair Gina Bartasi. The company can ship patient tissue from IVF-restricted states to others that don't restrict the procedure, she said.\par \par \uc2 There is also a scenario in which insurance coverage for IVF could widen, she said. Some states, including California, have passed laws expanding insurance coverage for IVF, and Trump has proposed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-proposal-to-cover-ivf-costs-faces-skepticism-0063d5cb?mod=article_inline&mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mandating insurance coverage}}}\uc2  for the treatment.\par \par \uc2 The Dobbs decision precipitated increased investor and entrepreneurial interest in \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and startups have found ways to be creative and innovate in the face of strong regulatory headwinds, said \uc2 Deena Shakir\uc2 , a general partner with \uc2 Lux Capital\uc2 . Startups will continue to advance technology in this field even if new regulatory hurdles emerge, she said.\par \par \uc2 "I expect the opportunity to invest will remain interesting," Shakir said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Brian Gormley at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:brian.gormley@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brian.gormley@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020241104ekb2001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
