\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 How the Antiabortion Movement Became a Cause Without a Candidate; The groups rode high when Roe was overturned. Now, they're splintered on strategy and facing state-level defeats after Trump and the GOP pulled back support, wary of election liability.\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 2,528 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 November 2024\par 01:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A couple of hours after \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/donald-trump-gives-mixed-signals-on-florida-abortion-referendum-2782c55c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggested in August that he would vote for a Florida ballot measure}}}\uc2  to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, a handful of irate antiabortion leaders got on the phone with one of his top advisers, determined to pressure the former president to walk it back.\par \par \uc2 In a tense call, \uc2 Kristan Hawkins\uc2 , president of Students for Life Action, laid down her group's position to the adviser: "This is a line you cannot cross."\par \par \uc2 She said if Trump voted in favor of such a measure, he would lose social conservative voters in the presidential election. "At that point there would be no difference between him and Kamala," Hawkins said, referring to the Democratic nominee, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As the call grew heated, Hawkins texted the adviser and said, "I apologize that you have five women yelling at you at the same time."\par \par \uc2 The next day, the campaign said Trump, a Florida resident, would in fact oppose the measure.\par \par \uc2 The victory was limited. Deep fractures have grown between Trump and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents, who just two years ago were on top of the world after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court overruled Roe v. Wade}}}\uc2  and eliminated a constitutional right to the procedure. The ruling was the culmination of the movement's unlikely relationship with Trump. The onetime \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporter appointed three conservative justices who helped overturn Roe and was the first sitting president to attend the annual March for Life.\par \par \uc2 That relationship is now in tatters, and the movement to end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in America finds itself struggling not to be written off as a political liability by Trump and the Republican Party, which are facing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/young-men-abortion-rights-movement-19c643ec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public backlash to the rollback of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2 . Antiabortion groups also have lost seven consecutive ballot referendums and appear on track to lose most of the 10 measures to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights that are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on state ballots}}}\uc2  in this election, including in conservative states such as Florida and Missouri.\par \par \uc2 "We've certainly seen some victories in recent years when it comes to our shared mission of abolishing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , making it unavailable and unthinkable. But we've also endured more defeats, and I fear there will be more to come this November and beyond," Hawkins said in a recent speech to Catholic business leaders in Cincinnati, urging discouraged supporters to keep fighting.\par \par \uc2 Trump publicly blamed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-rights-supporters-rack-up-victories-putting-gop-in-bind-for-2024-4bec7b38"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 costing the GOP critical votes in the November 2022 midterms}}}\uc2 , months after the Supreme Court decision. Democrats retained control of the Senate and performed better than expected in House races. He said Republicans poorly handled the issue in the midterms, and on social media in 2023 he disparaged advocates' ability to succeed on their agenda. "Pro lifers had absolutely zero status on the subject of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until I came along," Trump wrote. "Before our victory, they had nothing, and they will have nothing again if we don't win ELECTIONS."\par \par \uc2 This year, in an August social-media post, he said his administration "will be great for women and their \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 It was one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/former-first-lady-melania-trump-declares-her-support-for-abortion-access-43ceef07"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a series of indignities}}}\uc2  that have left \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents frustrated and scrambling to avoid losing much of the ground they gained. They're also split on whether to tell their supporters to drop Trump. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw426\pich640\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6390\pichgoal9600
