\par\par \uc2 Best of the Web Today\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The Tiresome Obamas; From Martha's Vineyard with scorn.\b0\par\par\uc2 By James Freeman \par \uc2 1,291 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 October 2024\par 21:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Whatever happens on Nov. 5, one silver lining of the end of election season is that Americans will likely soon enjoy at least a brief respite from self-righteous, inaccurate and arrogant lectures from the Obama family. Recently former President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  jetted into Pennsylvania {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/opinion/obamas-ugly-closing-argument-ce75cd5c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to insult voters}}}\uc2  who aren't supporting Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . On Saturday it was former First Lady \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 's turn. In Kalamazoo, Mich., she exhibited the charming family habit of treating people who don't share their politics as either ignorant or morally compromised.\par \par \uc2 As is now Democratic custom, Mrs. Obama didn't spend much time trying to make the case that Ms. Harris has earned a promotion. What can one say? Instead the former first lady offered an angry harangue against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as if he's the incumbent presiding over an era of inflation and disorder. Mrs. Obama echoed her husband's bizarre gripe from last week that as president Mr. Trump didn't look to Mr. Obama for guidance on dealing with pandemics. To her credit Mrs. Obama seems to have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/opinion/has-harris-given-up-on-harris-7ca55ea1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 learned from her husband's mistake}}}\uc2  and so she avoided presenting Canada's liberty-crushing lockdowns as some sort of model of Covid-era excellence.\par \par \uc2 Much of the speech was devoted to forecasting a dark future now that voters rather than unelected judges are allowed to decide some social policies. As with any issue where the Obamas have staked out a position, no well-informed and sincere objections are tolerated. Even on the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where millions of Americans have a deep conviction that it's wrong, such people are simply cast as unaware of the implications of their beliefs or callous opponents of women in the Obamaverse of progressive discourse.\par \par \uc2 Mrs. Obama's Saturday rant included the claim that if elected again, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  "could take actions that effectively ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide." She said this even though by now she must know that Mr. Trump has repeatedly expressed his opposition to a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and has said that the voters in each state should set their own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.\par \par \uc2 The absurd premise of Mrs. Obama's remarks was that in post-Roe v. Wade America, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is no longer dictated by the federal courts but instead left to up to the people, basic health care for women will essentially collapse as women are no longer able to find gynecologists.\par \par \uc2 Much of the speech was presented as a lecture to the men in the audience, who were treated as insensitive beasts who don't care enough or haven't considered the needs of the women in their lives, and also deserve no say in the policies affecting them. Said Mrs. Obama in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/28/opinion/michelle-obama-abortion-trump-election.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speech excerpt published}}}\uc2  in the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/26/us/politics/harris-michelle-obama-michigan.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described by Times headline writers}}}\uc2  as a "searing appeal to men":\par \par \uc2 I am asking you, from the core of my being, to take our lives seriously. Please do not put our lives in the hands of politicians, mostly men, who have no clue or do not care about what we as women are going through, who don't fully grasp the broad-reaching health implications that their misguided policies will have on our health outcomes.\par \par \uc2 The only people who have standing to make these decisions are women with the advice of their doctors. We are the ones with the knowledge and experience to know what we need.\par \par \uc2 So please, please do not hand our fates over to the likes of Trump, who knows nothing about us, who has shown a deep contempt for us. Because a vote for him is a vote against us, against our health, against our worth.\par \par \uc2 To say that voting for a particular candidate in a tight election means the voter has chosen to vote against half the population appears to be an effective way to create political polarization, but why would any party want to celebrate such rhetoric? Here's the closing in the Times excerpt, in which Mrs. Obama once again shames men who dare to deviate from her opinion on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Let me tell you all to think that the men that we love could be either unaware or indifferent to our plight is simply heartbreaking. It is a sad statement about our value as women in this world. It is both a setback in our quest for equity and a huge blow to our country's standing as a world leader on issues of women's health and gender equity.\par \par \uc2 So fellas, before you cast your vote, ask yourselves: What side of history do you want to be on?\par \par \uc2 Lest one think that Mrs. Obama only has contempt for men who disagree with her, she's even less respectful toward women who don't share her views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Perhaps because her entire argument would fall apart if she acknowledged their existence, she ignores them. But the truth is that there's never been a huge gender gap when it comes to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Most Americans think that it should be legal but with restrictions, while a small minority favor a total ban. Gender has less to do with their views than personal beliefs.\par \par \uc2 For example, the \uc2 Pew Research Center{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/fact-sheet/public-opinion-on-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 finds that ideology and political affiliation}}}\uc2  are much more predictive of someone's position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  than gender, where the differences are modest. Overall, \uc2 Pew\uc2  reports that 64% of women think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in most or all cases and so do 61% of men. Meanwhile 33% of women think it should be illegal in most or all cases and 38% of men share this view.\par \par \uc2 Interestingly though, while very few Americans favor a total ban\u8212\'20\'14in which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is illegal in all cases\u8212\'20\'14this position tends to be slightly more popular among women than men. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2024/05/13/broad-public-support-for-legal-abortion-persists-2-years-after-dobbs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pew reports that}}}\uc2  9% of women favor a total ban, compared with just 6% of men who think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should always be illegal.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/245618/abortion-trends-gender.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gallup finds}}}\uc2  that 12% of women favor a total ban, a slightly higher percentage than the 11% of men who want the practice to be illegal in all cases.\par \par \uc2 Obviously one doesn't expect fair and balanced coverage of issues in a partisan political speech, but the small minority of women who favor an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and the even smaller minority of men who do provide a kind of political reality check. Even if Mrs. Obama is inclined to attack those who don't share her views, she really doesn't need to direct such vitriol at people who have no realistic chance of seeing their policy wishes enacted nationwide. And she shouldn't be scaring men and women with outrageous claims about the U.S. health care system.\par \par \uc2 Gallup does find a bit of a gender gap in that more women than men favor no restrictions, while more men than women want \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be legal but with at least some restrictions, but the Obama stemwinder wasn't about nuance or understanding differences.\par \par \uc2 The good news is that in just another week or so, there's a decent chance Americans will be permitted to enjoy at least a modest vacation from such nasty rhetoric.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Bye-ku (Please) for an Epithet\par \par \uc2 Fasces (noun), "bundles,"\par \par \uc2 As of rods, coalitions,\par \par \uc2 And Dem donations.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Anonymous\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 James Freeman is the co-author of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1982163984"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 "The Cost: Trump, China and American Revival"}}}\uc2  and also the co-author of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/Borrowed-Time-Centuries-Booms-Bailouts/dp/0062669877/ref=asc_df_0062669877/?tag=hyprod-20&linkCode=df0&hvadid=312143020546&hvpos=&hvnetw=g&hvrand=10412016619786864649&hvpone=&hvptwo=&hvqmt=&hvdev=c&hvdvcmdl=&hvlocint=&hvlocphy=9003741&hvtargid=pla-525185269824&psc=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 "Borrowed Time: Two Centuries of Booms, Busts and Bailouts at Citi."}}}\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Follow James Freeman{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FreemanWSJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  on X}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "