\par \par \uc2 Trump supporter Bill Lloyd of Chandler, Ariz., said he appreciates the former president's tough talk. PHOTO: Ash Ponders for WSJ\par \par \uc2 Trump has a history of making derogatory comments about women, insulting former House Speaker Rep. \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D., Calif.) and \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , along with media personalities such as Megyn Kelly and \uc2 Mika Brzezinski\uc2 . In 2023, a federal jury found him liable for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/donald-trump-found-liable-in-e-jean-carroll-civil-case-ordered-to-pay-5-million-for-sexual-abuse-and-defamation-25e175b9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sexually abusing and defaming}}}\uc2  advice columnist E. Jean Carroll in a Manhattan department store 30 years ago. He denied the charges.\par \par \uc2 Trump's selection of Ohio Sen. \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  as his running mate was also seen as a nod to young male supporters. Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/why-jd-vance-worries-about-childlessness-00bb96cb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has upset many women}}}\uc2  with comments about "childless cat ladies."\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign spokeswoman Karoline Leavitt said that Trump "is speaking directly to the concerns of women about the border, inflation, and foreign policy crises we face. If women want a president who is going to restore law and order and protect their families and bring down inflation, then President Trump is the only option on the ballot."\par \par \uc2 During the Fox town-hall event, which aired Wednesday, Trump\u8212\'20\'14who has sought to moderate his position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14said that some states have passed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws that are "too tough" but argued "those are going to be redone." He also claimed he was "the father of IVF," without explaining himself. And on child care costs, Trump said he was going to "readjust things so that it's fair to everybody," but didn't provide details.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters, Harris called Trump's comments on in vitro fertilization "bizarre" and repeated her call for Trump to take responsibility for appointing three of the justices who overturned Roe. "The reality is, his actions have been very harmful to women and families in America on this issue," she said.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What do you think explains the gender gap in support for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Trump recently told women that he would be their "protector." Ortega was unmoved. "I don't feel as though I need a protector as a president, I just want someone to make decisions in the best interest of America," she said.\par \par \uc2 Even as his support among female voters has lagged, Trump has claimed that insulting Harris would actually appeal to women. At a rally last week in Pennsylvania, Trump said one of his aides told him: "Please don't call her dumb. The women won't like it." But he disagreed.\par \par \uc2 "The women want to see our country come back," Trump said. "They don't care. The women are tougher than the men, right?"\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine_lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine_lucey@wsj.com}}}\uc2 , Aaron Zitner at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:aaron.zitner@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aaron.zitner@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Xavier Martinez at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:xavier.martinez@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 xavier.martinez@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020241016ekag000gq\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
