\par\par \uc2 Main Street\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's Pennsylvania Catholic Problem; Her San Francisco progressive persona isn't a good fit for Joe Biden's native state.\b0\par\par\uc2 By William McGurn \par \uc2 849 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 October 2024\par 21:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Less than four weeks from the election, Michigan's Democratic governor made an in-kind contribution to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's campaign. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  appeared last week in a video featuring her placing a Dorito chip on the tongue of a kneeling social-media influencer. After Michigan's bishops denounced the clip as "specifically imitating the posture and gestures of Catholics receiving the Holy Eucharist," Ms. Whitmer apologized.\par \par \uc2 The kicker: She was wearing a Harris-Walz campaign hat in the video.\par \par \uc2 The swing-state governor says she had no idea people might find the post offensive, which speaks to how out of touch Democratic elites are. That cluelessness may prove costly in an election in which \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are separated by less than half a point in the RealClearPolitics polling average for the seven battleground states. In the most important of these\u8212\'20\'14Pennsylvania\u8212\'20\'14the latest RCP average shows Mr. Trump leads 48.3% to 47.9%. Ms. Harris's problem is that exit polls from 2020 show 30% of the state's voters are Catholic.\par \par \uc2 It isn't gaffes alone that could hurt the vice president in the Keystone Stone. "Throughout her career as a public official, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has long used government power to try to coerce people of faith to violate their consciences, especially regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gender ideology," says \uc2 Kristen Waggoner\uc2 , CEO of \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , which protects religious liberty.\par \par \uc2 As California's attorney general, Ms. Harris signed several friend-of-the-court briefs opposing religious exemptions for private employers such as \uc2 Hobby Lobby\uc2  and religious nonprofits such as the Little Sisters of the Poor. She said she was "proud" to have co-sponsored California's Reproductive FACT Act, which compelled pro-life pregnancy centers to display notices about where women could get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Supreme Court in 2018 rejected the law as a likely violation of the First Amendment.\par \par \uc2 But perhaps Ms. Harris's most notorious Catholic moment came after she was elected senator. When Brian Buescher was nominated for a federal judgeship, she grilled him about his membership in \uc2 the Knights of Columbus\uc2 , a Catholic men's fraternal organization. Although President John F. Kennedy was also a Knight, Ms. Harris treated the group as though it were the \uc2 Ku Klux Klan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She would later co-sponsor the Equality Act, which the U.S. Conference of Catholic bishops said could force doctors and hospitals to perform abortions they oppose. Last month she snubbed New York's Cardinal \uc2 Timothy Dolan\uc2  by declining to attend this Thursday's Al Smith dinner, an election-year staple that has brought Democratic and Republican candidates together in a civil setting for decades.\par \par \uc2 Though Joe Biden also found himself crosswise with the Catholic Church on issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and same-sex marriage, his Scranton, Pa., roots and familiarity with the culture meant he could overcome that. In 2020 Pew found he won the national Catholic vote, 50% to 49%, which Hillary Clinton lost in 2016. This helped him flip Pennsylvania and win the election.\par \par \uc2 Today the landscape looks more like 2016 than 2020. A Pew survey finds Ms. Harris trailing Mr. Trump among Catholics nationwide by 5 points, 47% to 52%. That puts Ms. Harris in Mrs. Clinton's territory.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden may be the last of the big-time Democrats whose base was the white working class. But it confers a sensibility Ms. Harris is conspicuously lacking. It's worth recalling that when the Obama administration was debating the Affordable Care Act's contraceptive mandate, news reports noted he pushed internally for a broader religious exemption.\par \par \uc2 His argument was that by backing a plan that forced Catholic institutions to provide contraceptives and other services they morally objected to, Mr. Obama would jeopardize his re-election prospects by alienating working-class Catholics in swing states such as Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Obama ignored him and won anyway. But Mr. Biden's argument looks more compelling today, and the press is cottoning on. Politico reports that Ms. Harris's prospects are "considerably dicier" because of a "cultural dissonance" between her progressive San Francisco persona and white working-class Catholic Pennsylvanians.\par \par \uc2 CatholicVote, a group that promotes Catholic values in public life, is highlighting this dissonance. In addition to the usual ads, mailings and social-media posts, this Thursday it is hosting a conversation with \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2  Mr. Kennedy is no one's idea of a staunch Catholic\u8212\'20\'14but on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , for example, he departs from Democratic orthodoxy by talking about help for pregnant woman who want to keep their babies as much as those who want an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Mr. Kennedy is offering skeptical Democrats social permission to follow his example by leaving the Democratic Party and voting Republican," says CatholicVote president Brian Burch. "Many Catholics in Pennsylvania are Democrats by tradition who might have voted for Joe Biden but have grown increasingly skeptical about their party under \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Write to mcgurn@wsj.com.\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020241014ekae004h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
