\par \par \uc2 Sen. Ted Cruz spoke to supporters at a campaign event in Allen, Texas, last week. PHOTO: Desiree Rios for WSJ\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/senate/2024/texas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Recent polls}}}\uc2  from Marist College and the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 /Siena College found Cruz leading Allred among likely voters by 5 points and 4 points, respectively. Both surveys showed former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  leading Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in the presidential race in the state by 7 points. Democrats hope to put Texas in play because the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/2024-presidential-senate-and-house-election-forecasts-5c4b54b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 map of other contested races}}}\uc2  this cycle has them in serious jeopardy of losing control of the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Austin, Texas-based Republican strategist \uc2 Matt Mackowiak\uc2  has been raising alarms about the race being unacceptably close. He said Cruz is consistently running behind Trump, who won Texas by less than six points in 2020. If this year's margin is two or three points tighter, Cruz could lose, Mackowiak said.\par \par \uc2 Still, Mackowiak doubts that will happen. He said appealing to crossover voters is a challenge for Allred. "Who are these voters who are Trump-Allred voters?" he asked. "What does that person even look like?"\par \par \uc2 A changing state?\par \par \uc2 Allred, who ranked in the top half of House members for bipartisanship and flipped a Republican district in 2018, has built a political career on moderate pragmatism. He has tangled with President Biden on border issues and refrained from linking himself much to Harris. Still, Cruz has portrayed his opponent as a far-left extremist.\par \par \uc2 The matchup comes six years after former Rep. \uc2 Beto O'Rourke\uc2  came within three points of beating Cruz, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/beto-orourke-draws-big-crowds-in-texas-but-his-voters-tend-not-to-vote-1538731801"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drawing national fascination}}}\uc2  and indicating Texas is potentially competitive. Fervor surrounding O'Rourke thrilled Democrats as he rallied supporters in all 254 Texas counties, livestreamed his every move and appeared on the cover of Vanity Fair. (O'Rourke's race for governor in 2022 was less suspenseful: He lost it by 11 percentage points.)\par \par \uc2 Allred has been running what might be considered the opposite of an O'Rourke campaign. He has focused on television advertisements over rallies, has been less prominent in the media and made many of his in-person events small gatherings centered on professional or industry groups. The soft-spoken former professional football player elicits little excitement and mostly talks about his reputation as a centrist. At times, some fellow Democrats have questioned whether he is trying hard enough. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
