\par \par \uc2 Supporters of Ted Cruz gathered last week at a Tex-Mex restaurant in the suburbs north of Dallas. PHOTO: Desiree Rios for WSJ\par \par \uc2 Naomi Dees, a former teacher and now full-time home-schooler to her 13-year-old, said she supports Cruz because she is conservative on most issues and particularly concerned about the U.S.-Mexico border and the "woke agenda."\par \par \uc2 First race since \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Allred's campaign has heavily pushed messaging about the loss of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in Texas, after the overturn of Roe v. Wade and passage of one of the nation's strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Cruz celebrated both the Supreme Court decision and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-new-texas-abortion-ban-law-takes-effect-providers-rush-to-adjust-11630521388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the state law}}}\uc2 , having previously said he opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceptions for rape or incest. On the campaign trail, he has generally refused to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying only that it is a matter for the state legislature and governor.\par \par \uc2 "It's what the press is obsessed with," he said to reporters last week.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Do you think Sen. Ted Cruz will be re-elected to the Senate? Why or why not? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Several North Texas voters, however, called the issue top of mind. In Plano, Sarah Young, a 29-year-old photographer and Navy veteran, called herself disillusioned with both political parties. The only thing motivating her to vote at all this year is her anger over the loss of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. "I have little sisters, and I don't want them in any harm," she said.\par \par \uc2 Leslie Newson, a 54-year-old undecided voter, drove an hour to see Cruz speak Tuesday. Her two top concerns are the economy and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and Newson, who works in health insurance, wanted to hear what he would say about the latter. She is distressed about the state's ban, which is so strict that she works with doctors who are afraid even to provide care for miscarriages, she said.\par \par \uc2 Newson left disappointed, not only by Cruz's silence on the subject, but also by the tone of his jokes, she said, citing a crack about Harris boarding a broomstick. The event made her less likely to vote for Cruz, she said.\par \par \uc2 But she and her husband still signed his bus\u8212\'20\'14just for fun. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
