\par \par \uc2 A small number of doctors and women already use Mifeprex without official signoff to treat miscarriages. PHOTO: Angela Owens/The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 The drugmaker responsible for bringing the{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone-f78f3320"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversial \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill}}}\uc2  to the U.S. is now pursuing a new use that could widen women's access: treating miscarriages.\par \par \uc2 Danco Laboratories is preparing scientific data and taking other steps to ask the Food and Drug Administration to approve use of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill regimen Mifeprex for management of miscarriages, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 A small number of doctors and women already use Mifeprex, or its generic equivalent mifepristone, without official signoff to treat miscarriages.\par \par \uc2 Such use has become enmeshed in fights over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Supporters say doctors are avoiding prescribing the drug to women facing dangerous complications so as not to run afoul of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-pill-parties-shipping-148e3c15"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 red-state \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions}}}\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents say {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  limits}}}\uc2  aren't meant to impede miscarriage care. They have also said Mifeprex is unnecessary for treating miscarriages and have highlighted the drug's risks.\par \par \uc2 An application for official \uc2 FDA\uc2  dispensation will heighten the controversy around the drug, while placing the agency's consideration under a political microscope.\par \par \uc2 It couldn't be determined when Danco will formally submit its application, though an \uc2 FDA\uc2  decision will likely take months.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  first approved Mifeprex for terminating a pregnancy in 2000. As part of the approval, the agency initially limited its use to the first seven weeks of gestation and required that certified doctors, not pharmacies, dispense it.\par \par \uc2 The agency has since{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fda-allows-women-to-get-abortion-pill-by-mail-11639698022?&mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eased the restrictions}}}\uc2 . Today it can be used for up to roughly 10 weeks of gestation, and it is dispensed by certified prescribers in person, mail-order pharmacies or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/cvs-walgreens-to-sell-abortion-pill-mifepristone-within-weeks-8d36f801"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bricks-and-mortar pharmacies}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/abortion-pill-increase-roe-wade-68472ff8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mifepristone is used}}}\uc2  in nearly two-thirds of abortions. The drug is given as part of a two-pill regimen. Doctors give mifepristone, commonly known as the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, which breaks down the uterine lining and softens the cervix. That is followed by misoprostol, which empties the uterus.\par \par \uc2 Most miscarriages occur in the first trimester, and doctors often offer women the choice of medication, surgery or waiting for their bodies to expel tissue naturally.\par \par \uc2 Doctors in the U.S. currently most often use only misoprostol\u8212\'20\'14a widely available generic drug\u8212\'20\'14when seeking to treat miscarriages with medication. In 2018, the \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2  said doctors should consider adding mifepristone, but few do, given the restrictions on the drug.\par \par \uc2 Randomized, controlled trials have shown that adding mifepristone helps miscarrying women completely pass pregnancy tissue without having to undergo follow-up surgeries.\par \par \uc2 A study of 300 miscarrying women, published in 2018 in the New England Journal of Medicine, found that 9% of those who received mifepristone as well as misoprostol required a follow-up surgical procedure, compared with roughly 24% in the group that received misoprostol alone.\par \par \uc2 A 2020 study of 700 women, published in the Lancet medical journal, had similar findings.\par \par \uc2 A study, published Tuesday in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jamanetworkopen/fullarticle/2824550#:~:text=Combination%20treatment%20with%20mifepristone%20plus%20misoprostol%20has%20been%20shown%20in,misoprostol%20alone%20for%20EPL%20management.&text=In%201%20randomized%20clinical%20trial,from%2076%25%20to%2091%25"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the journal JAMA Network Open}}}\uc2 , that looked at insurance claims data for more than 30,000 miscarriages found that women who got mifepristone and misoprostol, compared with those who just received misoprostol, were less likely to need follow-up surgeries or visit the emergency room for their miscarriages.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive-rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates have long hoped for a miscarriage indication for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill. In 2022, \uc2 ACOG\uc2  and 48 other medical and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups asked the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to grant an approval. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  said Danco itself needed to apply.\par \par \uc2 A new approval may encourage more doctors to get certified to prescribe mifepristone, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists say. It could also lessen stigma around the drug, according to the activists, and help doctors who are confused by their state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions feel more confident in giving it to miscarrying women.\par \par \uc2 The application would also give the \uc2 FDA\uc2  the chance to revisit\u8212\'20\'14and perhaps loosen\u8212\'20\'14the existing restrictions around the drug regimen.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents have argued that mifepristone isn't necessary for managing miscarriages, because both misoprostol and surgical treatments are available.\par \par \uc2 "This is a desperate attempt by the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobby to try to justify a product designed to end life," said Kristi Hamrick, spokeswoman for Students for Life Action, an antiabortion group.\par \par \uc2 The timing of the application means that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  most likely will decide the fate of the miscarriage indication under the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-claims-women-will-no-longer-be-thinking-about-abortion-if-he-wins-efcf6c7c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new presidential administration}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After the filing, the agency has 60 days to decide whether to accept the application for consideration or ask Danco to add information and refile it. If it decides to accept the application, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  then typically gives itself a deadline of six or 10 months to decide.\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 FDA\uc2  professional staff review the data and make a recommendation on approval or disapproval, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  commissioner, appointed by the president and confirmed by the Senate, has the power to overrule them.\par \par \uc2 Write to Liz Essley Whyte at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:liz.whyte@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liz.whyte@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020241008eka80035x\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
