\par\par \uc2 Review & Outlook (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Distortion Campaign; As Republicans move to the middle, Democrats falsely claim their opponents favor a national ban or no exceptions for rape or incest.\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Editorial Board \par \uc2 790 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2024\par 21:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a political winner for Democrats since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade in 2022, but could its political power be waning? We ask because that might explain why Democrats are making claims about their opponents' \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views that are flat-out false.\par \par \uc2 Knowing their vulnerability on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , most Republicans are moving toward the middle on the issue. But as they've done so, Democrats are making ever-more dishonest claims about what Republicans supposedly believe.\par \par \uc2 A major offender is \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , who in the recent vice-presidential debate said that Republicans support "a registry of pregnancies." This followed Mr. Walz's claim last month that "[Donald] Trump is trying to create this new government entity that will monitor all pregnancies to enforce their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans."\par \par \uc2 The Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee is running variations of this Handmaid's Tale fiction, with ads accusing House Republican candidates of wanting to "allow state governments to track pregnant women to prosecute them if they get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The alleged source for this claim is \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 's Project 2025 policy paper, which hasn't been adopted by the GOP as a party and Mr. Trump has disavowed many times. But even Project 2025 doesn't propose such a registry. Its hardly radical idea is for the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  to expand its collection of anonymous state statistics about abortions and miscarriages.\par \par \uc2 The idea is to better understand the scope and complications of certain procedures. There is no call for personal or pregnancy information at a federal or a state level. And by the way, the pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  collects data on the incidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and related issues without controversy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  distortion playbook has spread far and wide in Democratic campaigns. In California's 22nd House district, GOP Rep. David Valadao has said he opposes a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceptions for rape, incest and the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 Yet challenger Rudy Salas is running an ad implying that Mr. Valadao supports no exception for rape. "Washington Republicans want to criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even when a woman has been raped or is facing a medical emergency," the ad says, ending with "David Valadao, what if that was your daughter, or your sister?" The answer is that Mr. Valadao supports her right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In New York's 17th district, Democrat \uc2 Mondaire Jones\uc2  is running an ad with a banner that says Rep. Mike Lawler "would ban abortions in New York." Mr. Jones says in the ad that the Republican platform "would ban abortions even here in New York."\par \par \uc2 Except that the GOP platform doesn't include a ban and Mr. Lawler doesn't support one. While Mr. Lawler personally opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with exceptions for rape, etc., he has said he does "respect the will of the state's voters whom the Supreme Court have given exclusive jurisdiction over the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue." Albany Democrats are as likely to pass an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restriction as Iran is to approve same-sex marriage.\par \par \uc2 Even moderate Maryland Senate contender \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , who wants to codify Roe in a statute, is being attacked as anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Democrat Angela Alsobrooks claims Mr. Hogan would use a Senate seat to help Republicans "pass a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban."\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania Sen. Bob Casey is pulling the same dishonest trick, saying GOP challenger \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2  wants "to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even in cases of rape or incest." That's false. Mr. McCormick's position is that "any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law should make exceptions for rape, incest, and when the life of the mother is in danger." Montana's Democratic Sen. \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2  is giving the same "no exceptions" treatment to Tim Sheehy, despite the Republican's clear statements to the contrary.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Politics isn't pickleball, and distortions occur on both sides. But Democrats aren't even attempting to be honest about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year. Perhaps they're lying so extravagantly because \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a rare issue on which they have a clear political advantage. Republicans are left having to decide whether to spend scarce campaign dollars debunking the distortions or risk letting some voters believe them because they're unrebutted.\par \par \uc2 The distortions can also harm more than other politicians. They can frighten some women into thinking they can't risk getting urgent medical care if they have a pregnancy emergency. This from the party that claims to be the protector of women's health. The next time you see an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ad from a Democrat, assume it's not telling the truth.\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020241007eka7005bp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
