\par\par \uc2 Commentary (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The Truth About Amber Thurman's Death; Harris and Walz exploit a tragedy to further a political narrative about 'Trump  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bans.'\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nicholas Tomaino \par \uc2 905 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2024\par 20:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  dodged a question about Minnesota's permissive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statute at last week's debate by repeating a story about Georgia's restrictive one. He brought up the case of Amber Thurman, 28, of Atlanta, who "had to travel a long distance to North Carolina to try and get her care" because Georgia prohibits \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks. "Amber Thurman died in that journey back and forth," Mr. Walz said.\par \par \uc2 His source was an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 article}}}\uc2  by Kavitha Surana of \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 . Ms. Surana reports that in August 2022, nine weeks pregnant with twins, Thurman made an appointment at a North Carolina clinic for a dilation-and-curettage procedure, or D&C, a surgical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She drove there, arrived late, and was given mifepristone and misoprostol instead. After taking the first pill, she "insisted on driving home before any symptoms started."\par \par \uc2 Days later, after vomiting and passing out at home, Thurman was taken to a suburban Atlanta hospital, where she reported a tender abdomen. Doctors noted a foul odor during a pelvic exam, and an ultrasound showed possible tissue in her uterus. Thurman needed a D&C, but according to Ms. Surana, the state had "criminalized" that procedure, "with few exceptions," and practitioners who performed it risked "up to a decade in prison." Physicians operated some 20 hours after her admission, after diagnosing her with acute severe sepsis. She died.\par \par \uc2 In the 56th paragraph of the story, Ms. Surana acknowledges: "It is not clear from the records available why doctors waited to provide a D&C to Thurman." Mr. Walz obviously didn't read that far, and the article's title is meant to give the opposite impression: "\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Bans Have Delayed Emergency Medical Care. In Georgia, Experts Say This Mother's Death Was Preventable."\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has also cited the Thurman case to support her claim that "the Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban" means "doctors have to wait until the patient is at death's door before they take action." Both the Harris-Walz account and Ms. Surana's gloss over several complications:\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. Thurman's death affirms what antiabortion activists have argued: that the two-pill \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimen is far more dangerous than its advocates claim. \uc2 The Food and Drug Administration\uc2  in 2016 allowed nonphysicians to prescribe mifepristone, stopped requiring follow-up visits to evaluate patients for potential complications, and permitted use up to 10 weeks' gestation from seven. Five years later, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  eliminated the requirement that women be evaluated in person by any medical professional.\par \par \uc2 Christina Francis, CEO of the American Association of Pro-Life OBGYNs, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-medical-basis-of-the-mifepristone-ruling-supreme-court-abortion-health-risks-7ef3df6b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 written}}}\uc2  in these pages that the new protocols lead to far greater risk in the event of ectopic pregnancy, whose symptoms are similar to the normal effect of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. According to the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/020687s020lbl.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 label}}}\uc2 , after taking the regimen, between 2.9% and 4.6% of women visit the emergency room for an adverse reaction.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Georgia's statute. The law, which Gov. Brian Kemp signed in 2019 and a state judge in Atlanta enjoined last week, defines \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an act intended to "cause the death of an unborn child" when a "detectable human heartbeat" is present. Thurman's unborn children were, it seems, already dead. Even if they hadn't been, however, the law allows for immediate treatment "when a physician determines, in reasonable medical judgment, that a medical emergency exists" or that the "pregnancy is medically futile."\par \par \uc2 Contrary to Ms. Harris's claim, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lozierinstitute.org/fact-sheet-are-pro-life-state-laws-preventing-pregnant-women-from-receiving-emergency-care/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  statute in the country}}}\uc2  requires doctors to "wait until the patient is at death's door" to intervene. Several states with restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws\u8212\'20\'14including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/sbaprolife/status/1840064131807821857?s=46"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AHCA_FL/status/1836827821521412226"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/mccormackjohn/status/1805933161529892978?s=46"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14have taken formal actions to counter this misinformation. Other states with similar laws ought to communicate directly with hospitals and doctors to do the same.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 The hospital. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.medicare.gov/care-compare/details/hospital/110191/view-all?city=Atlanta&state=GA&zipcode="}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Medicare's rating}}}\uc2  of Piedmont Henry Hospital in Stockbridge, where Thurman died, gives it two out of five stars and reports that only 41% of patients with severe sepsis or septic shock "received appropriate care." (The national average is 61%.) Patient reviews report lower-than-average satisfaction with the hospital's cleanliness, responsiveness and communication. The hospital might have been underresourced: As Ms. Surana notes, "a D&C requires an anesthesiologist, nurses, attending physicians and others"\u8212\'20\'14a host of staff that might have been more readily available elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 Such tragedies also occur in states with permissive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. In Nevada, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal until 24 weeks, Alyona Dixon, 24, died on Sept. 28, 2022, owing to "{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.8newsnow.com/news/local-news/las-vegas-hospital-sued-after-woman-dies-from-septic-abortion-in-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complications from septic \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 ," six days after a \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  clinic reportedly gave her the same pills Thurman took. Dixon's widower has filed a wrongful-death lawsuit against the hospital where she was initially treated and discharged. The complaint cites a physician's expert declaration that the hospital "failed to adequately rule out sepsis as a cause of Ms. Dixon's symptoms."\par \par \uc2 Each of these details complicates the Harris-Walz narrative that Donald Trump is ultimately to blame for Amber Thurman's death. That may be a politically convenient claim, but it grossly ignores the facts, stokes needless fear among vulnerable women and medical professionals alike, and exploits a young woman who tragically died.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tomaino is an assistant editorial features editor at the Journal.\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020241006eka600231\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
