\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Former First Lady Melania Trump Declares Her Support for  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Access; Her husband, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has bragged about ending federal protections for the procedure\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joseph De Avila \par \uc2 565 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2024\par 20:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former first lady Melania Trump signaled her support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, a topic that has vexed her husband's presidential campaign, in a video promoting her upcoming memoir.\par \par \uc2 "Individual freedom is a fundamental principle that I safeguard," she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/melaniatrump/status/1841806743216537870?s=46&t=mc2vHozZJYYzru9DdSGqTQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in the video}}}\uc2  posted on social media Thursday. "Without a doubt, there is no room for compromise when it comes to this essential right that all women possess from birth. Individual freedom: What does 'my body, my choice' really mean?"\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has become a complicated issue for her husband, former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Trump has bragged about his role in ending federal protections for the procedure, though he has repeatedly shifted his stance on how exactly he would regulate it. Access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shown to be a powerful motivator for voters and could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-poll-trump-swing-state-voters-2024-election-3e12f57c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 play a major role}}}\uc2  in the suburban areas that may decide this year's presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump's support for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more explicit in her memoir, according to an excerpt published by British news organization the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 "Restricting a woman's right to choose whether to terminate an unwanted pregnancy is the same as denying her control over her own body," Trump wrote in her memoir, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/02/melania-trump-memoir-defends-abortion-rights?CMP=Share_iOSApp_Other"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Guardian}}}\uc2 , which obtained a copy of the book.\par \par \uc2 Skyhorse Publishing\uc2 , publisher of the memoir, didn't respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign deferred comment to the former first lady's office. Her office didn't respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, Trump's running mate, acknowledged during Tuesday's vice presidential debate that the GOP has often been out of step with voters on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Republicans "have to do a better job of winning back people's trust" by improving access to child care and fertility treatments, he said.\par \par \uc2 Former President Trump has bragged about helping to end Roe v. Wade by appointing three of the Supreme Court justices who overturned it in 2022. He said on social media during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/vance-walz-vice-presidential-debate-election-2024/card/trump-commits-to-vetoing-national-abortion-ban-u9gIefKceH3sBSKrry4V"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vice presidential debate}}}\uc2  that he would veto a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, after declining to commit to such a veto during last month's presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has made protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights a central pillar of her campaign.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign didn't immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-harris-poll-august-election-2024-e6fa024e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal poll}}}\uc2  taken in late August found Harris ahead of Trump in a head-to-head matchup among women voters by 13 percentage points. Asked whether there was an issue they felt so strongly about that they wouldn't vote for a candidate they disagreed with on it, 33% of women in the poll identified \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14the highest figure for any issue.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-claims-women-will-no-longer-be-thinking-about-abortion-if-he-wins-efcf6c7c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Last month, Trump said}}}\uc2 , "You will no longer be thinking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 " because the issue has now been returned to the states to decide.\par \par \uc2 Trump, a Florida resident, said in September that the state's current ban on the procedure after six weeks of pregnancy was too restrictive and suggested he would support a ballot initiative allowing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until fetal viability, or about halfway through a typical pregnancy. One day later, he said he would vote no.\par \par \uc2 Write to Joseph De Avila at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:joseph.deavila@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joseph.deavila@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020241003eka30050l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
