\par\par \uc2 Wonder Land\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 More Vance-Walz, Please; The vice-presidential nominees shocked the nation by being civil and reasonable.\b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Henninger \par \uc2 929 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2024\par 21:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Yes, we need to have a second debate\u8212\'20\'14between JD Vance and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . Demonstrably, a stage where the two vice-presidential candidates are debating is the only venue where one is likely to encounter anything of substance in the 2024 presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 Recall the two earlier debates. In the first, President Biden opened by self-destructing, and by evening's end he and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  were arguing over their golf skills.\par \par \uc2 Before the Trump-Harris debate, it was reported that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  would try to goad Mr. Trump into intemperance. True to promise, the vice president began by backing up a garbage truck of insults and unloading them on the former president, who\u8212\'20\'14as this column has noted\u8212\'20\'14elevated the art of political insult in the 2015 Republican primaries and has sustained it. This week, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2024/10/01/us-news/donald-trump-calls-tim-walz-a-total-moron-but-predicts-debate-will-be-stacked-against-jd-vance/?utm_campaign=nypost&utm_medium=referral"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  Mr. Walz "a moron."\par \par \uc2 Vance-Walz may not have been the Lincoln-Douglas debates, but it likely reassured many voters there are still people in American politics willing to speak seriously in public about important matters. But make no mistake: However impressive, this debate won't decide the election. The top of the ticket, however flawed, is the set-in-stone choice.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, heads of these imperfect tickets\u8212\'20\'14Mr. Trump and Ms. Harris\u8212\'20\'14loomed like the sword of Damocles over what I thought were the debate's two most interesting moments, which is to say the issues that neither Mr. Walz nor Mr. Vance would talk about\u8212\'20\'14respectively, whether there should be any restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Mr. Trump's denial that he lost the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 In opinion polls, Ms. Harris holds a double-digit lead over Mr. Trump on which candidate would best handle the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue. Given that this complex subject has been reduced to four words\u8212\'20\'14the "right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 "\u8212\'20\'14not much is likely to change before the election. Some suburban women will base their vote for Ms. Harris on this issue alone.\par \par \uc2 Despite that, it has become impossible not to notice that senior Democrats simply won't talk about restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump pressed Ms. Harris on the question of third-trimester abortions, however rare, and she deflected it. In Tuesday evening's debate, Mr. Vance asked Mr. Walz the same question, and \uc2 CBS\uc2  moderator Nora O'Donnell twice asked the governor to address the matter of restrictions. Three times he declined to discuss it.\par \par \uc2 Ms. O'Donnell (the second time): "Governor, would you like to respond and also answer the question about restrictions?"\par \par \uc2 Mr. Walz: "Yeah. Well, the question got asked, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made the accusation that wasn't true about Minnesota. Well, let me tell you about this idea that there's diverse states. There's a young woman named Amber Thurman . . ."\par \par \uc2 I'm going to go out on a limb here and try to read Mr. Walz's mind on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Elsewhere in the debate, during a discussion on the housing shortage, Mr. Walz, who is a Lutheran, said, "And when I think of a house, I'm thinking of Christmas services after midnight Mass, where you go with your family."\par \par \uc2 What a delightful image. It's hard to imagine that a man who carries that memory would in the privacy of his own thoughts favor no-restriction \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that's notwithstanding that as Minnesota's governor he presided over passage of one of the nation's least restrictive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mprnews.org/story/2024/10/01/fact-check-minnesota-claims-in-walz-vance-vp-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  laws}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14no 24-hour wait period, no parental notification for minors.\par \par \uc2 One may say that Mr. Walz ought to have the courage of his moral convictions and be willing to express some minimal degree of qualification. But politics couldn't care less about your personal convictions. Unrestricted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the Democrats' dogma, and none of them in public will divert from that absolutist position. Why not is a good and troubling question.\par \par \uc2 Sen. Vance tried to open the door to a conversation on the subject, admitting Republicans have "to do so much better of a job at earning the American people's trust back on this issue where they frankly just don't trust us." He went on to suggest creating more economic and personal options for women with unplanned pregnancies\u8212\'20\'14"pro-family in the fullest sense of the word."\par \par \uc2 The Democrats' valorization of terminating pregnancies is off-putting, and Mr. Vance's better-options comments offered Republicans a way to talk about the subject. Mr. Trump should take it, but if he won't, down-ticket GOP candidates should.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Vance's denial moment arrived with the inevitable question about Mr. Trump's assertions that he won the 2020 election. It is an immovable Trump obsession but also a reason some swing-state voters remain undecided.\par \par \uc2 Another limb: JD Vance knows Mr. Trump narrowly lost that election, and in a better world he would have said that Tuesday night. But if he had, his irrepressible running mate would have cracked back, driving a wedge between the two that would have been publicized daily by Harris-Walz and the media until Nov. 5. This isn't party dogma, however, and most down-ticket GOP candidates should feel free to admit the 2020 election train is long gone.\par \par \uc2 The silver lining here is that both Messrs. Vance and Walz, polar opposites, somehow concluded that, above all, they should come across as reasonable. If only for two hours in our age of unreason, it was progress.\par \par \uc2 Write henninger@wsj.com.\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020241002eka2005xx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
