\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Vance Seeks to Temper Trump's Policies, Walz Casts Former President as Dangerous; With \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at odds over another presidential debate, the matchup between the running mates took on more intrigue\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey and Alex Leary \par \uc2 1,484 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2024\par 11:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 JD Vance sought to temper \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's more controversial rhetoric on issues like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , immigration and guns during a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/five-vp-debate-moments-that-mattered-most-22cf244d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vice-presidential debate}}}\uc2  Tuesday night, as an occasionally tense \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  offered a defense of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's record and argued that Trump poses a danger to democracy.\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail, the Republican senator from Ohio has developed a reputation as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/jd-vance-trump-campaign-loyalty-e9ec0f58"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 partisan attack dog}}}\uc2 . But throughout the debate, he gave a more polished performance, playing down {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-immigration-plans-deportation-e91b1bc4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump's plans for mass deportations}}}\uc2  and saying the GOP needs to earn back the trust of Americans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , tacitly acknowledging a massive gender gap Trump suffers. And he reminded viewers of his modest roots and that he was raised by "two lifelong blue-collar Democrats."\par \par \uc2 "We've got to do so much better of a job at earning the American people's trust back on this issue, where they frankly just don't trust us," said Vance, 40, who was a passionate antiabortion voice as a Senate candidate and at times has supported a national ban after the earliest weeks of pregnancy. He called for the party to be "pro-family in the fullest sense of the word."\par \par \uc2 Walz, 60, the Democratic governor of Minnesota, stressed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-kamala-harris-election-2024-92511caa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris's support for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 , her middle-class-focused economic policies and argued Trump was a threat to democracy. But he was put on the defensive over the validity of his past statements and flubbed several lines, such as when he said, "I've become friends with school shooters." He was referring to relationships he has formed with the parents of victims of the 2012 Sandy Hook Elementary School shooting in Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 Near the end of the debate, Walz aggressively pushed Vance over Trump's repeated denial of the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 "To deny what happened on January 6, the first time in American history that a president or anyone tried to overturn a fair election and the peaceful transfer of power. And here we are, four years later, in the same boat," Walz said.\par \par \uc2 Walz then challenged Vance: "Did he lose the 2020 election?"\par \par \uc2 "Tim, I'm focused on the future," Vance replied, using a line advisers have long hoped Trump would adopt. Walz shot back: "It's a damning non-answer."\par \par \uc2 Several times Vance attempted to counter Democrats' warnings. "They make a lot of claims about if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  becomes president, all of these terrible consequences are going to ensue," Vance said.\par \par \uc2 The debate between the running mates was a proxy fight for the White House, playing out as the Biden administration sought to contain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/israeli-response-to-irans-attack-to-set-course-of-widening-war-0c8b5158"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 widening conflict in the Middle East}}}\uc2  and Americans in southern states grappled with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/climate-environment/hurricane-helene-north-carolina-crisis-search-and-rescue-9518ef43"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fallout from a massive hurricane}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hosted by \uc2 CBS\uc2  in New York City, the showdown carried an extra level of intrigue as the last scheduled debate before Election Day. It came as Harris and Trump are in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-harris-poll-august-election-2024-e6fa024e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deadlocked race for the presidency}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The tone of the event was sharp at times, but in a departure from earlier debates this year it was generally substantive and policy-focused. During Trump's June debate with President Biden, the two men argued over who would get the upper hand in a match of golf, and during the Harris-Trump debate, the vice president sought to provoke her rival over his felony convictions, while the former president mused about migrants eating cats and dogs.\par \par \uc2 Biden's debate performance was so disastrous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/biden-drops-out-presidential-race-6b1c74fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he dropped out of the race}}}\uc2  not long after it, and Harris was widely seen as the winner of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-and-harris-meet-for-high-stakes-presidential-debate-ae8719e7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her matchup with Trump}}}\uc2 . The vice-presidential matchup was far less dramatic but offered both a chance to explain their party's vision for governing.\par \par \uc2 Instant polls of viewers who watched the debate suggested it made little mark on the shape of the race. Surveys of debate watchers from CNN and \uc2 CBS\uc2 /\uc2 YouGov\uc2  showed Vance and Walz essentially tied on who won the event. Only 1% of respondents in the CNN poll said the debate changed their mind about who to vote for, while 8% of Harris backers said they were reconsidering their choice and 14% of Trump supporters said so.\par \par \uc2 On \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Walz offered specific stories of women who have dealt with harrowing health conditions due to restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. He also argued that Republicans would make it harder to get contraception and fertility treatments, noting that fertility treatments are "why I have a child."\par \par \uc2 Vance repeated Trump's position that the issue should be left to the states. Trump himself weighed in on social media during the debate, explicitly saying for the first time that he would veto a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, should Congress pass legislation. Democrats have repeatedly argued that Republicans would seek a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Asked about school shootings, Vance said "we do have to do better" and called for boosting security at schools. Walz emphasized that he is a hunter and a gun owner, but argued there were laws that could curb shootings without taking guns away.\par \par \uc2 Early in the debate, the two men were asked about Hurricane Helene, which had claimed more than 100 lives, and Iran's attack on Israel amid Israel's ongoing war with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . Both men said Israel had the right to defend itself but each used a question to accuse the other's campaign of weakness.\par \par \uc2 Walz cast the Biden administration as steady while noting a "nearly 80-year-old" Trump used some of his debate with Harris to talk about the size of crowds at his events. "\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is fickle," Walz said, as the candidates debated tumult in the Middle East. "He will go to whoever has the most flattery or where it makes sense to him."\par \par \uc2 Vance countered that Trump served in a time of relative global stability and said adversaries were "afraid of stepping out of line."\par \par \uc2 On Hurricane Helene, which hit communities across six states including the presidential battlegrounds of North Carolina and Georgia, Vance called it an "unspeakable human tragedy." Asked how a Trump administration would tackle climate change, he argued in favor of bringing manufacturing to the U.S., but didn't offer other policy prescriptions. Walz noted that Trump has called climate change a "hoax," and he stressed efforts under Biden and Harris to invest in solar energy and green jobs.\par \par \uc2 Vance and Walz repeatedly referred back to the top of the ticket. Vance sought to make the case that Harris is currently in the White House and has shared in policymaking with Biden.\par \par \uc2 Asked about his earlier criticism of Trump, Vance said he has been open in acknowledging that he "was wrong about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Walz was put on the defensive over his personal biography, including claiming he was in Hong Kong during the violent crackdown on protesters in Tiananmen Square in June 1989. Minnesota Public Radio and APM Reports have reported that he inaccurately claimed to be in Hong Kong for a teaching position at that time. Walz sidestepped that question, instead providing a lengthy response about why he went to China for teaching opportunities. Pressed again during the debate, Walz said he "misspoke."\par \par \uc2 "I've not been perfect and I'm a knucklehead at times," Walz said, trying to soften that and other biographical inaccuracies\u8212\'20\'14including his military history\u8212\'20\'14with an attempt at a folksy line.\par \par \uc2 Asked about Trump's plans for a massive deportation effort, Vance blamed the Biden administration for rolling back some tougher border policies. He said criminal migrants would be targeted first for deportation but stopped short of outlining a larger effort. He dodged a question about separating families, even if children are U.S. citizens.\par \par \uc2 Walz accused Trump of blocking a bipartisan immigration agreement that was before Congress earlier this year but ran into opposition from conservatives and Trump.\par \par \uc2 Moderator Margaret Brennan noted that migrants in Springfield, Ohio, were in the country legally\u8212\'20\'14despite the impression Trump and Vance have left. Trump said during last month's debate with Harris that migrants there {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/springfield-ohio-pet-eating-claims-haitian-migrants-04598d48"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were "eating" cats and dogs}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The rules were that you guys weren't going to fact-check," Vance interjected. As he attempted to make another point, the moderators cut off his microphone.\par \par \uc2 The debate was expected to draw tens of millions of viewers and was the last scheduled opportunity for Americans to hear from both parties at the same time, as Harris and Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/donald-trump-says-he-wont-do-another-debate-with-kamala-harris-c7d8e428"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have disagreed over terms for a second debate}}}\uc2 . After the vice-presidential debate, Trump repeated that he wouldn't debate Harris again.\par \par \uc2 Ken Thomas contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Alex Leary at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:alex.leary@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alex.leary@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020241001eka10060p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
