\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Republican \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 's Campaign Formula Includes Rejecting a Trump Endorsement; Maryland's popular former governor just got an $18 million boost in the deep blue state but still has an uphill battle\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kristina Peterson and Anthony DeBarros \par \uc2 1,336 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2024\par 18:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GAITHERSBURG, Md.\u8212\'20\'14Fifteen minutes into her speech, Democratic nominee Angela Alsobrooks acknowledged the strange reality of her Senate race in deep blue Maryland: Her Republican opponent, former Gov. \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , is popular.\par \par \uc2 Just don't vote for him, she implored voters at a suburban community center.\par \par \uc2 "We worked together and so I can tell you that as a person, I like \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 ," said Alsobrooks, the Prince George's County executive. "But that is not the question we are answering in this election," she said. "The question is who should have the 51st vote" and control of the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Hogan's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/anti-trump-republican-larry-hogan-runs-for-senate-in-maryland-79e337f1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 run as a centrist Republican}}}\uc2  who regularly criticizes former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14even rejecting his endorsement\u8212\'20\'14has made Maryland the nation's most unusual Senate race, forcing many Democrats to make hard political calculations. The former two-term governor's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/the-face-of-the-anti-trump-gop-is-now-larry-hogan-ce071535"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision to enter the contest}}}\uc2  in February created a surprise opportunity for the GOP, which is hoping that a coalition of Republicans and suburban swing voters can propel him to an upset win.\par \par \uc2 "We have an awful lot of ticket splitters," Hogan said in an interview. "Every day, people come up to me and say, 'I'm voting for [Democrat Kamala] Harris and I'm voting for you, because we think you're exactly what we need in Washington.'"\par \par \uc2 Democrats' message boils down to reminding voters that Hogan is still a Republican\u8212\'20\'14and that sending a Republican to Capitol Hill is different from electing one to run the state, with implications for national policy fights ranging from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to taxes. Democrats have a 51-49 majority in the Senate, and a GOP win in Maryland would almost guarantee Democrats lose control.\par \par \uc2 "I'd vote for him as governor, but not this Senate seat," said Gaithersburg resident Charles Glinka, 77 years old, a retired physicist and Democrat.\par \par \uc2 Maryland hasn't had a Republican in the Senate in nearly 40 years. But Hogan, 68, has defied the political laws of gravity before and continues to operate on what can seem like a different planet from the rest of the Republican Party. He is the highest-ranking Republican running for office to break with Trump, something many voters say resonates with them. Trump, who is eager for a GOP Senate majority if he recaptures the White House, publicly backed Hogan in June, but Hogan dismissed it.\par \par \uc2 "I rejected the endorsement, didn't request the endorsement," Hogan said. "I've been probably the leading voice of opposition to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the MAGA movement since the day he came down the escalator" in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/donald-trump-to-unveil-plans-for-2016-presidential-race-1434448982"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2015 to announce his presidential bid}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Addressing a packed room at Leisure World, a retirement community, Hogan said he had been the first Republican to oppose {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/project-2025-head-steps-down-89cba52b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025, a conservative road map}}}\uc2  for the next GOP administration. After fielding questions, he mingled with voters before driving an hour to his next appearance at a farm, stopping to switch into jeans and black boots.\par \par \uc2 Republicans typically have a hard time in Maryland. President Biden won the state by 33 points in 2020, and the 2024 Democratic nominee, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , is expected to cruise to victory. Polls show Hogan easily outperforming Trump in the state but still trailing Alsobrooks by eight points, according to the Real Clear Politics average. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
