\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Joe Manchin Won't Endorse \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  After Her Filibuster Comments; Vice president reiterates her support for eliminating the filibuster on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 -rights legislation\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joseph De Avila \par \uc2 508 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2024\par 20:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 West Virginia Sen. Joe Manchin said he won't endorse \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president, after she emphasized that she supported bypassing the Senate's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-filibuster-senate-explained-11656606298"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filibuster rule}}}\uc2  if needed to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 "She knows the filibuster is the holy grail of democracy," {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2024/09/24/politics/joe-manchin-not-endorse-harris-filibuster/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Manchin said in an interview with CNN}}}\uc2 . "It's the only thing that keeps us talking and working together. If she gets rid of that, then this would be the House on steroids."\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wpr.org/news/kamala-harris-presidential-campaign-vice-president-housing-affordability-pfas-pollution-wpr-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview with Wisconsin Public Radio}}}\uc2  that aired Tuesday, Harris reiterated her support for eliminating the filibuster on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights legislation. Such a move would enable a bill to pass with a simple majority, rather than the 60 votes currently required for most legislation.\par \par \uc2 "I think we should eliminate the filibuster for Roe," she said. "And get us to the point where 51 votes would be what we need to actually put back in law the protections for reproductive freedom and for the ability of every person and every woman to make decisions about their own body and not have their government tell them what to do."\par \par \uc2 President Biden in 2022 said he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-says-he-supports-exception-to-filibuster-to-codify-roe-v-wade-into-law-11656596123?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backed an exception}}}\uc2  to the filibuster to restore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access as a constitutional right, after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade. Harris, who as vice president would cast the tiebreaking vote in the Senate if needed, quickly followed him in saying she also supported that position. But the effort stalled, after Manchin and fellow centrist Sen. \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  (I., Ariz.) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/davos2023/card/kyrsten-sinema-defends-stance-on-filibuster-high-fives-joe-manchin-EBaZnIepJQLBX3nVqCi1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to support the move}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Senate has already discarded the 60-vote threshold for confirming judicial and executive branch nominees, but Manchin as well as many Republicans have argued for preserving the filibuster for legislation, saying it increases pressure on both sides to negotiate. Democrats have grown increasingly frustrated by Republicans' ability to block legislation on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , voting rights and other progressive priorities.\par \par \uc2 Manchin, a longtime centrist Democrat, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/sen-joe-manchin-leaves-democratic-party-69aa0984?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left the party}}}\uc2  in May to become an independent after years of disagreements with colleagues on issues like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/what-must-kamala-harris-do-to-win-over-moderates-joe-manchin-has-advice-f7444755"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 energy policy}}}\uc2  and partisanship. He is retiring after this term.\par \par \uc2 The filibuster promotes bipartisan cooperation and guards against partisan whiplash and dysfunction, Manchin said. He was backed up by Sinema. "To state the supremely obvious, eliminating the filibuster to codify Roe v. Wade also enables a future Congress to ban all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide," she said on social media.\par \par \uc2 Manchin, who continues to caucus with Democrats, had previously signaled he was open to endorsing Harris and was keeping an eye on her filibuster stance. But he said her latest comments meant that he would no longer consider backing her.\par \par \uc2 "That ain't going to happen," Manchin told CNN. "I think that basically can destroy our country."\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign didn't immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Catherine Lucey contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Joseph De Avila at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:joseph.deavila@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joseph.deavila@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240924ek9o003pd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
