\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Senate Control Hinges on the 'Last Democrat' in Montana; Voters are torn over whether \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2  is still advancing their interests\u8212\'20\'14or if he has become a creature of Washington\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lindsay Wise and Anthony DeBarros \par \uc2 1,943 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 September 2024\par 04:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GREAT FALLS, Mont.\u8212\'20\'14Voters here in one of the most sparsely populated states are wrestling with a question that could determine the direction of the entire country next year: Is Sen. \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2  still the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/sen-jon-tester-walks-blue-line-in-solid-red-montana-11623067915"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 same down-home dirt farmer}}}\uc2  they elected three times or has he become a Washington liberal who rubber stamps Democrats' agenda?\par \par \uc2 The stakes are high in Big Sky Country.\par \par \uc2 Tester, known for his signature flat-top haircut and three missing fingers\u8212\'20\'14he lost them in a meat grinder when he was 9 years old\u8212\'20\'14is the most vulnerable senator up for re-election. If he goes down in this red-leaning state, so does the Democrats' Senate majority. They currently have a 51-49 margin but are sure to lose a seat in deeper-red West Virginia, where Sen. Joe Manchin is retiring.\par \par \uc2 A loss by Tester would give Republicans a stronger hand in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/social-security-tax-trump-election-2024-9f911216"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rewriting the tax code}}}\uc2  for millions of American households and businesses in 2025. The party that controls the Senate confirms Supreme Court appointments and can approve\u8212\'20\'14or block\u8212\'20\'14cabinet picks. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip