\par\par \uc2 World News\par \uc2 World\par \b \uc2 Pope Francis Says U.S. Voters Must Choose 'Lesser Evil' in Presidential Election; \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  both endorse policies that mean they are 'against life,' pontiff says\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ginger Adams Otis \par \uc2 545 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 September 2024\par 01:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Pope Francis says U.S. voters will have to choose "the lesser evil" in the coming presidential election, criticizing both candidates for policies he said were "against life."\par \par \uc2 The 87-year-old pontiff didn't mention former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  by name in his comments released Friday. He urged Americans to vote even if faced with a difficult choice.\par \par \uc2 "Both are against life: the one that throws out migrants and the one that kills children," said Francis. "I can't decide; I'm not American."\par \par \uc2 He spoke to reporters during his return journey to Rome following a multicountry visit through Asia. Popes generally don't endorse political candidates.\par \par \uc2 "\u8203\'20\'0B\u8203\'20\'0BOne must vote. And one must choose the lesser evil," Francis said. "Which is the lesser evil? That lady or that gentleman? I don't know; each person must think and decide according to their own conscience."\par \par \uc2 The Harris and Trump campaigns didn't respond to a request for comment Friday. The two candidates have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/harris-vs-trump-policies-election-0c0e6032#reproductive-rights-e39bf1be"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 staked out distinct positions}}}\uc2  on immigration and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/trump-election-deport-immigrants-f21a943a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has}}}\uc2  said he would conduct a migrant-deportation campaign if he wins in November. Harris has said she supports allocating more money for immigration enforcement, but also supports legal migration to the U.S. and providing a citizenship pathway for longtime immigrants in the country illegally.\par \par \uc2 Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/harris-trump-presidential-debate-election-2024/card/harris-delivers-a-strong-punch-on-abortion-rights-02n3irYiXHiJjdihta36"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been vocal}}}\uc2  on the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying she supports codifying into national law the protections found in Roe v. Wade, the 1973 Supreme Court decision that protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Trump appointed three \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  justices who helped overturn Roe v. Wade in 2022, eliminating federal constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He has said the issue should now be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 settled state-by-state}}}\uc2 . The former president has said he wouldn't sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if it were to come across his desk.\par \par \uc2 The pope has been outspoken in the past about his sympathy for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/europe/pope-faces-down-growing-backlash-against-migrants-in-europe-390ad042"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plight of migrants}}}\uc2 , and clear that he upholds church doctrine that opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Both topics were front and center {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/five-debate-moments-that-mattered-most-58a1c307"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 during Tuesday night's presidential debate}}}\uc2  and remain hot-button campaign issues.\par \par \uc2 Failing to care for migrants and denying them the right to work is a "grave sin," Francis said.\par \par \uc2 "Sending migrants away, not allowing them to grow, not letting them have life is something wrong. It is cruelty," he said.\par \par \uc2 He spoke in the same frank terms about his view of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which he said the Roman Catholic Church forbids because it ends a life.\par \par \uc2 "The Church is not closed-minded because it forbids \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; the Church forbids \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because it kills," the pope said.\par \par \uc2 The pope also shared his concerns over the war in Gaza, saying it is horrible to know children have been killed and schools are being bombed.\par \par \uc2 "It's sometimes said that this is a defensive war, but sometimes I believe that it's a war\u8230\'20\'26too much, too much," he said. "I apologize for saying this, but I don't see steps being taken toward peace."\par \par \uc2 Write to Ginger Adams Otis at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Ginger.AdamsOtis@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ginger.AdamsOtis@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240913ek9d006hd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
