\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Five Debate Moments That Mattered Most; \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  appeared to get under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's skin in their first meeting\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey \par \uc2 1,078 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 September 2024\par 04:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  repeatedly went on offense in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-and-harris-meet-for-high-stakes-presidential-debate-ae8719e7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a fiery debate}}}\uc2  against former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Tuesday, as the two clashed on the economy, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , foreign policy and the size of their rally crowds.\par \par \uc2 "You're not running against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , you're running against me," Harris declared at one point, encapsulating how drastically the contest had shifted following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/biden-drops-out-presidential-race-6b1c74fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 President Biden's exit}}}\uc2  after his disastrous June debate performance.\par \par \uc2 Here are five key moments from the first 2024 presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 A historic introduction\par \par \uc2 Trump and Harris\u8212\'20\'14in their first formal meeting ever\u8212\'20\'14shook hands at the start of their face-off, a formality Trump and President Biden skipped in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/bidens-disastrous-night-stands-to-alter-course-of-the-election-fc69a58d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their June debate}}}\uc2 . Harris, dressed in a dark suit, walked over to Trump's side of the stage and introduced herself by saying, "\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The meeting showcased a stark height difference between the vice president and the Republican nominee, who sported a red tie. He is 6 feet, 3 inches tall, and she is 5 feet, 4 inches tall.\par \par \uc2 The two quickly launched {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/harris-used-debate-to-define-herselfand-trump-d9fb4cd7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 into a sharp exchange}}}\uc2  on the economy, as Harris declared herself a champion of the middle class, and Trump touted his plans for tariffs. He blasted her for overseeing a period of sharp inflation that has eased, but left many Americans still reeling.\par \par \uc2 Trump insisted he had presided over a strong economy before the Covid pandemic. "She's a Marxist," he claimed. "Everybody knows she's a Marxist. Her father's a Marxist professor in economics."\par \par \uc2 As Trump spoke, Harris kept staring at him and shaking her head. She said Trump would only provide tax cuts for billionaires and corporations. "\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has no plan for you," Harris said at one point.\par \par \uc2 Trump struggles on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Put in the hot seat on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Trump said the issue was best left to the states, but wouldn't say whether he would veto a national ban on the procedure as president. "I won't have to," Trump claimed, suggesting it would never get enough support to get through Congress.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a top issue for many voters following the 2022 Supreme Court decision to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturn Roe v. Wade}}}\uc2 . Last month, Trump suggested he would support a ballot measure that would roll back a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gov-ron-desantis-signs-florida-six-week-abortion-ban-b18029cc?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban in Florida}}}\uc2 , but then walked that statement back amid criticism from antiabortion activists.\par \par \uc2 Harris said the Supreme Court decision has triggered bans in numerous states, speaking about women who couldn't receive care for miscarriages or after being raped. "\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  certainly should not be telling a woman what to do with her body," she said.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who has boasted about appointing three of the Supreme Court justices that overturned Roe, has offered a more nuanced position recently as he tries to neutralize an issue that has been one of Republicans' biggest political liabilities over the past two years. He also said Harris would allow abortions after birth, which is false.\par \par \uc2 Personal attacks\par \par \uc2 "I'm talking now if you don't mind," Trump shot at Harris about halfway through the debate. "That sound familiar?"\par \par \uc2 Trump was mimicking a comment Harris made to his former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  during their 2020 debate. The remark underscored how personal the candidates got with their attacks in the empty studio in Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 Moments before, Harris listed Trump's legal issues at length, calling him: "someone who has been prosecuted for national security crimes, economic crimes, election interference, has been found liable for sexual assault and his next big court appearance is in November, at his own criminal sentencing."\par \par \uc2 The comment drew an emotional response from Trump, who said the prosecutions have been politically motivated. "I probably took a bullet to the head because of the things they say about me," Trump said, referencing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-taken-off-stage-after-apparent-shots-fired-at-rally-9d6680da?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the assassination attempt}}}\uc2  at a Pennsylvania rally in July.\par \par \uc2 At another point, clearly looking to get under Trump's skin, Harris declared of Trump's rallies: "People start leaving his rallies early out of exhaustion and boredom."\par \par \uc2 Trump, who has long prided himself on his large, exuberant rallies, responded testily that people don't attend Harris's rallies. "People don't leave my rallies," he said. "The biggest rallies, the most incredible rallies in the history of politics."\par \par \uc2 Asked if he would acknowledge that he lost the 2020 election, Trump refused. "No, I don't acknowledge that at all," he said. Harris declared that Trump was "fired by 81 million people, so let's be clear about that, and clearly has had a very difficult time processing that."\par \par \uc2 Trump also didn't directly answer a question about whether he had any regrets about his actions on Jan. 6, 2021, when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-protesters-are-in-the-building-inside-the-capitol-stormed-by-a-pro-trump-mob-11609984654"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a mob of his supporters stormed the U.S. Capitol}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Clash on Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Pressed on whether he thinks it is in the best interest of the U.S. for Ukraine to win its war against Russia, Trump refused to answer. "I want the war to stop," he said.\par \par \uc2 Trump has often touted his relationship with Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 . He claimed he could speak to Putin and Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelensky\uc2  and resolve the conflict, but didn't offer any details on how that would work.\par \par \uc2 Harris shot back: "If \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  were president, Putin would be sitting in Kyiv right now." She praised the work the U.S. has done with \uc2 NATO\uc2  allies to support Ukraine and said to Trump, "You adore strongmen instead of caring about democracy."\par \par \uc2 'Eating the cats'\par \par \uc2 Trump falsely claimed that migrants are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/the-origins-of-trumps-claim-that-immigrants-are-eating-pets-a6a82218"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eating a large number of pets}}}\uc2  in Springfield, Ohio. "In Springfield, they are eating the dogs," Trump said, repeating an internet conspiracy involving Haitian immigrants that has been debunked by major news organizations. "They're eating the cats."\par \par \uc2 Local police have said there is no evidence to substantiate those claims, which have been amplified by conservative media. Host David Muir told Trump the reports were untrue. The rumors started with a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post, citing the poster's "neighbor's daughter's friend," according to the police.\par \par \uc2 Harris shook her head and laughed as Trump continued to talk about the falsehood, which was also repeated this week by his vice presidential running mate, Sen. \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  of Ohio. "They're eating the pets of the people that live there," Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240911ek9b000ul\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
