\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights Are on the Ballot in Arizona. Will It Affect the Presidential Race? A proposed constitutional amendment has added another layer to the election in a battleground state\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jimmy Vielkind and Ariel Zambelich | Photographs by Caitlin O'Hara for WSJ \par \uc2 679 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 September 2024\par 01:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 This essay is the first installment in a series accompanying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/chasing-the-vote-the-battlegrounds-dfa2e502"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 "Chasing the Vote,"}}}\uc2  a limited-run podcast in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://on.wsj.com/3o375VH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Wall Street Journal's What's News feed}}}\uc2  . The multipart audio program seeks to understand, examine and present to listeners the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/harris-vs-trump-policies-election-0c0e6032"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issues and dynamics}}}\uc2  driving voters in several swing states.\par \par \uc2 There is little from the outside to indicate that Camelback Family Planning is Arizona's busiest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic. It is just another office in another strip mall, with the occasional antiabortion protester outside.\par \par \uc2 But \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/arizona-abortion-poll-election-2024-def7bb14"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are a hot topic in Arizona}}}\uc2 . In addition to the presidential contest between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , Arizonans will vote on a proposal to amend the state constitution to broadly guarantee \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. The ballot question is being pushed by the Arizona for \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access (AAA) campaign, which submitted more than 823,000 signatures\u8212\'20\'14twice what was needed.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  question is as powerful a reason to vote as the candidates, according to recent interviews The Wall Street Journal conducted for its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/podcasts/whats-news/chasing-the-vote-arizonas-abortion-battle/d09973b4-e85b-4c22-a1a6-784a079f36c5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 "Chasing the Vote" podcast series}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dr. Gabrielle Goodrick says the clinic she owns is like any other medical office, and she tries to keep it nonpolitical. But there is one room with walls and cupboards covered with thank-you notes. Many are from medical residents who have received training at Camelback. Some are from patients, who Goodrick says come from across the political spectrum. And on one wall, there is a voter registration placard with a QR code.\par \par \uc2 Now, Goodrick said, speaking up in the debate over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is part of her job.\par \par \uc2 Harris, on the campaign trail, has repeatedly asserted that Trump would seek a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Trump says he has no plans to sign one; but in leaving the issue to states, about 18 have enacted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bans or restrictive laws}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The AAA campaign spent months collecting signatures around the Grand Canyon State. On the other side of the issue, antiabortion activists held a "decline to sign" effort against the referendum that included more than 3,000 volunteers. Former Arizona state Sen. Nancy Barto was part of that push.\par \par \uc2 The AAA campaign is still meeting with voters, including at a table outside of the Brick Road Coffee shop in Tempe. Robin Williams, a retired \uc2 Costco\uc2  worker, handed out information as people went into the cafe.\par \par \uc2 Brick Road became something of a hub of the AAA campaign. After the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  overturned Roe v. Wade in 2022, volunteers have gone there to collect signatures for ballot referendums.\par \par \uc2 Surveys generally show a majority of Arizona voters favor \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Democrats frequently mention \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in campaign speeches and political ads.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion activists like Mayra Rodriguez are actively campaigning against the amendment but don't expect that many GOP candidates, including Trump, will pick the same mantle.\par \par \uc2 T.J. Shope is a Republican state senator who crossed party lines this year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/arizona-abortion-ban-repeal-f3f0a530"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to repeal an 1864 law}}}\uc2  that banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in almost every circumstance. He thinks having the amendment on the ballot will let people split their thinking on the issue from their choice in the presidential election. (Shope, 39, said he would vote against the amendment.)\par \par \uc2 In the food court of Scottsdale Fashion Square mall, Josh and Ephraim Lonsako said they were approaching the ballot in a different way this year. The brothers are devout Christians who oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and both said they would vote against the ballot measure. But Ephraim, 27, supported Trump in 2020, while Josh, 24, voted for Biden. Josh said in July that he was ready to vote for Biden again, and now is researching Harris.\par \par \uc2 Jenica Olah, 43, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum was a big motivator for her to vote for Harris.\par \par \uc2 Write 