\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Trump Says He Will Vote Against Florida  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Referendum; GOP nominee said he still opposed his adopted home state's six-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban but referendum on November's ballot was too permissive\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alex Leary in Washington and Vivian Salama in Johnstown, Pa. \par \uc2 809 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 August 2024\par 00:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sought to clarify his \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  position Friday, saying he would vote against a Florida ballot measure to roll back a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gov-ron-desantis-signs-florida-six-week-abortion-ban-b18029cc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  in his adopted home state, one day after criticizing that limit as harsh.\par \par \uc2 Trump in an interview before a rally here Friday maintained his opposition to the six-week ban but characterized the ballot measure as too permissive. "I'll be voting no for that reason," he told Fox News.\par \par \uc2 His {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/donald-trump-gives-mixed-signals-on-florida-abortion-referendum-2782c55c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unclear stance}}}\uc2  a day earlier angered antiabortion activists who saw him as lending support to the November ballot initiative, and was the latest example of Trump straining to find a middle ground on the\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/republicans-adopt-stripped-down-platform-that-reflects-trumps-abortion-views-14a5ba98"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contentious issue}}}\uc2 . The Florida measure would protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access through fetal viability, or about halfway through a typical pregnancy, effectively invalidating the six-week ban.\par \par \uc2 "We thank President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for announcing he will vote no on Amendment 4," said Marjorie Dannenfelser, head of the antiabortion group Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday she issued a statement saying Trump's initial comment about the six-week ban "completely undermines" his position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But she then issued another statement indicating she and Trump had spoken and noted, "He has not committed to how he will vote on Amendment 4." Trump's campaign also affirmed that Thursday night, before his clearer comments Friday.\par \par \uc2 Some antiabortion leaders argue that it may be difficult to motivate religious conservative voters who care deeply about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November unless Trump shows a firm commitment to the issue. At the same time, Trump has publicly talked about how the issue {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/these-republicans-are-pushing-for-abortion-rights-cadf5606"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has hurt Republicans}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump is locked in a tight race with Vice President{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-harris-poll-august-election-2024-e6fa024e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new Wall Street Journal poll}}}\uc2  shows her with a narrow lead. Trump had a 2-point advantage over Harris in the Journal's head-to-head test {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/harris-erases-trumps-lead-wsj-poll-finds-e286144d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in late July}}}\uc2 . The poll found that 64% of voters said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-kamala-harris-election-2024-92511caa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have rallied effectively}}}\uc2  around the issue since the Supreme Court in 2022 overturned Roe v. Wade, with a conservative majority bolstered by three justices Trump appointed in his first term.\par \par \uc2 Harris in a statement Friday argued that, by opposing the amendment, Trump would "vote to uphold an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban so extreme it applies before many women even know they are pregnant," adding she trusts women to make their own healthcare decisions. Trump had previously criticized Florida's new law as harsh.\par \par \uc2 In citing opposition to the Florida measure, Trump said Democrats were "radical," and wanted to legalize the procedure until the ninth month of a pregnancy. He falsely claimed some states allow a mother to "execute the baby after birth." Infanticide is illegal in every state. Major medical associations say abortions can only be performed during a pregnancy, not after it has ended.\par \par \uc2 Overwhelmingly, abortions occur during the first trimester of a pregnancy, according to the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 . In 2021\u8212\'20\'14before Roe was overturned\u8212\'20\'1493% of abortions took place at or before 13 weeks of gestation. An additional 6% occurred between 14 and 20 weeks of pregnancy while 1% were after that.\par \par \uc2 Trump has long had difficulty with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an issue. In the late 1990s, as he got more involved politically, he described himself as "strongly pro-choice," citing his background of growing up in New York. He gradually took a more Republican position.\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail now Trump brags about how he reshaped the Supreme Court but has said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws should be up to the states. He has refused to take a clear stand on the national level. Trump says he has no plans to sign a national ban, but 18 states have enacted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bans or restrictive laws}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an interview this week with the Daily Mail, Trump wouldn't commit to vetoing legislation containing a national ban. "I don't mind answering that question, but there's no reason to, because the states are all voting," he said. He also said recently on social media that he will be "great for women and their \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 In a step in that direction, Trump this week said he backs federal funding for in vitro fertilization or forcing insurers to pay for the costly procedure. That proposal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-proposal-to-cover-ivf-costs-faces-skepticism-0063d5cb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was met with concern}}}\uc2  from antiabortion groups that oppose the treatments and skepticism from advocates who have been working for such care for years.\par \par \uc2 Catherine Lucey contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Alex Leary at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:alex.leary@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alex.leary@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Vivian Salama at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:vivian.salama@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vivian.salama@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240830ek8u0070t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
