\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Trump Says  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Should Be Legal for 'More Than Six Weeks'; Campaign also unveils expansive proposal to support IVF in bid to allay voter fears of threats to fertility care\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Alex Leary \par \uc2 866 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 August 2024\par 15:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  suggested Thursday he would support a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/florida-activists-abortion-ballot-amendment-afa804c6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ballot measure}}}\uc2  that would roll back a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gov-ron-desantis-signs-florida-six-week-abortion-ban-b18029cc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban in Florida}}}\uc2 , but then his campaign scrambled to walk it back, his latest halting attempt to try to find a middle ground on the issue.\par \par \uc2 Seeking to blunt Democrats' advantage with women, the Republican presidential nominee also outlined an expansive proposal to provide federal funding for in vitro fertilization or force insurers to pay for the costly procedure.\par \par \uc2 Trump said a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Florida is too restrictive and doesn't give women enough time to access the procedure. A measure on the ballot in November in his adopted home state\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/these-republicans-are-pushing-for-abortion-rights-cadf5606"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would protect \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2  through fetal viability, or about halfway through a typical pregnancy, effectively invalidating the six-week ban.\par \par \uc2 "I am going to be voting that we need more than six weeks," Trump told NBC News. Later on Thursday a spokeswoman said Trump "has not yet said how he will vote on the ballot initiative in Florida."\par \par \uc2 Trump's comments stirred outrage and confusion among antiabortion activists, who form an important part of the Republican base. Many initially interpreted him as saying he plans to vote for the Florida ballot measure but later said he appeared to be uncommitted.\par \par \uc2 "What should the pro-life movement do when the \uc2 RNC\uc2  and the formerly pro-life presidential candidate abandons the pro-life position? Elections are about the FUTURE, not the past," said \uc2 Lila Rose\uc2 , president of Live Action, an antiabortion group.\par \par \uc2 Trump once boasted of his role in overturning Roe v. Wade\u8212\'20\'14having appointed three of the Supreme Court justices who voted to overturn the landmark decision\u8212\'20\'14but has expressed an increasingly nuanced view of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in an attempt to neutralize an issue that has been one of Republicans' biggest political liabilities over the past two years. He has said he believes the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue should now be decided at the state level.\par \par \uc2 "My Administration will be great for women and their \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Trump said in a recent post on Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 Trump has sought to blunt criticism of Republicans' support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in his campaign to return to the White House. Trump is locked in a tight race with Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-harris-poll-august-election-2024-e6fa024e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new Wall Street Journal poll}}}\uc2  shows her with a narrow lead. Trump had a 2-point advantage over Harris in the Journal's head-to-head test {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/harris-erases-trumps-lead-wsj-poll-finds-e286144d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in late July}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Campaigning in Georgia on Thursday, Harris repeated her assertion that Trump would seek a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Trump says he has no plans to sign one, but in leaving the issue to states about 18 have enacted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bans or restrictive laws.}}}\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for the Harris campaign said, "Because Trump overturned Roe v. Wade, IVF is already under attack and women's freedoms have been ripped away in states across the country."\par \par \uc2 Trump's running mate, Sen. \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  of Ohio, said on NBC's "Meet the Press" on Sunday that he could "absolutely commit" that Trump wouldn't seek a national ban. Asked whether Trump would veto such a ban, Vance said, "I think he would. He said that explicitly that he would."\par \par \uc2 Democrats have sought to paint a future Trump administration as a threat to IVF, which is broadly popular. The issue flared nationally after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/alabama-shields-ivf-providers-with-new-law-53d54d16"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an Alabama Supreme Court decision}}}\uc2  earlier this year that briefly led clinics in the state to stop providing care.\par \par \uc2 Trump also said at campaign events in Michigan and Wisconsin on Thursday that if he wins a second term his administration would provide federal financial support or mandate that insurance companies cover in vitro fertilization treatments.\par \par \uc2 Trump said he would let parents deduct major newborn expenses from their taxes, aiming to offset some of the costs associated with parenting and competing with a recent Democratic proposal. He didn't offer additional details and has now floated several tax breaks on top of a promise to extend his 2017 tax cuts.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Harris announced a different benefit aimed at new parents, offering a $6,000 refundable child tax credit for newborns, along with other expansions of the credit for older children. Vance floated a $5,000 child tax credit, but Trump hadn't expressed support for that and offered the deduction idea on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Tax credits are dollar-for-dollar reductions in tax bills, and refundable credits are paid to people even if they don't owe income taxes. Deductions, by contrast, shrink taxable income. They typically provide benefits only to people who owe income taxes, and the benefit increases for people in higher tax brackets.\par \par \uc2 In recent years, about 40% of households didn't have net federal income tax bills, though many of those are retirees, according to the \uc2 Tax Policy Center\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Richard Rubin\uc2  and Catherine Lucey contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Alex Leary at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:alex.leary@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alex.leary@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240830ek8u000gp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
