\par\par \uc2 Main Street\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Confessions of a Pro-Lifer; Today Democrats celebrate  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 , while Republicans run away from the issue.\b0\par\par\uc2 By William McGurn \par \uc2 867 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 August 2024\par 21:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 For anyone who can't forget that each \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  involves more than one life, joy isn't the right word to describe the Democratic convention. Out is "safe, legal and rare," replaced by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's full-throated celebration of what Democrats call "reproductive freedom." Oddly underscoring the party's commitment not to reproduce was a \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  van offering free vasectomies and abortions.\par \par \uc2 The Republicans are hardly more encouraging. There was a time when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  liked to call himself "the most pro-life president in American history." But on Friday he posted the following on his social-media site, Truth Social: "My administration will be great for women and their \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." This was followed by his running mate, JD Vance, promising NBC that Mr. Trump would veto any federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 It gets worse. In 10 weeks, voters in 10 states will decide whether to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a right in their state constitutions. In the two years since the Supreme Court's Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization overturned its 1973 decision in Roe v. Wade, voters in seven states\u8212\'20\'14red ones included\u8212\'20\'14have already come down on the pro-choice side on ballot measures.\par \par \uc2 What's a pro-lifer to do?\par \par \uc2 In the thick of a presidential election it's easy to forget that, for pro-lifers, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't merely one box on an issues checklist. It is a beachhead for an ethic that says that what the Declaration calls the unalienable right to life can disappear when that life is inconvenient to others. This has implications for everything from assisted suicide to in vitro fertilization.\par \par \uc2 In American politics today, this is a hard sell\u8212\'20\'14and those advancing the pro-life argument must expect to be unpopular. We are, after all, the new counterculture. Though our counterculture seeks to build and not tear down.\par \par \uc2 At times it can be tempting to think, "We are just a court ruling or an election away from getting what we want." It's at precisely these moments we must recognize that the only secure defense for the unborn is persuading our fellow Americans of the intrinsic dignity of their lives. This is especially true with advances in medical technology fast rendering any ban easier to get around. The \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  reckons that 63% of abortions now are medication abortions, which can be done at home.\par \par \uc2 Pro-lifers understand that what is most needed is a culture of life. Absent that, laws and Supreme Court rulings make for a brittle foundation. It is simply too much to expect an ordinary politician to parse the complexities of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14not least the real hardships the denial of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can bring\u8212\'20\'14and then, in the face of a hostile media looking to trip that politician up at every turn, deliver a public and compelling defense of the unborn. It is harder still when the pro-choice side holds the commanding heights of the culture, and even the pulpits are timid.\par \par \uc2 Neither Democrats, who spent their convention celebrating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , nor Republicans, who spent theirs running away from it, challenged the idea that the 60 million abortions since Roe raise no troubling questions. The public debate is dominated by gut-wrenching stories of women denied \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in truly horrific circumstances.\par \par \uc2 Far less reported on is a Charlotte Lozier Institute study last year of women who had abortions. Just 33% identified their abortions as "wanted and consistent with my values and preferences," 43% as "accepted but inconsistent with my values or preferences," 14% as "unwanted" and 10% as "coerced." Sixty percent of these women said they would have preferred to give birth if they had received either more emotional support or financial wherewithal.\par \par \uc2 The good news is that today yeoman's work is being done to ensure that the cold front door of a \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  clinic isn't these women's only choice. In New York and New Jersey, Chris Bell runs four Good Counsel homes helping women, mostly African-American, keep their babies\u8212\'20\'14and go back to school or whatever else a new mom might need to do to support herself and her baby.\par \par \uc2 Erica Pelman founded Shifra, a nationwide effort to help Jewish women with unplanned pregnancies by offering financial aid, professional counseling through the baby's first birthday and a lifetime of parenting support classes. And tiny Benedictine College in Kansas is planning to build a pro-life medical school.\par \par \uc2 All these groups and leaders have stared into a bleak political landscape before: when Roe was handed down; when a raft of Democrats such as Ted Kennedy\u8212\'20\'14who started out pro-life\u8212\'20\'14embraced \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; when Justice \uc2 Anthony Kennedy\uc2 's defection in Planned Parenthood v. Casey 1992) seemed to destroy hope in ever overturning Roe.\par \par \uc2 But, as the name implies, pro-lifers are in it for life. We don't oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because we can end it. We oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because it's the taking of a human life at its most innocent and vulnerable\u8212\'20\'14and we are compelled to try.\par \par \uc2 Write to mcgurn@wsj.com.\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240826ek8q0048t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
