\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Harris Accepts Democratic Presidential Nomination, Vowing to Unite Nation 'Around Our Highest Aspirations'; On the closing night of the DNC, the vice president spoke about why she's running\u8212\'20\'14without dwelling on the historic nature of her candidacy\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tarini Parti and Ken Thomas \par \uc2 1,594 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 August 2024\par 04:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CHICAGO\u8212\'20\'14{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  frequently recalls her mother telling her that she might be "the first to do many things" but to make sure she isn't the last. Yet as Harris formally accepted the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/dnc-harris-speech-election-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic presidential nomination}}}\uc2  Thursday, the vice president didn't directly invoke the historic nature of her candidacy.\par \par \uc2 Instead of leaning into what her campaign thinks is obvious, the 59-year-old former California senator and prosecutor tried to accomplish something she has struggled to do since her unsuccessful presidential bid in 2019: provide a clear picture to Americans of{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/dnc-kamala-harris-election-2024-4ddf9e83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what she stands for\u8212\'20\'14and why}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I will be a president who unites us around our highest aspirations," Harris said. "A president who leads\u8212\'20\'14and listens. Who is realistic, practical and has common sense. And always fights for the American people. From the courthouse to the White House, that has been my life's work."\par \par \uc2 Harris used the prime-time address to pitch Americans on her{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/kamala-harris-election-2024-fd6ca18b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 central campaign message}}}\uc2  since unexpectedly{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/biden-drops-out-presidential-race-6b1c74fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 replacing President Biden}}}\uc2  at the top of the Democratic ticket: She portrayed her opponent, former President{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  as a threat to freedom, arguing she has a more forward-looking agenda on protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and on expanding economic mobility for the middle class.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is an unserious man, but the consequences of putting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  back in the White House are extremely serious," Harris said during her speech. "Consider not only the chaos and calamity when he was in office, but also the gravity of what has happened since he lost the last election," she said, referring to the Jan. 6, 2021, riot at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Trump reacted in real time on his Truth Social platform, saying Harris and Biden had years to address some of the problems they outlined at the DNC. He accused the Democrats of failing on the border and violent crime\u8212\'20\'14and rebutted Harris's claim that Republicans would seek to further restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. "I TRUST WOMEN," Trump wrote in all caps. "She's done nothing for three and a half years but talk, and that's what she's doing tonight, she's complaining about everything but doing nothing!" Trump wrote.\par \par \uc2 Harris is the nation's first Black vice president. If she wins in November, as the first{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kamala-harris-to-make-history-as-first-female-u-s-vice-president-11604769441"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 woman or person of South Asian descent}}}\uc2  in the Oval Office, she will face steep challenges in unifying a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/men-women-vote-republican-democrat-election-7f5f726c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 divided electorate}}}\uc2  around her vision for the country.\par \par \uc2 The vice president sought to allay those concerns, saying the nation has a "precious, fleeting opportunity to move past the bitterness, cynicism and divisive battles of the past."\par \par \uc2 Harris also emphasized elements of her biography\u8212\'20\'14such as{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-kamala-harriss-family-of-fighters-influenced-her-campaign-message-11572429601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her upbringing}}}\uc2  by a middle-class, immigrant mother\u8212\'20\'14to portray herself as an authentic and relatable messenger for her priorities.\par \par \uc2 "Building that middle class will be a defining goal of my presidency," Harris said. "And I'll tell you, this is personal for me. The middle class is where I come from."\par \par \uc2 She offered a personal account of her family's unlikely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/campaign-lays-bare-debate-over-what-it-means-to-be-a-real-american-815bf205"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 path to America}}}\uc2  and her decision to become a prosecutor. Harris recalled the journey of her mother, Shyamala Harris, who traveled from India to California at age 19 "with an unshakable dream to be the scientist who would cure breast cancer."\par \par \uc2 In high school, Harris said she noticed her best friend, Wanda, was sad at school. When Wanda confided that she was being sexually abused by her stepfather, Harris told her friend that she had to come stay with her family, she recalled.\par \par \uc2 "This is one of the reasons I became a prosecutor," she said. "To protect people like Wanda, because I believe everyone has a right to safety, to dignity, and to justice."\par \par \uc2 With early voting beginning in some states in about a month and Election Day just over two months away, she has limited time to reintroduce herself as a leader in her own right. Biden stepped away from the race in July, the first president to abandon a re-election campaign since 1968, and endorsed Harris to succeed him.\par \par \uc2 Part of Harris's task going forward will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/kamala-harris-fundraising-donors-election-2024-724da4f6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to maintain the momentum}}}\uc2  of the first month of her candidacy while continuing to characterize Trump\u8212\'20\'14who is about two decades older than her\u8212\'20\'14as a relic of the past. Her team will also need to deny Trump the mantle of an outside change agent when Harris remains closely tied to Biden's policies and as surveys show that many Americans yearn for change.\par \par \uc2 David Axelrod, a top strategist for former President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 's campaigns, said Harris could make a compelling case.\par \par \uc2 "The fight right now is whether the Trump folks can push her back into the box of being an incumbent and hold her accountable for the things that Biden has done, or whether she can continue on this path as the choice to turn the page," Axelrod said.\par \par \uc2 Although Harris's popularity has surged since her whirlwind ascent to the top of the Democratic ticket, in a recent CBS News poll, over a third of respondents said they didn't know what she stands for.\par \par \uc2 Harris during her speech drew sharp contrasts between herself and Trump on issues such as taxes and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, warning that the president would slash taxes on the wealthy and increase tariffs on goods from foreign countries. She likened the former president's proposal to raise tariffs to a national sales tax\u8212\'20\'14"call it a Trump tax," she said.\par \par \uc2 On \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Harris blamed Trump for putting into place the Supreme Court justices who in 2022 overturned Roe v. Wade, which had established a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She accused Trump of preparing for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/abortion-donald-trump-2024-election-fe641cc5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nationwide \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14which the former president has denied he would pursue.\par \par \uc2 "Simply put, they are out of their minds," Harris said. "And one must ask: Why exactly is it that they don't trust women?"\par \par \uc2 She also addressed one of Trump's biggest lines of attack head on: the Biden administration's handling of the southern border. She blamed Trump for killing a bipartisan border-security bill that failed in the Senate earlier this year and said, as president, she would push for that legislation and sign it into law.\par \par \uc2 In recent days, Harris has begun {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/kamala-harriss-economic-team-and-agenda-start-to-take-shape-7682e539"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rolling out parts of her agenda,}}}\uc2  releasing a vision to make housing more affordable while lowering the cost of groceries. Harris's aides have said they want her agenda to provide a contrast with Trump without reading like a think-tank white paper.\par \par \uc2 Republicans, who have at times struggled to form a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/donald-trump-framing-kamala-harris-race-identity-db66ced2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 consistent line of attack}}}\uc2  against Harris, have criticized her for not providing detailed plans and tried to cast her as an out-of-touch liberal, pointing to her past support for the Green New Deal and Medicare for All.\par \par \uc2 Trump supporters also have tried to tie her to Biden's policies on the economy and inflation and decisions such as the withdrawal of troops from Afghanistan, which have been unpopular with voters.\par \par \uc2 Surveying America's standing around the globe, Harris made clear she would offer continuity on Biden's foreign policy goals, promising to "stand strong with Ukraine and our \uc2 NATO\uc2  allies," while working to end the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war.\par \par \uc2 Harris said she was working with Biden "around the clock" to broker a cease-fire deal and release of hostages in the region. She pledged to defend Israel's right to defend itself and end the humanitarian crisis in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Polls show Harris and Trump locked in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/dnc-election-2024-harris-walz/card/polling-shows-harris-s-gains-opening-paths-to-electoral-college-victory-Xh09WBpMtBb7fCVfw4MF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tight race}}}\uc2 , with the vice president gaining on the former president in most surveys, which had previously shown Biden lagging, before he bowed out. Harris leads Trump by 3.6 percentage points in the FiveThirtyEight.com average of public polls.\par \par \uc2 But her lead in most polls is within the margin of error\u8212\'20\'14and she trails in many polls of the battleground states. "This is a dead heat," said \uc2 Jen O'Malley Dillon\uc2 , Harris's campaign chair, during an event this week. "We are winning some battleground states and we are losing some."\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Harris's husband, Doug Emhoff, described a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/doug-emhoff-aims-to-be-the-first-first-gentleman-ad8bc3fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warm, family-focused person}}}\uc2 , who his children know as "Momala" and who officiated at his son's wedding. Harris's speech came on their 10th wedding anniversary.\par \par \uc2 The chance for America to elect the first woman to serve as president\u8212\'20\'14the strongest opportunity since Hillary Clinton's candidacy in 2016\u8212\'20\'14wasn't lost in Thursday's programming, though it wasn't always explicit.\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Annie Kuster\uc2  (D., N.H.), who is retiring from Congress after a dozen years, was one of many attendees who wore suffragist white inside Chicago's United Center, as many House Democrats have done during State of the Union addresses since the rise of Trump. Harris wore a dark suit and didn't talk of breaking the glass ceiling, as Clinton did earlier in the week.\par \par \uc2 "I have been waiting my entire life. It makes me really tearful," Kuster said, noting her late mother's long involvement in New Hampshire politics. "We've given our lives to this."\par \par \uc2 Alex Leary contributed to this article. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
