\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 The Parties Where Volunteers Pack  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pills for Red-State Women; Amid risks, volunteers are mobilizing to assist networks that mail  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  medication to women in states with strict limits\b0\par\par\uc2 By Scott Calvert | Photographs by Kayana Szymczak for WSJ \par \uc2 1,389 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 August 2024\par 01:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SOMERVILLE, Mass.\u8212\'20\'14The women huddling around the conference table shuttled the small cardboard boxes along, assembly-line style. Into each went medical-information paperwork and a handwritten note proclaiming, "We wish you the best!" Then came the critical addition, a two-drug regimen that ends a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 This tiny Boston-area office represents a new bulwark in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/abortion-rights-donors-karlie-kloss-phoebe-gates-ccf6ebbd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 America's \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  battle}}}\uc2 . Volunteers are mobilizing with growing frequency for pill-packing parties to help strangers in faraway states circumvent strict laws. On a recent Monday evening, the group filled 350 boxes\u8212\'20\'14in-home \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  kits ready for mailing to women in states such as Texas and Florida with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 near-total or six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Melissa Fischer, a 57-year-old internist, sees these efforts as a way to assist people tripped up by geography. "I strongly believe where somebody lives shouldn't dictate their access to critical healthcare," she said.\par \par \uc2 Retirees and professionals ate pizza, sipped Chardonnay in red plastic cups and chatted while working purposefully. Many portray the sessions as a tangible way to push back against the 2022 Supreme Court ruling that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated a constitutional right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It's a little bit of an antidote to hopelessness," said Judy Fleishman, 70, a medical educator. "There's something you can do."\par \par \uc2 Growing urgency\par \par \uc2 The parties support the Massachusetts Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Project, also known as the MAP, part of a growing movement to send \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills into ban states, often for just a few dollars. The nearly year-old MAP, like similar programs, leverages a state shield law meant to protect clinicians from legal jeopardy, including extradition. Massachusetts is among eight states with such laws.\par \par \uc2 These operations are intensifying amid more heated political debates. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-kamala-harris-election-2024-92511caa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spotlighting \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  in her presidential bid, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/republicans-adopt-stripped-down-platform-that-reflects-trumps-abortion-views-14a5ba98"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans struggle to articulate}}}\uc2  a winning message.\par \par \uc2 From July 2023 to March, shield-law groups provided more than 68,000 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  kits by mail to residents in states with tight limits on the procedure or telemedicine, according to WeCount, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -data project sponsored by the Society of Family Planning, which backs \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Shield-law providers accounted for about 9,500 medication abortions in March, up from 5,620 in July 2023, WeCount says.\par \par \uc2 "I think as long as we see states that are passing more and more restrictions, we're going to see these numbers continue to grow," said WeCount co-chair Ushma Upadhyay, a professor at the \uc2 University of California at San Francisco\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Abortions reached nearly 100,000 nationwide in March, up from 84,000 in May 2022, according to WeCount, despite 18 states imposing near-total or six-week bans. Medication abortions now outnumber surgical procedures. Nearly 20% of all abortions are via drugs sent by mail, including from bricks-and-mortar clinics.\par \par \uc2 So far, efforts targeting telemedicine abortions have failed. The Supreme Court in June {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone-f78f3320"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected a bid}}}\uc2  to restrict access to mifepristone, one of the two \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs. Some Republicans in Congress, including vice presidential nominee JD Vance, have called for enforcing the 1873 Comstock Act, a federal law barring the shipping of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs. More recently Vance has said the issue should be left to states.\par \par \uc2 Risk and pushback\par \par \uc2 Still, legal experts say there are risks for those involved in mailing pills to states with bans.\par \par \uc2 Angel Foster, 50, a doctor who helped launch the MAP last fall, trusts the Massachusetts shield law. But because it doesn't apply in other states, she won't visit her mother and stepfather in South Carolina and avoids flights that require stopovers in Texas.\par \par \uc2 Maureen Paul, the MAP's medical director, doesn't feel safe visiting her brother in Florida, where a six-week ban took effect in May. "We are no strangers to risk. I've had my home picketed, I've had death threats," she said. "But we're not fearful, we're not paralyzed. We're determined to act."\par \par \uc2 Frustrated officials in states with stringent laws can't disrupt the mail, but some are warning providers. Arkansas Attorney General Tim Griffin, a Republican, demanded two entities in May stop helping state residents get the pills, asserting such actions violate Arkansas law.\par \par \uc2 One warning went to Choices Women's Medical Center in New York, which doesn't mail pills but removed from its website wording about Arkansans taking clinic-provided pills at home. Founder Merle Hoffman said she thinks Griffin misunderstood how her clinic operates. A cease-and-desist letter also went to Aid Access, the largest shield-law provider, which disputes the allegations.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups say it is dangerous for women to take these pills without medical supervision. Providers say it's safe and that they screen for potential problems.\par \par \uc2 Pill-mailers are in new legal terrain. "No one has challenged any of these laws yet," said Rachel Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9, dean of the Temple University Beasley School of Law. "Texas has not tried to prosecute [clinicians], they haven't been sued, a medical board hasn't tried to discipline them. That's not to say those things aren't possible."\par \par \uc2 In Massachusetts, Paul, a 74-year-old doctor, is one of four prescribers at the MAP. In 1968, pregnant at age 18, she couldn't get a hospital \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and feared seeking an illegal one. She carried to term and gave up her child for adoption, an experience she calls "deeply traumatic and defining."\par \par \uc2 Launched last fall, the MAP is a project of Cambridge \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Health\b0 \highlight\uc2  Consultants, a nonprofit co-founded by Foster that has worked to boost medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in countries including Thailand, Pakistan and Uganda\u8212\'20\'14and saw a need for similar work in the U.S. MAP harnesses websites like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plancpills.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plancpills.org}}}\uc2  to get the word out to women nationwide. Prospective patients fill out intake forms online and mainly correspond by email, although some talk by phone with Foster or a prescriber.\par \par \uc2 The program accepts patients up to the 11th week of pregnancy, aiming to get pills to them by 12 weeks. Most are earlier than nine weeks, Foster said. Despite a $250 list price, patients pay about $130 on average; a third pay $25 or less.\par \par \uc2 The 6 p.m. party\par \par \uc2 At the MAP's office, before the recent pill-packing party, Foster read aloud comments women shared on intake forms. A Nebraska mother wrote: "I was using protection, but it failed, and I cannot afford to have another child right now." A Florida woman with a diabetic 5-year-old said: "I am struggling to pay my bills, and I'm not mentally ready to bring another child into my life yet."\par \par \uc2 Nearby, a MAP staffer printed address labels for 45 boxes of pills before packing them into tote bags for the trip to the post office. They were bound for 19 states, including Texas, Georgia and Florida.\par \par \uc2 Around 6 p.m., the volunteers filed in from work or home to replenish the supply of preloaded boxes. The gatherings jumped from monthly to twice-monthly in July, the MAP's busiest month with 560 boxes shipped, and are set to go weekly this fall.\par \par \uc2 Sonia Dettmann, 81, a retired clinical social worker, hasn't missed any. "I feel that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care is healthcare, and this is one way of supporting healthcare for folks from states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned. It's that simple," she said as she dropped mifepristone cartons into each box.\par \par \uc2 Another regular, Erin Gately, 47, likes to write notes in gold ink for "a little extra touch." An OB-GYN nurse practitioner, she sees "the challenges that come with an unplanned pregnancy and, whether somebody decides to continue with that unplanned pregnancy or not, it's their choice."\par \par \uc2 As boxes circulated around the table, conversation pinged from the Paris Olympics to a promising birth-control gel for men. Amid upbeat banter, the crew kept their production line humming. Though they fell short of Foster's goal of packing 475 boxes, she assured them 350 was more than fine.\par \par \uc2 "I am very impressed with us," she said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Scott Calvert at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:scott.calvert@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scott.calvert@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240813ek8d000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
