\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Trump Calls for Three Debates Against Harris, More Influence Over the Fed; Republican also casts his Democratic opponent as dodging the news media\b0\par\par\uc2 By Vivian Salama and Alex Leary \par \uc2 1,379 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2024\par 22:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PALM BEACH, Fla.\u8212\'20\'14Donald Trump called for three debates against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , said presidents should have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trumps-plans-stir-fears-for-fed-independence-inflation-689bc113"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 influence over the Federal Reserve}}}\uc2  and conceded he might be losing support among Black women during a news conference meant to recapture the spotlight after his rival picked up momentum.\par \par \uc2 The former president and 2024 GOP nominee said he agreed to a Sept. 4 debate on Fox News, a Sept. 10 debate on ABC, and a third on NBC on Sept. 25. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/the-2024-presidential-debate-plan-was-set-now-its-chaos-734f3886"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC debate was previously agreed upon}}}\uc2  when President Biden was in the race. Trump had called into question whether he would face off on ABC with the vice president now at the top of the Democratic ticket.\par \par \uc2 "I hope she agrees to them," Trump said during a news conference at his Mar-a-Lago estate Thursday afternoon. "I think they will be very revealing."\par \par \uc2 Harris said Thursday she was looking forward to debating Trump on Sept. 10. She had previously committed to it. Harris also said she was open to having another debate, without committing to the dates or networks Trump tossed out.\par \par \uc2 NBC declined to comment. Fox didn't comment.\par \par \uc2 On the Fed, Trump asserted that he has better instincts than the central bank's chairman and governors. "I feel that the president should have at least [a] say in there, yeah. I feel that strongly," he said.\par \par \uc2 "I think that, in my case, I made a lot of money," he added. "I was very successful and I think I have a better instinct than, in many cases, people that would be on the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  or the chairman."\par \par \uc2 Trump criticized the Fed, arguing that the central bank has "gotten it wrong a lot." He noted that he clashed with Fed Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  while he was in the White House. "I fought him very hard," Trump said. But, he added, "We got along fine."\par \par \uc2 Some allies of Trump have been advocating for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/central-banking/trump-allies-federal-reserve-independence-54423c2f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a more assertive role toward the Fed}}}\uc2 , the Journal previously reported.\par \par \uc2 Trump's press conference was meant, in part, to draw a contrast with Harris, whom Trump cast as dodging the news media. "She hasn't done an interview," Trump said, echoing a line of attack from his campaign in recent days.\par \par \uc2 Nearly three weeks since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/biden-drops-out-presidential-race-6b1c74fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden dropped out of the race}}}\uc2  and Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/kamala-harris-election-biden-5e2a0271"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 coalesced around Harris}}}\uc2  as the party's presumptive nominee, the vice president hasn't yet sat for an interview or taken public questions from reporters. Harris has held large rallies and given statements to reporters on the tarmac while traveling the country, but she hasn't engaged with the press beyond those events.\par \par \uc2 Harris's campaign shot back, saying Trump hasn't kept up as rigorous a schedule and accused him of focusing on grievances rather than discussing a vision for the country. "It's why voters will reject him again at the ballot box this November," said Ammar Moussa, a Harris campaign spokesman.\par \par \uc2 Trump had been largely off the campaign trail since his most-recent rally in Georgia on Saturday, when he attacked Republican Gov. Brian Kemp as "a bad guy" while characterizing Harris as overly liberal and weak on immigration. (On Friday he departs for a fundraising swing in Western states and will hold a rally that night in Bozeman, Mont.).\par \par \uc2 Trump's news conference followed a briefing by campaign aides for reporters in which they outlined their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/donald-trump-campaign-force-47-6f52b817"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strategy for winning in November}}}\uc2 , largely by courting so-called target persuadables, a sliver of undecided voters in battleground states.\par \par \uc2 "As long as we hold North Carolina, we just need to win Georgia and Pennsylvania," Trump pollster Tony Fabrizio told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Nontraditional battleground states such as Virginia and Minnesota\u8212\'20\'14which the campaign said were in play when Biden was in the race\u8212\'20\'14remain in play with Harris at the top of the ticket, senior Trump campaign officials said, further underscoring their view that Harris's recent bump in the polls won't last. Early polling since Biden left the race showed Harris and Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/harris-erases-trumps-lead-wsj-poll-finds-e286144d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 locked in a dead heat}}}\uc2  nationally and Harris narrowly ahead in certain swing states.\par \par \uc2 Trump, assessing his electoral prospects since Harris entered the race, acknowledged a changing landscape.\par \par \uc2 "It's possible that I won't do as well with Black women, but I do seem to do very well with other segments," Trump said, adding that he thought he was doing well with Hispanics, Jewish voters and white men. "White males have gone through the roof," Trump said.\par \par \uc2 He said he thought he was doing well with Black men and might see less support from Black females, but he said he could win some over. "I think ultimately they'll like me better, because I'm going to give them security, safety and jobs," Trump said.\par \par \uc2 He played down the significance of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an issue in the election, despite Harris and Democrats making it a focal point. And he declined to take a position on a Florida ballot initiative this fall that would override the state's new ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks and enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the Florida constitution. Rather, Trump said he would hold a news conference at a later time on the subject.\par \par \uc2 "Florida does have a vote coming up on that, and I think probably the vote will go in a little more liberal way than people thought," he said. Trump has said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be left to the states while at the same time bragging that he installed three conservatives on the Supreme Court, paving the way for the overturning of the landmark Roe v. Wade decision.\par \par \uc2 Trump spoke for over an hour to a standing-room crowd of reporters squeezed into the "living room," an opulently decorated space overlooking the Mar-a-Lago club patio, with towering ceilings of coffered gold and a stone fireplace partially-encapsulated in pillars. A few men in golf attire sat in chairs next to Alina Habba, one of Trump's lawyers.\par \par \uc2 It was the latest in a series of press availabilities the former president has done since Harris became the expected nominee last month, as his campaign went on the offensive looking to define Harris before she has the chance to define herself. She'll have her biggest opportunity to do that at the Democratic National Convention in Chicago later this month.\par \par \uc2 While acknowledging Harris has had a boost and energized Democrats, senior Trump campaign officials are confident her "honeymoon" phase will end. They are trying to cast Harris and her new running mate, Minnesota Gov. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , as too outside the mainstream for the country, hitting the ticket on immigration, crime and cultural issues, such as gender-affirming care.\par \par \uc2 During the press conference Thursday, Trump said Walz was "heavy into the transgender world." Despite carving out a lane as a moderate lawmaker in Washington, Walz had a left-leaning record as governor of Minnesota. He signed a law that made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a "fundamental right," passed paid family and medical leave, paid sick leave and transgender-rights protections.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately Trump's campaign thinks the economy is where the election will be won or lost. Campaign officials pointed to polling showing more Americans feel Trump is more trusted on the issue and can better bring down inflation. Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/cracks-in-economy-pose-risk-to-harriss-momentum-83665500"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sought to capitalize this week}}}\uc2  on market gyrations, though {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/stock-market-today-dow-sp500-nasdaq-live-08-08-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stocks rebounded}}}\uc2  and mortgage rates fell to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/housing/mortgage-rates-drop-to-15-month-low-e744aa2c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 15-month low}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The campaign will seek to make voters feel Harris is indistinguishable from Biden, whom she replaced following the incumbent's decision to withdraw amid widespread concerns among Democrats about his ability to defeat Trump given his advanced age.\par \par \uc2 Officials also expressed confidence in Trump's running mate, Ohio Sen. \uc2 JD Vance\uc2 , who has been targeted by Democrats for past positions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and for demeaning comments about childless women, among other things.\par \par \uc2 "JD Vance has really stepped up. He's doing a fantastic job," Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Isabella Simonetti, Tarini Parti and Andrew Restuccia contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Vivian Salama at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:vivian.salama@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vivian.salama@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Alex Leary at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:alex.leary@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alex.leary@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240808ek88004ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
