\par\par \uc2 Tim Higgins\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 How \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 's Baby Fever Is Shaping His Public Persona; The billionaire's worries about birthrates help fuel the political moment\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tim Higgins \par \uc2 1,320 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2024\par 09:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 's baby fever has gone political.\par \par \uc2 "Having a kid is a vote for the future," the billionaire said recently. "It is the most optimistic thing that somebody can do."\par \par \uc2 It was just one of his many remarks lately aimed at blunting a decline in birthrates, a concern he has talked about for years but has grown more intense as the topic has become au courant in the presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 The chief executive of \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  cautions about policies promoted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1719398881870356695"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what he calls "extinctionists."}}}\uc2  He has pointed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and birth control as causes, and frets that civilization will "die with a whimper in adult diapers" if {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1480564443629207557"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declining birthrates}}}\uc2  aren't addressed.\par \par \uc2 Years ago, his observations about birthrates seemed like just another one of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/business/elon-musk-dei-criticisms-star-wars-fc17b115"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mercurial interests}}}\uc2  or a convenient reason for why the thrice-divorced father has had so many children. (He said last month that he has 12.)\par \par \uc2 More recently, demographers and government officials are increasingly pointing to low birthrates as a real threat. Leaders\u8212\'20\'14including the prime ministers of Japan and Italy\u8212\'20\'14express worry about the ramifications, from shrinking workforces to slowing economic growth.\par \par \uc2 The topic has taken on political hues as Republicans try to paint Democrats as being against families while Democrats advocate for a woman's right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "If your society is not having enough children to replace itself, that is a profoundly dangerous and destabilizing thing," JD Vance, the Republican vice-presidential candidate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q5eKcsdOf7k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said recently}}}\uc2  on "The Megyn Kelly Show." The Ohio senator was defending old comments about the dangers of "childless cat ladies," saying he was attacking those who he says are antifamily, while rivals have said his words were cruel and offensive to women.\par \par \uc2 After endorsing former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/shots-fired-elon-musk-heard-a-call-donald-trump-3c2f3f27"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bid to return to the White House}}}\uc2 , Musk was quick to praise Vance as the VP pick and amplify the senator's idea of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1813004941964750939"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 giving parents more votes}}}\uc2  than childless citizens.\par \par \uc2 Musk's bullish views on fatherhood have had an imprint on his business\u8212\'20\'14small and large.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's Model S sedan in 2012 was uniquely designed to have seven seats to fit his family, which at the time included five young children. (The kids featured prominently in a New Yorker photo with their dad playing with modeling clay ahead of the car's release.)\par \par \uc2 Last month Musk announced that the headquarters of \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  and the social-media platform X were moving to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/elon-musk-california-democrats-864ea6ed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas from California}}}\uc2  in part because of the Golden State's enactment of a law that supporters say is aimed at protecting transgender children. Musk and others say the law hinders parental rights.\par \par \uc2 Musk's objections regarding medical procedures for transgender children appear rooted in broader worries about procreation. "So-called gender affirming care, which is a terrible euphemism," Musk told the author Jordan Peterson during an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/realDailyWire/status/1815504648788193405"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview last month streamed on X}}}\uc2 . "It's really a child sterilization\u8230\'20\'26They can never have children again."\par \par \uc2 In 2021, Musk sounded the alarm about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/video/events/elon-musk-on-his-tech-empire-and-the-role-of-government/F9430AD3-D951-4B78-B529-6BFC07D78612.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 birthrate concerns}}}\uc2  at a Wall Street Journal event.\par \par \uc2 "I can't emphasize this enough, there are not enough people," he said. "And I think one of the biggest risks to civilization is the low birth rate\u8230\'20\'26If people don't have more children, civilization is going to crumble."\par \par \uc2 Since that year, Musk has tweeted about his "birth rate" worries at least 26 times\u8212\'20\'14including nine times this year alone. (For comparison, since 2021, he has only made jokes about 420, a favorite reference to marijuana use, nine times.)\par \par \uc2 He has also aired his birthrate concerns on stage at numerous public events, including last year, when Musk said he supported tax breaks or other government incentives for having children.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What do you think of \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 's push for having more children? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 More recently, Musk has become more vocal in criticizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and birth control. During an interview with Fox News last year, he blamed them for declining birthrates, and this year has tweeted several times about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1767569935314669615"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 downsides of hormonal birth control}}}\uc2 . (Some researchers have said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/is-there-a-link-between-a-decline-in-u-s-births-and-abortion-11550847334"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  isn't a primary driver}}}\uc2  of declining birthrates.)\par \par \uc2 "Women in the West have been taught that an accidental pregnancy is the worst thing that could possibly happen to them," {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1722317780647583908"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Musk tweeted last year}}}\uc2 . "Thus, they strongly oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans as being an existential threat. Many men also fear that they will be unable to have 'fun' if \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is outlawed."\par \par \uc2 As Musk has become more outspoken on his views around children, he faces more scrutiny about not just his role fathering many kids but the part he plays in parenting them, including a recent public clash with his daughter.\par \par \uc2 The philanthropist Melinda French Gates recently suggested his views are "silly." Asked about Musk in a \uc2 New York Times Magazine\uc2  interview, she took issue with why male tech leaders, who spend so much time working, are questioned about their parenting style. "I'm sure he's a fantastic CEO and has done a great job\u8212\'20\'14maybe or maybe not\u8212\'20\'14in their company," she said without mentioning Musk specifically. "But then they get asked about parenting, and they spew all this stuff, and you think, 'Something doesn't add up here.' "\par \par \uc2 As the world's richest man, Musk has resources that give him advantages when it comes to extra mouths to feed.\par \par \uc2 His first wife, Justine Musk, once wrote that when they discussed having children before marriage, he asked how many kids she wanted. "One or two," she replied. "Although if I could afford nannies, I'd like to have four," she told him, according to her account in Marie Claire magazine, which came out around the time of their contentious divorce.\par \par \uc2 He laughed, according to her telling in 2010. "That's the difference between you and me," he said. "I just assume that there will be nannies."\par \par \uc2 And there were. Divorce records show that even though Musk's finances were troubled at the time, he was spending on nannies for their five children\u8212\'20\'14twins and triplets. (A sixth, their first child, died as an infant\u8212\'20\'14a loss that Musk occasionally discusses when talking about his views on children.)\par \par \uc2 One of those children has recently said Musk was rarely around during her childhood. In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/elon-musk-transgender-daughter-vivian-wilson-interview-rcna163665"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview with NBC News}}}\uc2 , Vivian Jenna Wilson, now 20, disputed Musk's claims last month that he was tricked into consenting to her transition to female from male as a teenager. Musk figuratively called her "dead."\par \par \uc2 "He was cold," Wilson is quoted as saying of her father. "He's very quick to anger. He is uncaring and narcissistic." Musk hasn't commented on the interview.\par \par \uc2 Roughly 15 years after his first divorce, Musk now has with two other women a new batch of young children, including one named X \u198\'00\'C6 A-12, or X for short. The 4-year-old, who is part of a custody dispute between Musk and his mother, has become something of a companion for the globe-trotting billionaire, heard in the background during late-night rap sessions on social media or tagging along to meet foreign leaders, such as the president of Turkey.\par \par \uc2 In public photos, the senior Musk is often seen doting on little X. Musk talks about such bonds, saying that we are biologically inclined to "love our children" and that even those who have taken a hedonistic approach to life can find the appeal.\par \par \uc2 "I've had friends who are hedonistic and they're very good people and I've actually convinced some of them to have kids, which I'm happy to say, and they thanked me afterwards," Musk said last month. "And not one person has said they regretted\u8212\'20\'14ever."\par \par \uc2 Write to Tim Higgins at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:tim.higgins@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tim.higgins@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240803ek83000jj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
