\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Harris Puts  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 , a Weakness for Trump, at Center of Campaign; In contrast with Biden, who was reluctant to say the word  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 , Harris has campaigned aggressively on it\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey, Laura Kusisto and Vivian Salama \par \uc2 1,174 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 July 2024\par 02:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is making {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/kamala-harris-policies-abortion-taxes-climate-d746f220"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights central to her candidacy}}}\uc2  for president as Republicans struggle to articulate a winning message on the issue.\par \par \uc2 In contrast with President Biden, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-activists-push-for-biden-to-be-more-outspoken-11653044400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was reluctant to say the word}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the vice president has campaigned aggressively on it since the 2022 Supreme Court ruling that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated the constitutional right}}}\uc2  to the procedure. At the White House, she has met with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and women who have had abortions. Earlier this year, Harris was believed to be the first president or vice president to visit an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic.\par \par \uc2 After {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/how-kamala-harris-locked-up-nomination-b5ccf4e6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 locking up the support}}}\uc2  to be the Democratic nominee, Harris's campaign launched a blitz of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related campaign activities Monday, including events hosted by second gentleman Doug Emhoff and advocates. The campaign also released a video with the vice president condemning a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2  in Iowa, hoping to energize women and independent voters with her promise to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 As the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/kamala-harris-black-voters-georgia-a3b758b6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landscape of the 2024 race rapidly shifts}}}\uc2 , Republican presidential nominee \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  must now contend with an opponent who embraces \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in a way that Biden didn't\u8212\'20\'14and who is viewed positively on the issue. A recent Wall Street Journal poll showed that 51% of voters thought Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/harris-erases-trumps-lead-wsj-poll-finds-e286144d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was best able to handle \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , compared with 33% who preferred Trump. Harris lagged behind Trump on issues such as immigration and the economy.\par \par \uc2 Mike Bocian, a Democratic pollster who conducted the poll with Republican pollster David Lee, said: "It makes a lot of sense for her to elevate this issue. Republicans wanted to take away women's reproductive freedom and now that they did it, they want to talk about it as little as possible."\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the Republican National Convention earlier this month, the GOP released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/republicans-adopt-stripped-down-platform-that-reflects-trumps-abortion-views-14a5ba98"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stripped-down party platform}}}\uc2  that only mentions the word "\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 " once. It also states that the party opposes late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while supporting prenatal care as well as access to birth control and in vitro fertilization treatments. That language appears intended to undercut {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/schumer-forces-republicans-to-take-sides-on-ivf-contraception-1209703d?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warnings from Democrats}}}\uc2  that Republican victories in November would lead to a GOP-led crackdown on contraception and fertility treatments.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups, which have been frustrated with Republicans' efforts to play down the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate, argue that Harris's efforts now make the issue impossible for Republicans to avoid.\par \par \uc2 "They've had this ostrich mentality," said Kristan Hawkins, president of Students for Life Action. "I really think \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  being at the top of the Democratic ticket is going to force the GOP to engage in this debate."\par \par \uc2 At her first official campaign rally, Harris vowed to "stop \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans." \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocacy groups have rushed to support her, with the political arm of Emily's List announcing a $2 million advertising campaign backing Harris that focuses on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 "This is somebody who isn't just comfortable, she's a fighter on this issue," said \uc2 Mini Timmaraju\uc2 , the president of \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights could be on the ballot in at least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/abortion-rights-donors-karlie-kloss-phoebe-gates-ccf6ebbd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 half-a-dozen states in November}}}\uc2 , including the battleground state of Arizona. And new state laws and legal cases have also kept \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  top of mind for many voters. The latest example is an Iowa law banning most abortions after about six weeks of pregnancy, which takes effect Monday.\par \par \uc2 Republican congressional candidates underperformed in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-dobbs-year-after-roe-support-politics-d1ef5a5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2022 midterm elections}}}\uc2 . Polls showed that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a top issue that energized Democratic voters, as well as suburban women who identify as Republicans or independents.\par \par \uc2 Harris is looking to put Trump and his running mate, Sen. \uc2 JD Vance\uc2 , (R., Ohio), on defense given the fight for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has been a political loser for Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Trump appointed three of the Supreme Court justices who voted to overturn the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/trump-says-it-was-great-honor-to-appoint-justices-who-voted-to-overturn-roe-bG8IoHon8J4NePvvnKQc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has repeatedly bragged about it}}}\uc2 . He also selected a vice president with a conservative record on the issue. But Trump also has said he wants to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/abortion-donald-trump-2024-election-fe641cc5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leave the issue to the states}}}\uc2  to decide and has said he won't block access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone, used in the majority of abortions.\par \par \uc2 "President Trump has long been consistent in supporting the rights of states to make decisions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Karoline Leavitt, the Trump campaign's national press secretary.\par \par \uc2 During the Republican National Convention, Trump avoided the topic of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But at his first rally since Harris became the expected Democratic nominee, he tried to paint her as extreme and out-of-step with many Americans, portraying her as supporting abortions in the eighth and ninth month of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What impact will the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue have on the presidential election? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Harris has said that she supports restoring the protections found in Roe v. Wade, which protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access nationwide until a fetus is viable outside the womb, or about halfway through a typical pregnancy. Roe also allowed for abortions after viability to preserve the life or health of the pregnant woman. When pressed for more specifics in a \uc2 CBS\uc2  interview last fall, Harris declined to elaborate.\par \par \uc2 Vance's past views on abortions have come under scrutiny. He has expressed support for banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout pregnancy with only an exception for the life of the mother. He has also said the issue should primarily be left up to the states but has at times supported a national ban after the earliest weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 As a Senate candidate he also said that a bill setting what he called a "minimum national standard" was a good idea. More recently he has echoed Trump's position that the issue should be left to the states.\par \par \uc2 "Senator Vance has made his position clear: he agrees with President Trump that each state should have the chance to individually set their own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws," said Taylor Van Kirk, a spokeswoman for Vance. "Desperate attacks from Democrats will not distract voters from the deadly effects of Kamala's wide open border, the untenable cost of living caused by her inflationary spending, or any other aspect of her far left, radical agenda."\par \par \uc2 As a senator, Vance also signed a letter asking the Justice Department to enforce the Comstock Act, a 151-year-old ban on mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills that has been a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/democrats-shine-spotlight-on-1873-abortion-law-despite-risks-8113a469"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 central concern}}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates in a potential future Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 "I think his heart is 100% pro-life," said Frank Cannon, chief political strategist at Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America. "When you are the vice president you have to adapt your position to that of the presidential candidate."\par \par \uc2 Liz Essley Whyte contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com}}}\uc2 , Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Vivian Salama at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:vivian.salama@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vivian.salama@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240730ek7u000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
