\par \par \uc2 Harrison Wells at his family home in Menlo Park, Calif. PHOTO: Ian Bates for WSJ\par \par \uc2 He led a chapter of a conservative group, Young Americans for Freedom, at the \uc2 University of Wisconsin\uc2  and voted for Trump in 2020. He sides with the former president on the economy, taxes and immigration.\par \par \uc2 Journal polling found that young men are open to Trump policy proposals that young women reject. That includes Trump's idea to deploy troops to the U.S.-Mexico border and to deport millions of undocumented immigrants.\par \par \uc2 Ems, the \uc2 Penn State\uc2  student, cited widely viewed TikTok videos showing women being asked if they would rather be stuck in the woods with a man or a bear. Most women picked the bear, reasoning that a man might be more dangerous.\par \par \uc2 Ems wasn't sure which she would pick\u8212\'20\'14though the bear, she said, could well be the safer bet.\par \par \uc2 Sources: Wall Street Journal survey of 500 voters under age 30, conducted Feb. 21\u8211\'20\'1328, 2024; margin of error: +/- 6.1 pct. points for young women and 6.3 points for young men (\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  always/mostly legal; student loans); Wall Street Journal survey of 250 registered voters under age 30, conducted Feb. 21\u8211\'20\'1328, 2024: margin of error: +/- 8.7 pct pts for young women and 8.9 pts for young men. (tax cut; gender identity; Obamacare; climate; immigration proposals)\par \par \uc2 Write to Aaron Zitner at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:aaron.zitner@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aaron.zitner@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Andrew Restuccia at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:andrew.restuccia@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 andrew.restuccia@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240729ek7t000gr\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
