\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 The New Wave of Powerhouse Donors Backing  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights; Phoebe Gates, Karlie Kloss and Connie Ballmer push for rights after Dobbs\b0\par\par\uc2 By Juliet Chung and Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 906 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 July 2024\par 12:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Phoebe Gates recalls a moment two years ago that set her on the path to donating millions of dollars to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups.\par \par \uc2 Gates, now 21, was upset about the Supreme Court's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning of the landmark Roe v. Wade ruling}}}\uc2  that enshrined the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Her mother, philanthropist Melinda French Gates, urged her to stay angry, then asked, "What are you going to do about it?"\par \par \uc2 Visits to women's health clinics in Louisiana and Mississippi last year helped her see the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans firsthand and decide how to direct her giving.\par \par \uc2 "For me, having freedom to make decisions about your future really kind of transcends everything," said Gates, who graduated from college in June.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court decision in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization is animating prominent young advocates and heavy-hitting donors who are helping elevate one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-kamala-harris-election-2024-92511caa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strongest issues for Democrats}}}\uc2  heading into the November elections. Their backing is going to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/abortion-rights-advocates-deploy-a-new-red-state-playbook-8f13a644"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state-by-state legal and political fight}}}\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights that has emerged since Dobbs, or supporting women caught up in the practical fallout.\par \par \uc2 Model and activist Karlie Kloss said her Gateway Coalition has helped direct more than $3 million in donations to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in the Midwest. Kloss, who as a teenager trained to escort patients arriving at \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  in St. Louis, Mo., began planning to fund \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access when the Dobbs decision was leaked in May 2022.\par \par \uc2 Kloss has also given personally to ballot initiatives in Florida and Missouri that would add a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until fetal viability, or about halfway through a typical pregnancy, to those states' constitutions.\par \par \uc2 "What's going to happen in November is a very important front line on so many state levels, and certainly in the White House," said Kloss, 31.\par \par \uc2 Kloss is married to venture investor \uc2 Josh Kushner\uc2 , the brother of \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2 , who is former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's son-in-law. A spokeswoman for Kloss said she is "a lifelong Democrat and will vote for the Democratic ticket this fall."\par \par \uc2 Recent polling has shown Americans' support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/support-for-abortion-access-is-near-record-wsj-norc-poll-finds-6021c712"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the highest levels on record}}}\uc2  since researchers began tracking it in the 1970s. President Biden has tapped into that sentiment by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/the-tragic-pregnancy-stories-filling-the-abortion-campaign-airwaves-74c4fa41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 running ads featuring women}}}\uc2  who struggled to obtain emergency abortions and blaming Trump for Roe's overturning.\par \par \uc2 A Republican party platform, meanwhile, recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/republicans-adopt-stripped-down-platform-that-reflects-trumps-abortion-views-14a5ba98"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 softened the party's language on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , which Trump views as a vulnerability. The platform now reflects his view that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should largely be left to the states.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What impact will the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue have on the presidential election? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The fight playing out across the country around {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-allows-emergency-abortions-in-idaho-but-leaves-big-questions-unresolved-7fae6427"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 emergency abortions}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone-f78f3320"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pills to terminate pregnancies}}}\uc2  and efforts to restrict out-of-state travel for abortions is drawing donors who want to restore rights they view as fundamental. Others see a chance to drive voter turnout up and down the ballot.\par \par \uc2 Some of the new giving is coming from tech fortunes. Wendy Schmidt, who is married to former \uc2 Google\uc2  CEO \uc2 Eric Schmidt\uc2 , has donated at least $10 million to state ballot initiatives on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, said people familiar with her giving. Connie Ballmer has given $2 million to an initiative in Michigan, where she and her husband, \uc2 Los Angeles Clippers\uc2  owner \uc2 Steve Ballmer\uc2 , have deep ties.\par \par \uc2 In May, French Gates said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/business/melinda-french-gates-is-resigning-from-the-gates-foundation-76b0fcd7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her Pivotal Philanthropies Foundation}}}\uc2  would give a portion of $200 million over the next two years to groups working on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/the-abortion-rights-movement-is-on-a-winning-streak-will-ohio-stop-it-4c13d41f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long have relied on large donors}}}\uc2 , including the Catholic Church and \uc2 Richard Uihlein\uc2 , a billionaire conservative who founded an industrial shipping company.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups have also depended on funding from a handful of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/warren-buffetts-estate-planning-bill-and-melinda-gates-foundation-sends-charities-scrambling-11655811074"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 big donors}}}\uc2 , including the Susan Thompson Buffett Foundation and the \uc2 David and Lucile Packard Foundation\uc2 . A flood of so-called "rage giving" from smaller donors boosted groups after Dobbs, but that has since subsided, re-emphasizing the importance of big gifts.\par \par \uc2 Longtime backers of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have stepped up as well.\par \par \uc2 Sheryl Sandberg\uc2 , who left \uc2 Meta Platforms\uc2 's board earlier this year, has donated anonymously to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics for years. After Roe was overturned, she gave $3 million to \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  to fight \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, her biggest public commitment yet.\par \par \uc2 Tracy Weitz, an \uc2 American University\uc2  sociology professor who focuses on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the new giving reflects a change from the decades when Roe was seen as settled law, and donors felt there weren't many opportunities to effect large-scale change.\par \par \uc2 "People see an opportunity with ballot initiatives, they see opportunity with political candidates, and they see opportunity with organizing," Weitz said.\par \par \uc2 For Phoebe Gates, that means backing ballot initiatives and giving to groups helping women in urgent need of abortions, like Just the Pill, which provides medication abortions. She is also funding activists who are trying to galvanize young people to vote in November for candidates who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 She said speaking with activists helped inform her plan to give millions this year.\par \par \uc2 "There's a tangible chance to make a change here," she said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Juliet Chung at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Juliet.Chung@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Juliet.Chung@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240719ek7j001rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
