\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Democrats Shine Spotlight on 1873  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law, Despite Risks; Whether to try to overturn Comstock law presents dilemma for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters\b0\par\par\uc2 By Liz Essley Whyte and Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 1,071 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 July 2024\par 16:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 After months of trying to play down a 151-year-old ban on mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  items, Democrats are now the ones who could raise its public profile.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/a-19th-century-law-could-help-influence-the-abortion-pills-future-639dddb6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal 1873 Comstock Act  }}}\uc2 , a criminal law, prohibits shipping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs or other items used in abortions but isn't currently enforced for that purpose. Democrats in Congress last month launched an effort to repeal parts of the law, despite concerns from some allies that doing so would undermine the Biden administration's argument that the statute is unenforceable.\par \par \uc2 "My legislation is simply recognizing that anti-choice Republicans in a future Trump administration believe this is a tool," said Sen. \uc2 Tina Smith\uc2  (D., Minn.), the bill's sponsor in the Senate. "We need to draw awareness to that and try to take that tool away from them."\par \par \uc2 The Comstock law presents a dilemma for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters, with different camps arguing the law is irrelevant\u8212\'20\'14or highly dangerous.\par \par \uc2 Smith is still lining up Democratic colleagues to co-sponsor the bill; currently she has about two dozen. The measure would face an uphill battle to pass in the chamber, where 60 votes would be needed under chamber rules, and likely wouldn't get to the floor in the GOP-controlled House.\par \par \uc2 Still, a vote would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-ivf-republicans-election-2024-f044dc5b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 force congressional Republicans to take a public stance  }}}\uc2  on whether to keep Comstock, generating headlines on the broader \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -access debate that Democrats see as critical to the 2024 election. Proponents say it is worth trying.\par \par \uc2 "I think that would be a grave mistake not to push for repeal, a significantly grave mistake," said Larry Gostin, a professor of global health law at Georgetown law school.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department has said the law only applies when the sender intends to aid an illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pointing out that there are legal uses for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in every state, such as treatment for a miscarriage or abortions that protect the life of the mother. The administration relied on that interpretation when it successfully defended access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone before the Supreme Court earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 Major \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups last year endorsed a House resolution introduced by Democratic lawmakers saying that access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills "does not violate federal law," citing the Justice Department memo.\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats in the Senate have been slow to sign onto the Comstock repeal effort, wary of undercutting the Biden administration's legal arguments, a Democratic aide said.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department "has made it very clear that Comstock does not apply," Sen. \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  , a Washington Democrat who hasn't signed onto the bill, said at a press conference last month. "At this point I've not seen the legislation. We'll obviously review it."\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for the White House said federal agencies must follow the Justice Department's interpretation of the law but that it supports congressional efforts to protect reproductive freedom.\par \par \uc2 "The litigators might prefer we say nothing, but I am not willing to wait to see what the Supreme Court does on this," said Kirsten Moore, director of the Expanding Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access project, who has pushed for the repeal effort. "We just can't afford to take that chance."\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How do you view the Comstock Act in relation to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The effort also comes as Democrats are holding votes on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/schumer-forces-republicans-to-take-sides-on-ivf-contraception-1209703d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 other messaging bills tied to \b  \highlight22reproductive rights\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , including contraception and in vitro fertilization. On Wednesday, Democrats tried to pass an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights bill that would codify {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  into law. It failed to advance, with 49 in favor and 44 against, short of the 60 votes needed under chamber rules.\par \par \uc2 Smith said she first learned about Comstock in the early 2000s when she worked for \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  's Midwestern affiliate and was researching the history of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. After Roe was overturned in June 2022, the old law came to mind for Smith.\par \par \uc2 "I thought, 'Well gosh, what's to stop these antiabortion extremists from trying to use Comstock to make it more difficult for women?' " she said.\par \par \uc2 Her staff worked on the bill for more than a year. They sought to build support among allies, some of whom early on were reluctant to bring attention to Comstock and feared that if a repeal vote fails in Congress that could be used as a weapon in litigation, people familiar with the matter said. But as Republicans grew more vocal about using the law to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including in oral arguments at the Supreme Court where two of the court's most conservative justices asked questions about the law, more Democrats saw the value in speaking up as well.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion activists are also divided on how much to emphasize Comstock and how it should be used.\par \par \uc2 "We see it as one of many tools in the toolbox," said Kristi Hamrick, spokeswoman for Students for Life, an antiabortion group.\par \par \uc2 Some see a chance to use it in certain, limited ways, such as nixing telehealth and mail-order pharmacies for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. \uc2 The Heritage Foundation\uc2  , a conservative think tank, argued in its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/donald-trump-project-2025-dcd4ad47"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 "Project 2025" policy plan  }}}\uc2  that a potential future Trump administration should enforce Comstock.\par \par \uc2 Others worry that prosecuting people for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related activities could backfire amid public disapproval.\par \par \uc2 In his debate with President Biden, Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sought to distance himself from some Republicans' efforts to block access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill. His articulation of the details was fuzzy, however, and he didn't mention Comstock specifically. "I will not block it," Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Some activists want to see the law enforced at every opportunity, including to prosecute \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors and shut down \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics. Nearly 80 local governments across seven states have passed ordinances making themselves "sanctuary cities for the unborn," with about 20 of those explicitly relying on Comstock, at the urging of Mark Lee Dickson, director of Right to Life of East Texas.\par \par \uc2 "This is the strongest law that the pro-life movement has on the books in America right now," Dickson said. "We would be foolish not to advocate for its full enforcement."\par \par \uc2 Write to Liz Essley Whyte at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:liz.whyte@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liz.whyte@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at \par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240712ek7c004mp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
