\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Abortions to Save Mothers' Lives Are an Agonizing Call for Doctors; Supreme Court decision on emergency  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  laws in Idaho leaves unresolved challenges for physicians nationwide\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas and Betsy McKay \par \uc2 1,354 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 June 2024\par 16:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 For two years, doctors in more than a dozen states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is restricted have faced an agonizing calculus.\par \par \uc2 When has a pregnant woman's medical condition deteriorated enough to qualify for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under state law? And at what point might doctors compromise their medical duty to help a patient by not performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  sooner?\par \par \uc2 "Pick your poison," said Dr. Sarah Osmundson, a maternal-fetal medicine doctor in Nashville, Tenn.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court on Thursday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-allows-emergency-abortions-in-idaho-but-leaves-big-questions-unresolved-7fae6427"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed emergency abortions to be performed }}}\uc2  in Idaho. The majority of justices voted to dismiss Idaho's appeal of a lower-court order permitting emergency abortions under federal law governing hospitals that accept Medicare.\par \par \uc2 The ruling doesn't clarify when abortions can be performed in emergencies. While it allows doctors in Idaho to perform abortions to stabilize women's health, the decision leaves doctors around the country in the limbo they have occupied for two years.\par \par \uc2 The overturning of Roe v. Wade in 2022 created a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 patchwork of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2  across the country, prompting women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/new-mexico-abortion-clinics-demand-1a888fa7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to travel across state lines }}}\uc2  for the procedure. Fourteen states enforce laws that ban nearly all abortions. Three others restrict abortions after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 All include exceptions to save a pregnant woman's life. But determining when a life is in enough danger to qualify for exceptions under these laws {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/doctors-struggle-with-state-abortion-restrictions-at-odds-with-federal-law-11657445400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has proved challenging }}}\uc2  for doctors who worry their decisions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/doctors-struggle-with-navigating-abortion-bans-in-medical-emergencies-11665684225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could make them vulnerable to prosecution }}}\uc2  under state law.\par \par \uc2 "No one wants to be the test case\u8212\'20\'14myself included," said Dr. Richard Todd Ivey, an obstetrician-gynecologist in Houston. He said one recent pregnant patient suffered premature rupture of membranes and had to wait until she developed an infection before receiving an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw479\pich640\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal7185\pichgoal9600
FF
