\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Supreme Court Allows Emergency Abortions in Idaho but Leaves Big Questions Unresolved; Decision tees up longer-term fight over issue that has galvanized voters\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 874 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 June 2024\par 18:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court officially announced Thursday that it would allow emergency abortions in Idaho without deciding key issues in the case, closing an unusual episode in which a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-draft-opinion-suggests-it-will-allow-emergency-abortions-62234e5b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 draft of the decision accidentally became public }}}\uc2  a day earlier.\par \par \uc2 Since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the court overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  two years ago, ending federal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the inability of women in some states to access abortions in medical emergencies has emerged as a top issue, shifting public opinion on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and galvanizing political opposition to bans on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's nondecision, in which a majority\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://prod-i.a.dj.com/public/resources/documents/SCOTUSIDABORTION.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to dismiss the case }}}\uc2  as "improvidently granted," will do little to end that debate or provide clarity to doctors struggling with how to interpret {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortions-to-save-mothers-lives-are-an-agonizing-call-for-doctors-3d580f73"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lifesaving exceptions to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Three different camps of three justices expressed a range of views on the case. In the end, the court voted 6-3 to ditch the case without a ruling.\par \par \uc2 By stepping back from the case, the justices reinstated a lower-court order allowing doctors broad discretion to perform abortions in Idaho in medical emergencies. The action won't change anything for physicians nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court had two \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases on its docket this term. It ended up deciding nothing of substance in either of them. The other case involved a challenge to decisions by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  to expand {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone-f78f3320"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 access to the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill mifepristone }}}\uc2 , which is used in the majority of abortions in the country. Earlier this month, the justices said the plaintiffs, antiabortion medical associations and physicians, didn't have standing to bring the suit.\par \par \uc2 The continued legal turmoil could affect races up and down the ballot in November. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-ivf-republicans-election-2024-f044dc5b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an important motivator for some voters }}}\uc2  over the last couple of years and Democrats are trying to persuade them that it remains salient. Republicans plan to focus attention on other issues, such as the economy and immigration, but have struggled to counter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/the-tragic-pregnancy-stories-filling-the-abortion-campaign-airwaves-74c4fa41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 emotional stories of pregnant women }}}\uc2  denied abortions when faced with medical crises.\par \par \uc2 "Because Trump's Supreme Court majority overturned Roe v. Wade, women are being turned away from emergency rooms and forced to the brink of death before receiving the care they need," a senior adviser to President Biden's re-election campaign said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's presidential campaign said: "President Trump has long been consistent in supporting the rights of states to make decisions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court had taken up the Idaho case to decide whether the federal Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act requires doctors to perform abortions to stabilize a seriously ill patient, even when state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans only allow the procedure if a patient's life is in danger.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/idaho-must-allow-abortions-in-certain-emergencies-judge-rules-11661386919"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which sued Idaho }}}\uc2 , had argued the act requires hospitals to provide an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a woman at risk of long-term disabilities, including infertility or kidney damage. The state argued the federal law doesn't mandate, or even mention, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 More than a dozen states now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have bans on most abortions }}}\uc2 . All of them have some type of exception if a woman's life is in danger but a handful don't allow one if her long-term health is at serious risk. Republicans and antiabortion groups have said such laws balance the mother's suffering against the needs of her unborn child.\par \par \uc2 Idaho Attorney General \uc2 Ra\u250\'00\'FAl Labrador\uc2  said he tells doctors around the state that they are empowered to use their good-faith judgment in difficult situations.\par \par \uc2 "I think they have been told incorrectly by some of these pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawyers in the United States that they're going to be prosecuted all the time and that is just not the case in any way," Labrador said.\par \par \uc2 Though the Supreme Court ducked the issue for now, the justices will have to confront it again soon. A U.S. appeals court in New Orleans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ca5.uscourts.gov/opinions/pub/23/23-10246-CV0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled earlier this year }}}\uc2  that the federal emergency-care law doesn't mandate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care and Texas should be allowed to enforce the full scope of its near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. The Justice Department has already filed an appeal with the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 In an embarrassment for the court, a copy of the Idaho decision was very briefly available on the court's website Wednesday before being quickly removed. The court acknowledged the error.\par \par \uc2 Three justices in the court's center\u8212\'20\'14Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  and Justices \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14effectively controlled Thursday's outcome, saying time had shown the court had taken up the case prematurely.\par \par \uc2 The court's three liberal justices\u8212\'20\'14\uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 , \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2  and \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14also voted to dismiss the case but said they believed federal law pre-empts state law in cases where a woman's health is at risk.\par \par \uc2 The three most conservative justices\u8212\'20\'14\uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14said the court should have decided the case and ruled for Idaho.\par \par \uc2 Catherine Lucey and Alex Leary contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240627ek6r0035x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
