\par\par \uc2 Health Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Rights Advocates Deploy a New Red State Playbook; After Ohio voters approved a constitutional amendment, movement's lawyers are citing it to challenge state restrictions\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 871 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 June 2024\par 13:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates have a plan to undo dozens of longstanding restrictions in some of the country's more conservative states. It starts with Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Clinics are challenging a host of limits the state adopted over the past decade or so, including waiting periods for the procedure, requirements that doctors check for fetal cardiac activity before an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rules that prevent patients from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone-f78f3320"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtaining \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills }}}\uc2  legally through the mail.\par \par \uc2 For years, those restrictions were often on solid legal footing. That is because the Supreme Court, while protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, allowed states to regulate the procedure so long as they didn't place an undue burden on a woman's access to it. Oddly enough, when the high court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overruled Roe v. Wade in 2022 }}}\uc2 , a series of events made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions more vulnerable in some parts of the country.\par \par \uc2 More than a dozen states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moved to ban most abortions }}}\uc2 , prompting voters in Ohio and several other states to respond by passing ballot measures that added \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections to their state constitutions. Those constitutional amendments arguably provide broader legal rights than what the Supreme Court previously endorsed, giving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights plaintiffs new weapons in litigation.\par \par \uc2 The dynamic could come into play in more states after November because \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights amendments will again be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-rights-election-ballot-2024-3c50731d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a hot issue this election season }}}\uc2 , with ballot measures expected in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/florida-activists-abortion-ballot-amendment-afa804c6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/arizona-abortion-poll-election-2024-def7bb14"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona }}}\uc2  and Missouri, all states with restrictions similar to Ohio's.\par \par \uc2 "A lot of states after 2024 will be looking at this," said Jessie Hill, a law professor at \uc2 Case Western Reserve University\uc2 , in Cleveland, who is representing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in the Ohio cases.\par \par \uc2 The Ohio challenges are in their early days, and judges have yet to rule in any of them. If the plaintiffs win these and future lawsuits, legal access in Ohio\u8212\'20\'14where Republicans control both chambers of the Legislature\u8212\'20\'14could look much like it does in Democratic-led states such as California and Illinois.\par \par \uc2 The Ohio amendment, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/election-day-ballots-ohio-abortion-maine-texas-colorado-d9922480"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed in November }}}\uc2  with about 57% of the vote, said every individual "has a right to make and carry out one's own reproductive decisions," including on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And the state "shall not, directly or indirectly, burden, penalize, prohibit, interfere with, or discriminate against" the exercise of those rights.\par \par \uc2 The amendment effectively negated a so-called heartbeat law that would have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after about six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Since 2011, Ohio lawmakers passed some 30 new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, according to a list compiled by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups. Long term, the groups say they hope to challenge every one of them in court.\par \par \uc2 "We're not on the defense anymore," said Kellie Copeland, executive director of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Forward, a state organization that recently rebranded from Pro-Choice Ohio. The state lost half of its clinics during the years of mounting restrictions, she said.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups say their opponents are trying to undermine important protections for women's health and haven't been upfront about their intentions when campaigning for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights amendments.\par \par \uc2 "The amendments were intentionally vague and deceptive," said \uc2 Kristen Waggoner\uc2 , chief executive of \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , a conservative legal group. "It's really gaslighting the American public." \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
