\par \par \uc2 Ohio antiabortion activist Janet Porter, in 2019. PHOTO: Maddie McGarvey for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Janet Porter, a longtime Ohio antiabortion activist who helped pioneer heartbeat laws nationwide, said her side is building plans to fight in the legislature and the courts. The other side is trying "to unravel and undo every pro-life and protective law that we've passed over the last 50 years," she said.\par \par \uc2 Ohio Attorney General David Yost, a Republican, acknowledged in a memo before the November vote that the state amendment would create \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections beyond what Roe had guaranteed. A spokeswoman for his office said the amendment didn't mean that every law that touches on "\b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  or medical care must be stricken."\par \par \uc2 One area where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates are being cautious is the issue of parental consent, which in Ohio is required for minors to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in most circumstances. During the ballot campaign, antiabortion activists raised the specter of parents losing control over their teenagers.\par \par \uc2 "There are a lot of really good reasons to challenge parental consent," said Lauren Blauvelt, executive director of Planned Parenthood Advocates of Ohio, citing hardships on minors whose parents are abusive. But, she added, "it's not our intention to be necessarily too ahead of public opinion."\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, another battle in the November election\u8212\'20\'14for control of the state's Supreme Court\u8212\'20\'14could ultimately help determine the extent of the protections under the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights amendment. The court has a Republican majority, but Democrats would take control of it if they win all three of the current races. Both sides are preparing for a fierce campaign in which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to be a focus.\par \par \uc2 "I certainly think with enough investment and momentum\u8212\'20\'14and we have a lot of momentum\u8212\'20\'14that we can win these important elections," Blauvelt said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240619ek6j0012y\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
