\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Pill Ruling and IVF Battle Highlight Vulnerability for GOP; Fights over  \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights \highlight\uc2  played out this week in the Supreme Court, in the Senate and in churches\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey and Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 1,249 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 June 2024\par 09:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14\b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive-rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates saw some momentum during a dramatic week in which the Supreme Court maintained widespread {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone-f78f3320"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 access to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills }}}\uc2  and Republicans were put on the defensive over whether they support in vitro fertilization.\par \par \uc2 The rapidly unfolding events came as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fights over related issues such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/ivf-vote-in-senate-raises-heat-on-republicans-9502d2a7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 IVF and contraception }}}\uc2  are expected to drive turnout in the 2024 election. President Biden has campaigned aggressively on a pledge to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the 2022 Supreme Court ruling that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated the right to the procedure }}}\uc2 . Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has taken credit for appointing justices who joined that decision but has struggled to articulate a message and has warned fellow Republicans that the issue is perilous for them.\par \par \uc2 The country's largest Protestant denomination also came out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/southern-baptist-convention-vote-against-ban-on-churches-with-women-pastors-9a0d9ec4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 against the use of IVF }}}\uc2  this week, keeping it at the center of a debate playing out from churches to the U.S. Capitol.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the Supreme Court unanimously rejected an effort seeking to restrict {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-arguments-abortion-pill-mifepristone-c31de31a?"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 access to the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill mifepristone }}}\uc2 , ruling that a group of antiabortion doctors who filed suit had no legal standing to challenge \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  regulations for prescribing the drug. The ruling ensures the pills will for now remain widely available but certainly won't end the legal and political fight over the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/abortion-pill-access-case-texas-judge-11651775689?"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most common method for ending a pregnancy }}}\uc2  in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 While Democrats applauded that access to the drug remains in place, they cautioned that the ruling was reached on procedural grounds and that threats to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access continue. Biden campaign manager Julie Chavez Rodriguez said: "This case\u8212\'20\'14brought on by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's allies\u8212\'20\'14was only one tactic in a broader, relentless strategy to strip away access to reproductive freedom everywhere in this country."\par \par \uc2 Trump, on Capitol Hill Thursday, acknowledged that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  subject was a vulnerability, telling GOP lawmakers that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics cost the party in recent elections, and that they can't ignore the topic but need to talk about it carefully, according to two Republicans in the room. Trump also said Republicans should say they support exceptions to banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14for rape, incest and the life of the mother, according to one of the lawmakers. Trump has previously said he supports IVF.\par \par \uc2 Trump's campaign reacted to the Supreme Court ruling Thursday by saying in a statement the matter was "settled," without praising or criticizing the decision. The campaign also said Trump supported leaving decisions about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the states and accused the Biden campaign of lying about the former president's views.\par \par \uc2 The ruling provided another moment for the Biden campaign to focus on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an issue that could help the president over the finish line in a close race. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  joined an organizing call on the topic Thursday night. The campaign is also planning events around the anniversary of the 2022 ruling that overturned Roe v. Wade, which is on June 24.\par \par \uc2 New polling from Gallup shows that 32% of registered voters say they will only vote for candidates who share their views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which includes 23% who support {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/abortion-rights-advocates-deploy-a-new-red-state-playbook-8f13a644"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2  and 8% who oppose. Before 2022, that split was more even.\par \par \uc2 Since March 13, when both Trump and Biden became the presumptive nominees, the incumbent and his allies have spent heavily on broadcast television ads featuring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the issue most frequently mentioned in their ads in the seven states expected to be the most competitive, data from AdImpact shows. Almost a third of spots aired by Biden and his allies in those states mentioned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with spending totaling more than $15 million.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't a topic often addressed by Trump and his allies in broadcast ads. The top issues referred to by them are immigration, inflation and crime.\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans also tried to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/ivf-vote-in-senate-raises-heat-on-republicans-9502d2a7?"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 play defense on IVF access }}}\uc2  Thursday as Democrats forced a vote on a bill enshrining access to the procedure into law, seeking to put Republicans on the record opposing the practice. The vote came a day after the Southern Baptists, the country's largest Protestant denomination, voted to oppose the use of in vitro fertilization as it is commonly practiced.\par \par \uc2 All 49 Republicans in the chamber signed a letter backing IVF, and they argued that Democrats had drafted overly broad legislation designed to score political points and scare voters. Democrats say the IVF package is needed to head off fresh challenges to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How do you think the debates over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills and IVF will affect the results of the November elections? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Polling has shown broad bipartisan support for IVF. The Gallup poll showed that 82% of Americans saw IVF as "morally acceptable." That includes 89% of Democrats, 84% of Independents and 72% of Republicans.\par \par \uc2 IVF has emerged as a newly potent political issue after the \uc2 Alabama Supreme Court\uc2  in February ruled that frozen embryos are children and providers in the state paused services until the state's legislature passed a law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/alabama-shields-ivf-providers-with-new-law-53d54d16"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shielding them from liability.  }}}\par \par \uc2 The fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is also playing out in several states.\par \par \uc2 More than a dozen states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have banned most abortions, }}}\uc2  a number that remains in flux two years after the overturning of Roe. Earlier this year, the Arizona Supreme Court revived a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-ban-821501cb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Civil War-era ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  before lawmakers repealed the law. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/six-week-abortion-ban-florida-c5f00f7e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A six-week ban }}}\uc2  took effect in Florida this past month.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups have gone on offense in even some of the country's more conservative states after winning a string of referendum victories in places as politically diverse as Kansas and Ohio. Measures to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights could be on the ballot in half a dozen or more states this November, including political battlegrounds such as Arizona, Montana and Florida.\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, advocates are using a measure that passed in November to try to challenge longstanding state laws, including waiting periods and rules requiring doctors to look for fetal cardiac activity before performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -pill debate is also likely to continue. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  challenge was the most prominent move by antiabortion groups on a national scale since Roe was overturned, but it rested on some novel legal arguments. Antiabortion groups were adamant Thursday that they will continue to find legal and political avenues to restrict access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills.\par \par \uc2 "This is only the beginning frankly," said Students for Life Action spokeswoman Kristi Hamrick.\par \par \uc2 Another strategy by antiabortion groups involves trying to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/a-19th-century-law-could-help-influence-the-abortion-pills-future-639dddb6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revive the Comstock Act }}}\uc2 , a 19th-century federal law that banned mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs over state lines. Some advocates have been urging a potential future Trump administration to enforce the law, which could ignite a new national fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills.\par \par \uc2 Sen. Tina Smith (D., Minn.) said she plans next week to introduce a bill to repeal the Comstock Act. Republican legislators in Congress have introduced bills to ban Medicare funds from going to doctors who prescribe the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill via telehealth, prohibit the \uc2 FDA\uc2  from approving any new drugs to terminate pregnancies and strip funding from colleges that host health services that provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs.\par \par \uc2 John McCormick and Liz Essley Whyte contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240614ek6e001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
