\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Democrats Plan $100 Million Push on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights to Win House; House Majority PAC's new fund will be spent in swing districts for advertising and voter mobilization\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalie Andrews \par \uc2 908 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 May 2024\par 09:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The super PAC supporting Democrats' effort to win back the House majority is launching a $100 million fund focused on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the latest sign that the party is leaning heavily on the issue this fall to help counter concerns about the economy and immigration policy.\par \par \uc2 In a memo to donors, the House Majority PAC outlined the Reproductive Freedom Accountability Fund, which it said will be spent in swing districts across the country for advertising and voter mobilization. The fund will also focus on voter outreach in House districts where there aren't competitive presidential or Senate races, such as in New York, California, Oregon, Washington and Virginia.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/republicans-narrow-control-of-house-sets-up-barnburner-in-2024-14d242d9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 battle for the House majority }}}\uc2  is expected to be a dogfight, with the current balance of the House at 217 Republicans and 213 Democrats, with five vacancies. The nonpartisan Cook Political Report rates 11 seats held by each party, or 22 total, as tossups, meaning they could go for either party. Several dozen more are also seen as competitive, though leaning toward one party or the other.\par \par \uc2 With the focus on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, Democrats are seeking to overcome President Biden's weak poll numbers and Republicans' advantages in surveys on combating inflation and better controlling the border. Many Republicans back limits on abortions, while former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the presumptive Republican nominee for president, has said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws should be left up to the states.\par \par \uc2 House Majority PAC President Mike Smith said the focus on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has mobilized voters "to focus on reproductive freedoms as one of the defining campaign messages of the 2024 cycle."\par \par \uc2 The memo, viewed by The Wall Street Journal, was sent this month, signaling to donors and supporters the PAC's plans for the fall. The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related fund will be comprised of new money and cash already raised.\par \par \uc2 Super PACs can take in unlimited donations from individuals and corporations. Major donors so far this cycle for the House Majority PAC include \uc2 Reed Hastings\uc2 , the co-founder and executive chairman of \uc2 Netflix\uc2 , and entrepreneur \uc2 Fred Eychaner\uc2 , according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opensecrets.org/political-action-committees-pacs/house-majority-pac/C00495028/donors/2024?page_length=25"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 OpenSecrets }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democrats see \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate as helping their side: Two years ago, the party campaigned on defending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, winning the Senate majority and losing the House, but avoiding a feared "red wave" wipeout.\par \par \uc2 A recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-biden-poll-swing-states-ad594acb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal poll }}}\uc2  of seven battleground states found that 39% of suburban women cite \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a make-or-break issue {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/nikki-haley-primary-voters-donald-trump-support-election-82666934"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for their vote }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14making it by far the most motivating issue for the group. Of those women, nearly three-quarters of them say the procedure should be legal all or most of the time.\par \par \uc2 Suburban women named \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a leading reason to back President Biden, and 57% of the same group said Trump's policies on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  were too restrictive.\par \par \uc2 "Democrats can't ignore voters' concerns about the economy and safety and immigration, but I don't think there's been a race in the last three years where Democrats regretted highlighting the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue," said Nathan Gonzales, editor of Inside Elections, which provides nonpartisan analysis of campaigns.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have countered that Democrats don't embody the mainstream stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Democrats don't generally put a limit on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the number of weeks of pregnancy, saying any decision should be between a woman and her doctor. Republicans have encouraged their candidates to talk more about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  this cycle, arguing that some voters support limits and that not all in their party back a total ban.\par \par \uc2 "With voters rejecting Democrats on just about every issue under the sun, this is their sole strategy," said Dan Conston, the president of the Congressional Leadership Fund, which boosts House Republicans. He said the impact of the issue varies by state. "In blue states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal, Republican candidates can clearly and empathetically communicate this is a state issue and settled law," he said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to the top of many voters' concerns after the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned the Roe vs. Wade decision }}}\uc2 , which enshrined access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in 2022. While a major win for social conservatives, the ruling also threw the matter back to Congress and the states, motivating voters who favor \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and now saw it being curtailed in many states.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How will the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights shape the election? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court has since heard arguments about limiting access to medications that can lead to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . in February, the conservative \uc2 Alabama Supreme Court\uc2  ruled that embryos created through in vitro fertilization should be considered children, temporarily halting infertility treatments in the state until {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/ivf-has-largely-restarted-in-alabama-patients-are-still-worried-93c48e75"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the legislature passed protections }}}\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups are also working to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on the ballot through referendums and initiatives. Democrats see these as boosting turnout in their direction in swing states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/arizona-abortion-poll-election-2024-def7bb14"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 such as Arizona }}}\uc2  and Nevada.\par \par \uc2 Overall, House Majority PAC has reserved over $186 million in initial television and digital reservations for the 2024 election cycle across 58 markets, the largest in the history of the group.\par \par \uc2 Comparatively, the Congressional Leadership Fund has reserved $141 million for television, streaming, and digital platforms in 37 media markets. It is also more than it has spent in previous election cycles.\par \par \uc2 Write to Natalie Andrews at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:natalie.andrews@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 natalie.andrews@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240529ek5t001up\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
