\par\par \uc2 Business\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Melinda French Gates\uc2  to Donate $1 Billion to Groups Supporting Women,  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights; Philanthropist discloses her first major donations since saying she would resign from the \uc2 Gates Foundation\uc2  to Donate $1 Billion to Groups Supporting Women,  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights; Philanthropist discloses her first major donations since saying she would resign from the\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alyssa Lukpat \par \uc2 692 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 May 2024\par 19:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Melinda French Gates\uc2  said she will be donating $1 billion over the next two years to organizations and individuals supporting women, families and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Her organization \uc2 Pivotal Ventures\uc2  announced the donations Tuesday, about two weeks after she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/business/melinda-french-gates-is-resigning-from-the-gates-foundation-76b0fcd7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said she was resigning  }}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation\uc2  . She said she was leaving the foundation she started with her ex-husband, \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  co-founder \uc2 Bill Gates\uc2  , on June 7 to do philanthropy elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 As part of an agreement with Gates, she was set to receive $12.5 billion to commit to her work for women and girls.\par \par \uc2 "For too long, a lack of money has forced organizations fighting for women's rights into a defensive posture while the enemies of progress play offense. I want to help even the match," she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/05/28/opinion/melinda-french-gates-reproductive-rights.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote  }}}\uc2  Tuesday in the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Pivotal Ventures\uc2  said French Gates would give grants to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pivotalventures.org/articles/melinda-french-gates-announces-1billlion-commitment-to-advance-women-globally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than a dozen groups  }}}\uc2 . They include the Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which advocates for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights; the \uc2 Institute for Women's Policy Research\uc2  , a think tank focused on women; and Time's Up Legal Defense Fund, which supports people who have faced workplace harassment.\par \par \uc2 French Gates said she felt compelled to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the U.S. after the Supreme Court in 2022 eliminated the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She added that women's rights are often pushed aside.\par \par \uc2 "In nearly 20 years as an advocate for women and girls, I have learned that there will always be people who say it's not the right time to talk about gender equality," she wrote in Tuesday's opinion piece. "The second the global agenda gets crowded, women and girls fall off."\par \par \uc2 One of the most influential philanthropists in the world, French Gates has often focused her advocacy efforts on gender equality. She and Gates started their foundation in 2000 and ran it as equal partners. When their divorce finalized in 2021, it raised questions about the future of the foundation. French Gates, 59, had decided last summer to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/melinda-french-gates-decides-to-stay-with-gates-foundation-766c4940?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stay with the foundation  }}}\uc2  before she announced her resignation taking effect next month.\par \par \uc2 French Gates published her own Giving Pledge in 2021, saying she would donate the bulk of her fortune to different causes instead of just the \uc2 Gates Foundation\uc2  . She has a net worth of $13.3 billion, according to the Bloomberg Billionaires Index.\par \par \uc2 Pivotal Ventures\uc2 , the organization she founded in 2015, said a dozen people would each receive a $20 million fund to give to charities focused on women's health and well-being. The individuals include filmmaker Ava DuVernay, Olympian Allyson Felix and former New Zealand Prime Minister \uc2 Jacinda Ardern\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 French Gates in her opinion piece called these grant-making funds a novel tactic that she hoped would unlock new funding opportunities.\par \par \uc2 "As a young woman, I could never have imagined that one day I would be part of an effort like this. Because I have been given this extraordinary opportunity, I am determined to do everything I can to seize it and to set an agenda that helps other women and girls set theirs, too," she wrote.\par \par \uc2 The organization said that of the $1 billion donation, French Gates was setting aside $250 million to be distributed through an open call to organizations working on behalf of women.\par \par \uc2 Pivotal Ventures\uc2  said other grant recipients include the Collaborative for Gender + Reproductive Equity, which works on gender, racial and reproductive issues; the \uc2 Institute for Women's Policy Research\uc2  , a think tank focused on women; and MomsRising Education Fund, which advocates economic security for families.\par \par \uc2 Another recipient is the 19th, a news organization focused on women and LGBT people.\par \par \uc2 "Sometimes dreams do come true," the 19th said, while adding: "we are beyond grateful for French Gates' confidence in our team and our mission."\par \par \uc2 Write to Alyssa Lukpat at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:alyssa.lukpat@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alyssa.lukpat@wsj.com  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240528ek5s002s1\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbr